(404, 'learn-how-to-combat-aging', 'Learn How To Combat Aging – Anti-Aging Facial Benefits', 'As we age, it’s only natural that we want to look our best. And while there are a number of ways to combat the signs of aging, one of the most effective is getting an anti-aging facial.', '<p>As we age, it’s only natural that we want to look our best. And while there are a number of ways to combat the signs of aging, one of the most effective is getting an anti-aging facial. In this blog post, we’re going to give you a crash course in everything you need to know about anti-aging facials. We’ll cover the benefits, the different types of facials available, and how to choose the right one for you. We’ll even provide some tips on how to get the most out of your facial. By the end of this post, you should have a good understanding of anti-aging facials and how they can help you look your best.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Introduction To Anti Aging Facials</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re looking to fight the signs of aging, then you need to consider getting an anti-aging facial. There are a variety of different types of facials that can help to do just that, so it&#39;s important to know what they are. In this section, we&#39;ll go over the three main types of facials and their respective benefits. We&#39;ll also recommend when you should get them and how often. So read on to learn more about these amazing treatments!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When it comes to fighting the signs of aging, facials are a great option. They can help to reduce wrinkles, age spots, and other signs of skin aging. There are three main types of facials: exfoliation facials, anti-aging facials, and regeneration facials. Let&#39;s take a closer look at each one.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Exfoliation facials are the simplest type of facial and they just involve scrubbing your skin clean. This is great for removing dead skin cells and making your skin look younger overall. They&#39;re typically recommended for every two months as part of your regular skincare routine, but you can go longer if you&#39;d like.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anti-aging facials are more comprehensive than exfoliation facials and they aim to target several different areas of aging skin. These treatments might include serums or lotions that help to reduce the appearance of wrinkles or age spots, as well as mechanical peels that remove layers of dead skin cells from the face. You should schedule an anti-aging facial every six to eight weeks depending on your specific needs and goals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Regeneration facials are designed specifically for people who want to improve their appearance overall rather than just deal with specific issues like wrinkles or age spots. These treatments work by stimulating new cell growth in the dermis layer of the skin which helps to rebuild collagen and elastin tissue. You should schedule a regeneration facial every twelve weeks in order to see the best results!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>The Benefits Of Anti-Aging Facials</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are many benefits to having an anti-aging facial. One of the most significant is that it can reduce the appearance of wrinkles. Wrinkles are caused by the accumulation of skin cells and inflammation, both of which can be addressed with a facial. By reducing the appearance of wrinkles, an anti-aging facial can give you a more youthful appearance.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Another benefit to having an anti-aging facial is that it stimulates collagen production. Collagen is a key protein in your skin that helps to keep it elastic and healthy. By stimulating collagen production, an anti-aging facial can improve skin texture and tone as well as hydrate and nourish your skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Finally, an anti-aging facial also improves skin tone and pigmentation. By addressing any underlying causes of these issues, an anti-aging facial can help to restore your skin’s natural beauty.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are many different types of anti-aging facials, each with their own set of benefits. A classic anti-aging facial may include skin cleansing, exfoliation, and toning. This type of facial can help to reduce the appearance of wrinkles and improve skin texture and tone. In addition, a classic anti-aging facial can also improve pigmentation and lighten skin color.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A more targeted approach to an anti-aging facial is called a resurfacing treatment. This type of facial includes deeper cleansing as well as laser or IPL treatments that target unwanted areas such as age spots or acne scars. With a resurfacing treatment, you can not only reduce the appearance of wrinkles but also address any underlying causes of skin issues such as age spots or uneven pigmentations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Finally, there is a category of facials known as rejuvenation facials which address all aspects of your skin’s health in one go. This type of facial includes deep cleaning; exfoliation; moisturizing; brightening; sunscreen application; nourishing ingredients applied topically; and/or radiance boosting technologies like LED light therapy or microdermabrasion. By addressing all these areas at once, a rejuvenation facial offers unbeatable overall results for your skin care regimen.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>The Types Of Anti Aging Facials Available</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a variety of different types of anti-aging facials available, each with its own unique benefits. To find the right type for you, it is important to understand the different types and how they work.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The first type of facial is called a resurfacing treatment. This type of facial removes excess skin and surface cells, which helps to improve the appearance of wrinkles and age spots. It also improves the texture and density of your skin, which can help to reduce the appearance of cellulite.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The next type of facial is called a hydrating treatment. This type of facial helps to restore hydration levels in your skin, which can improve its appearance and feel. In addition, it can help to reduce inflammation and redness in the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The final type of facial is called an elasticity treatment. This type of facial targets sagging areas in your skin by restoring collagen and elastin production. As a result, these areas will become more firm and elasticized – promoting better overall skin health.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How To Choose The Right Anti Aging Facial For You</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>As we age, our skin becomes less elastic, which can cause wrinkles and other signs of aging. To help address this issue, it is important to choose the right anti-aging facial for you. At Skinfinity, we offer a variety of facials that can help you achieve your desired results. Our team of expert estheticians will work with you to determine which facial is best suited for your individual needs. Contact us today to learn more about our anti-aging treatments and to <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/contact-us/\">schedule a consultation!</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>When choosing an anti-aging facial, it is important to consider your skin type and the specific concerns you have about aging. Are you concerned about fine lines and wrinkles? Do you want to reduce the appearance of age spots? Our team can help you find the right facial treatment for your needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Another factor to consider when choosing an anti-aging facial is your budget. We offer a variety of facials that range in price from $60 to $200. Whether you are looking for a basic face treatment or something more elaborate, our team will work with you to find the best option for your wallet and skin care goals. Contact us today to learn more!</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How Often Should You Get An Anti Aging Facial?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>There is no one-size-fits-all answer to this question, as the frequency of anti-aging facials depends on a number of factors, including the severity of signs of aging. In some cases, people may only need facials once a month, while others may require them more often. The key is to work with your facialist to find an optimal frequency that will suit your needs and maximize results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anti-aging facials can help improve the appearance of fine lines and wrinkles, as well as age spots. They can also promote collagen production and improve skin elasticity. Additionally, they can help reduce the appearance of pores and unnoticeable blemishes. If you are looking for improved skin texture and tone, then an anti-aging facial should be at the top of your list!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a number of factors to consider when determining the frequency of your anti-aging facials. First, you should discuss your skin type with your facialist. Anti-aging facials are not universally effective for all skin types, so it is important to find one that will work best for you. Secondly, age and sun exposure can affect the rate at which skin ages and becomes more wrinkles and pores. If you have noticed a significant increase in wrinkles or fine lines over the past few years, then it may be time for an anti-aging facial. However, if you do not experience these signs of aging regularly, then weekly facials may be adequate.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As with any skincare regimen, it is important to heed the advice of your facialist and monitor results closely over time. Facialists often recommend completing an annual anti-aging checkup to ensure optimal results continue long term!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Tips For Getting The Most Out Of Your Anti-Aging Facial</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a number of benefits to getting an anti-aging facial. These benefits can include reducing the appearance of wrinkles, age spots, and other signs of aging. Additionally, an anti-aging facial can improve your skin’s texture and tone.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To get the most out of your facial, it is important to use quality products. This means selecting products that have been specifically designed for face care. Additionally, it is important to keep your skin well hydrated before and after your facial appointment. Finally, be sure to schedule regular facials to maintain optimal skin health over time!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Common Mistakes To Avoid When Getting An Anti Aging Facial</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>When it comes to getting an anti-aging facial, there are a few common mistakes that people make. One of the most common is not choosing the right facial for your skin type. This can result in ineffective and uncomfortable treatments. Additionally, people may also choose an <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\"><strong>anti-aging treatment </strong></a>that is too strong or too harsh for their skin. By following these tips, you can avoid making common <strong>anti-aging facial </strong>mistakes and achieve great results!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It&#39;s important to remember that your skin type is unique and will respond differently to different types of facials. For this reason, it&#39;s important to consult with a professional before beginning any <strong>treatment for anti-aging</strong> plan. They will be able to recommend the best facial for your skin type and help you customize the treatment plan accordingly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Finally, don&#39;t forget to take care of yourself after your facial! Skincare products should be applied regularly after an anti-aging facial so that you maintain optimal results over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>To Conclude</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>While we can&#39;t completely stop the aging process, there are a number of things we can do to help combat its effects. One of the most effective is getting regular anti-aging facials. These treatments can help reduce wrinkles, improve skin texture and tone, and promote collagen production. If you&#39;re looking to fight the signs of aging,<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/contact-us/\"> contact us today to schedule a consultation!</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/a56252f70194848390911a9a00894340.jpg', 'Combat Aging', 'Learn How To Combat Aging – Anti-Aging Facial Benefits', 'Skinfinity: Learn How To Combat Aging - Anti-Aging Facial Benefits', 'Combat Aging,  Anti-Aging Facial Benefits', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/learn-how-to-combat-aging/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Combat Aging\",\"Anti-Aging Facial Benefits\"]', 0, 1, '2022-11-22 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(405, 'how-to-get-radiant-beauty', 'How to get Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding', 'Getting Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding is a dream for most women. But, not everyone knows how to achieve their dream. Getting Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding is a dream for most women.', '<p>Getting Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding is a dream for most women. But, not everyone knows how to achieve their dream. Getting Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding is a dream for most women. But, not everyone knows how to achieve their dream. In order to get Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding, you must follow some important tips. Here, we will tell you about how to get Radiant Beauty with a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/organic-hydrafacial/\"><strong>Hydra-facial</strong></a> Before your wedding.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What are Hydra facial treatments, and how do they differ from other facial treatments?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Hydra facial treatments</strong> are different from other facial treatments because they are multi-step, acid-based treatments. The multi-step treatment combines cleansing, exfoliation, extraction, hydration, and antioxidant protection.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydrafacial treatments remove the dead skin cells from the surface of the face. This is accomplished using gentle exfoliation and gentle extraction of the impurities from underneath the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydrafacial treatments rehydrate the skin with solutions and moisturizers. Hydrafacial treatments are also effective at diminishing the signs of aging and minimizing the appearance of fine lines, wrinkles, dark spots, and hyperpigmentation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In addition to skin appearance, Hydrafacial treatments are also effective at treating congested skin (e.g., rosacea), acne, and enlarged pores.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Does Hydra facial work, and what are its advantages?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydrafacial is a revolutionary skin treatment which exfoliates and extracts impurities while simultaneously bathing the new skin with cleansing, hydrating and moisturizing serums. This treatment is soothing, refreshing and immediately effective.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>BENEFITS OF hydra facial :</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>1. It exfoliates dead skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. It cleanses impurities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. It extracts blackheads and whiteheads.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. It replenishes the skin with antioxidants and peptides.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5. It hydrates the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2> </h2>\r\n\r\n<h3>What is involved in a Hydra facial treatment and what can you expect during this process?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The Hydra facial uses a type of facial massage that helps to exfoliate the skin, remove toxins, and improve circulation. As a result, your complexion will look healthier and more youthful.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Hydra facial begins with a cleanse to remove dirt and oil from the skin. The next step involves a massage of the face with steam and a cleansing solution that causes dead skin cells to slough off. This exfoliation process is followed by an infusion of antioxidants and nutrients into the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The final step involves a hydrating mist that hydrates the skin and seals in the nutrients, leaving you with a healthy glow. Because of the exfoliation, the Hydra facial may be slightly uncomfortable, but it is not painful. Most patients find the results to be worth it.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How much does it cost to get a Hydra facial at skinfinity skin clinic?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydra facial is a skin treatment that uses only water and serums to hydrate and refresh your skin. It involves the use of serums for skin treatment that contain ingredients like antioxidants, peptides, and hyaluronic acid.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>These serums are applied to the skin using a special machine. The machine draws water through the machine&#39;s nozzles that apply a combination of the serums directly onto the skin. The serums contain antioxidants and other ingredients that can help the skin glow.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There is no downtime associated with Hydra facials and you can resume your normal daily activities immediately after completing the treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydra facial prices usually depend on the price range of the clinic. Skinfinity Skin Clinic offers Hydra facials in a basic package that is priced at 6,000. You can also choose a deluxe package that includes a chemical peel treatment for 12,000. Other packages are available at the clinic as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Conclusion</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>To get Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding, you must focus on the Hydra-facial procedure. Hydra-facial is a procedure that brightens your skin, reduces fine lines, and removes blackheads. To get Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding, you must give your skin enough time to heal. You need to use skincare products that are gentle on your skin. If you follow these tips, then you can get Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding.</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/79182842eb0b6f03e22190fccd9931e9.jpg', 'Get Radiant Beauty', 'How to get Radiant Beauty with a Hydra-facial Before your wedding', 'Looking for a way to achieve radiant beauty before your wedding? Skinfinity can help! Our Hydra-facials are known for their ability to help improve the appearance of skin tone and texture, giving you a more radiant look before your big day.', 'Get Radiant Beauty,  Hydra-facial Before wedding', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/how-to-get-radiant-beauty/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Get Radiant Beauty\",\"Hydra-facial Before wedding\"]', 0, 1, '2022-11-14 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(406, 'enhance-your-skincare-routine-for-less-dark-circles', 'Enhance Your Skincare Routine For Less Dark Circles', 'If you\'re concerned about your dark circles, there are a few products that can help. The first step is to identify the right products for your skin type.', '<p>For many of us, <strong>dark circles under the eyes</strong> are just something we have to deal with on a daily basis. But what if we told you that there are some simple steps you can take to <strong>reduce dark circles</strong> and <strong>under-eye puffiness</strong>? In this blog post, we’re going to share with you some of the best tips and tricks for <strong>dark circle removal</strong>. From the right <strong>under-eye creams</strong> and <strong>skincare products</strong> to <strong>natural home remedies for dark circles</strong>, we’ve got you covered. If you’re looking for professional solutions, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dark-circle-treatment/\"><strong>dark circles treatment in Noida</strong> </a>offers advanced options like laser therapy, chemical peels, and dermal fillers. Understanding the underlying causes is the first step towards finding an appropriate solution, and consulting with a skilled <strong>skin doctor in Noida</strong> or <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong></a> can provide tailored treatments such as laser therapy, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\">chemical peels</a>, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler/\">dermal fillers,</a> or <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hairfall-treatment-noida/\">PRP </a>to effectively reduce <strong>under-eye dark circles</strong> and restore a fresh, youthful look.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>The Right Products For Reducing Dark Circles</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re concerned about your dark circles, a few products can help. The first step is to identify the right products for your skin type. There are different types of skincare products that can work well for different people, so it&#39;s important to find one that will reduce the darkness under your eyes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Next, be consistent with your skincare routine. If you don&#39;t use the same skincare products and methods every day, you won&#39;t see results. And finally, consider other factors that may be causing your dark circles - such as allergies or lack of sleep. If you notice that these things are affecting your skin in a negative way, talk to a dermatologist about what steps might be necessary to correct the issue.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>A Good Night&#39;s Sleep: The Best Treatment For Dark Circles?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Everyone knows that a good night&#39;s sleep is essential for overall health and well-being. But what about dark circles? Are they really as bad as they seem? In fact, according to some experts, dark circles are actually caused by excessive sunlight exposure or caffeine and alcohol consumption. So if you&#39;re looking for a cure, the best solution might be to get some sleep!</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sleep is obviously crucial for healthy skin, but sometimes people find it difficult to get enough shut-eye. This is especially true for people who are busy and stressed - their bedtimes start to slip away from them! To make things even harder, caffeine and alcohol can interfere with our natural sleep cycle. As a result, these substances can cause dark circles under your eyes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fortunately, there are plenty of home remedies for dark circles that you can try at home. For example, you could try using cold compresses or cucumber slices as a remedy. Skinfinity offers treatments specifically designed to address this issue in Noida and Gurgaon - so don&#39;t hesitate to give us a call if you&#39;re looking for help!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Caffeine Fixes Everything Or Does It?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Are you looking to reduce the appearance of dark circles? Do you have sensitive skin? If so, applying caffeine topically is an effective way to do so. Caffeine can help constrict blood vessels and stimulate circulation, both of which improve the look of dark circles. Additionally, caffeine derived from green tea or other sources may be more suited for those with sensitive skin. So if you&#39;re looking for a solution to reduce the appearance of your under-eye circles, give topical caffeine a try!</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are many different ways to consume caffeine, and they all have their own benefits and drawbacks. Some people prefer to drink coffee, while others prefer to use tea or energy drinks. Coffee is a great way to start your day because it provides you with energy while also improving your cognitive function. Tea can also help improve your mood, but it can also cause drowsiness if you don&#39;t have enough caffeine in it. Energy drinks provide you with immediate energy, but they can be expensive and may contain harmful chemicals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>In general, caffeine is safe for most people when consumed in moderation. However, pregnant women should avoid coffee because of its high levels of caffeine. Additionally, children should not consume more than 100mg of caffeine per day because too much caffeine can lead to negative side effects such as headaches and irritability.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Hiding Dark Circles With Makeup</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hiding dark circles with makeup can be a challenge, but there are a few tricks that can help. First, use a primer to help the concealer stay in place. Next, apply the concealer in an upside-down triangle shape. Finally, set the concealer with powder and add brightness with the highlighter.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>To avoid looking too made up, go for natural makeup looks that can be enhanced with a few simple tricks. Choose a light foundation to conceal any dark circles, and add contour and false eyelashes to create depth and definition. For a more subtle look, try using a pink blush or lip balm as your base color. And finally, finish the look with natural eye shadow that doesn’t emphasize the circles.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>When To See A Doctor About Your Dark Circles</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>When it comes to dark circles, there is no one-size-fits-all answer. That&#39;s why it&#39;s important to speak with a doctor about your specific situation. Here are some tips on when you should <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/contact-us/\">see a doctor </a>about your dark circles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have very severe dark circles, then you should definitely see a doctor. This is because the condition may be caused by an underlying medical condition, and treatment may be required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you experience moderate to severe dark circles fairly often, then you should also see a doctor. This is because the condition could be indicative of an underlying health problem. For example, if you are experiencing dry skin or skin that is sensitive to UV rays, then seeing a dermatologist may be beneficial in finding out what the cause of your dark circles is and how best to treat it.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Finally, if you experience light or occasional dark circles, then there isn&#39;t necessarily anything wrong with them and they don&#39;t need to be treated right away. However, if they bother you or cause other problems (such as sleeplessness), then speaking with a doctor can help determine whether further action needs to be taken.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Natural Home Remedies For Reducing Dark Circles</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a number of reasons why people develop dark circles under their eyes, including genetics, allergies, and chronic stress. While there is no one-size-fits-all solution to reducing the appearance of them, there are a variety of natural home remedies that can help lessen the appearance of them. Some simple changes to your skincare routine, such as using eye cream and sleeping with an extra pillow, can also help reduce the appearance of dark circles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Some of the most popular natural remedies for reducing the appearance of dark circles include:</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>-Using an eye cream that is specifically designed to reduce the appearance of under-eye circles. The best eye creams contain ingredients such as caffeine, thickening agents, and antioxidants that work together to nourish and hydrate the skin around your eyes. Some examples of effective Eye Creams are La Roche-Posay Toleriane Youth Activating Eye Cream and Kiehl&#39;s Ten Kate Visible Dark Circle Eraser.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>-Eating foods that are high in antioxidants can also help reduce the appearance of dark circles. Foods that are rich in antioxidants include fruits and vegetables, nuts, legumes, and whole grains. Eating these foods on a regular basis can help protect your skin from becoming age or acne prone.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Foods That Help Reduce The Appearance Of Dark Circles</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a variety of foods that can help reduce the appearance of dark circles. Cucumber slices are a popular remedy, as they contain cucurbitacin, which is a compound that has anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties. Potato starch is another common ingredient, as it helps to lighten the skin. Green tea also has anti-inflammatory properties, which can help to soothe and calm the skin. Cold milk contains lactic acid, which helps to brighten the skin and constrict blood vessels, thereby reducing the appearance of dark circles. Rose water also has anti-inflammatory properties and can be used as a natural toner for the skin. Finally, caffeine in coffee can help to constrict blood vessels and reduce puffiness around the eyes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Some people also prefer to use home remedies such as astringent tonics or herbal infusions. These remedies help to cleanse and detoxify the skin, which can help to reduce the appearance of dark circles. Examples of astringent tonics include witch hazel and aloe vera juice, while an example of an herbal infusion for dark circles is chamomile tea. Both of these remedies are effective in reducing inflammation and restoring balance to the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Supplements That May Help Lessen The Appearance Of Dark Circles</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re looking for a way to diminish the appearance of dark circles, you may want to check out some of the supplements that Skinfinity dermatologists have recommended. Here are four supplements that have been shown to help lessen the appearance of dark circles:</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Ashwagandha This supplement is known to improve mental health, and it has also been shown to reduce inflammation and fatigue. It can be taken as a standalone supplement or in combination with other supplements, such as caffeine or green tea extract.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Horny Goat Weed This herb is also known for its anti-inflammatory properties. It has been shown to help improve skin elasticity and brightness, which can help diminish the appearance of dark circles. Horny Goat Weed is best taken fresh or dried, in capsules or tinctures form.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Cucumber water is a natural alternative to traditional eye drops. It helps relax the eyes and provide hydration while reducing puffiness and inflammation around the eyes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. Retinol A topical prescription medication used for treating wrinkles and other signs of aging, retinol can be applied topically over dark circles under your eyes in order to lighten them up. <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">Skinfinity dermatologists</a> recommend 0\% retinol products because they are less likely to cause irritation or sensitivity than higher-concentration products.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Final Thoughts</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a number of different things that can cause dark circles, but there are also a number of different ways to reduce their appearance. From the right skincare products to natural home remedies, there are plenty of options available. So if you’re looking for ways to reduce the appearance of dark circles, give some of these tips and tricks a try!</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/4825c4d2e633a0cf18cd91b492da1cc2.jpg', 'Dark Circles', 'Enhance Your Skincare Routine For Less Dark Circles', 'Looking to take your skincare routine to the next level without spending a fortune? Look no further than Skinfinity! Our affordable and effective products will help you get rid of dark circles and look younger, faster!', 'Dark Circle, Skincare Routine', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/enhance-your-skincare-routine-for-less-dark-circles/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Dark Circles\",\"Skincare Routine\"]', 0, 1, '2022-11-05 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(407, 'semi-permanent', 'Semi-permanent makeup techniques to look your best this festive season', 'As the festive season progresses, everyone wants to look their best at every celebration. ', '<p><strong>As the festive season progresses, everyone wants to look their best at every celebration. So it’s high time to start preparing yourself for the upcoming holiday season. We&#39;ve gathered some fantastic suggestions for you in this article.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Semi-permanent makeup has gained a lot of popularity in recent times. It is probably the best solution for someone who is constantly occupied and worried about reapplying makeup. It is a quick, non-invasive procedure that involves application of  semi-permanent pigment to the desired area.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>A temperamental definition to yourbrows, lips, and eyesgives  face the required significance. Other indications of semi permanent makeup are burns, camouflage, vitiligo, and severe pigmentation problems. We do the following procedures at our clinic:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Microblading eyebrows</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>This procedure is ideal for you if you want to cut down your everyday hassle of drawing in your brows, matching them and filling them in. </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>It is a technique where we create hair-like strokes as accurately as feasible, thus offering a more natural looking and defined brows . Cleansing the brows to get rid of dust is followed by local anesthesia application to lessen discomfort during the procedure. This technique involves use of a hand held microblade tool with microneedles that deposit the pigment in superficial layers of skin .</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Lip blush/ Semi-permanent lipstick</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Lip blushing or semi-permanent lipstick is a technique that is performed using a highly advanced PMU machine that delivers pigments to your lips. Although it seems frightening, it is perfectly safe and quite advantageous.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Why lip pigmentation?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Redefine your lips</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Customized color that can lay upto 3 years</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Enhances your natural shape to create fuller looking lips</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Corrects the unwanted discolouration and uneven color</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Eyeliner tattoo</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ink for body tattoos is considerably different from the pigment used to make eyeliner. This procedure involves your eye, thus a qualified technician performs it. You won&#39;t need to apply eyeliner every day after the procedure because it is waterproof and smudge-proof.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>BB&#39;s brightness</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>According to your skin type, deep cleansing and exfoliation will be done. Combining a moisturizing mask, toner, and boost serum  with the BB glow pigment.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>One of BB glow&#39;s advantages is:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Skin hydration</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Provides you with a makeup-free look durable for a month</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Blackheads and pores are less visible.</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Creases and fine lines are less visible.</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>At Skinfinity, dermatologists perform the permanent makeup procedures here as they can make the best judgment about the color of the pigment, depth and other minute details to give the best desired results. Also, high-end PMU machine like GOOCHIE with good quality pigments are used at our clinic.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>And that’s how you can enjoy semi-permanent makeup at Skinfinity with a wide range of such procedures available.You can get rid of all your makeup woes and enjoy the festivity as it brings joy and prosperity to your life. And for the makeup, let the expert dermatologists and trained staff provide you a boost to your already glowing beautiful skin. </strong></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/ecee3d8a65f45e0863a521c35363b2ac.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Semi-permanent makeup ', 'As the festive season progresses, everyone wants to look their best at every celebration.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-10-25 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(408, 'pre-bridal-treatment', 'Pre-bridal treatments for the ravishing bridal glow', 'Every woman desires to look perfectly gorgeous on the most cherished day of their life. ', '<p>Every woman desires to look perfectly gorgeous on the most cherished day of their life. However, most of the brides- to be get so occupied in the wedding shopping and preparations that they forget the most important part that is to prime and prepare their hair and skin. If you&#39;re seeking for the fundamental treatments that will help you look perfect on your wedding day, then Skinfinity is the right place for you. Here are few Skinfinity’s recommended pre- bridal treatments that will make you look stunning on your wedding day.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-removal-in-gurgaon/\">Laser hair removal treatment</a></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A smooth, hair free skin is very important for building the bride’s confidence. At our clinic, we have the best top quality lasers like Primelase, Alma Soprano Platinum for hair reduction that ensures efficient results. Alma Soprano Platinum is a US FDA approved, triple wavelength laser which offers benefits like quick, painless procedures and can be used on all skin types, even tanned skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Face Treatments for Bride-To-Be</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1) HYDRAFACIAL-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It is recommended <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/organic-hydrafacial/\">Hydrafacial treatment</a>  for those brides who already have a good skin and are just looking for glow. It combines exfoliation, hydration, extraction, cleansing, and antioxidant protection. The benefits of hydrafacial are:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Rejuvenation</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Brightening</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hydration</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Exfoliation</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Brightening</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Extraction of black heads and white heads</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>2) PHOTOFACIAL-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This facial includes carbon peel/laser toning. It is an efficient way to treat <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/melasma-treatment/\">pigmentation</a> and uneven skin tone. The best results are observed in 7-10 days after the procedure. It is a painless procedure with minimal downtime.The benefits of this treatment area-</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Improves skin texture</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces fine lines and wrinkles</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Tightens dilated pores</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces acne, post- acne marks and scars</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Stimulates collagen production</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Downtime minimal to zero</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>3) MDA PEEL MASK-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>In this treatment, microdermabrasion is performed which removes the topmost layer of the skin, unclog the skin pores; following which chemical solution according to the skin type is applied, thus boosting  your skin’s appearance. We usually recommend this treatment to the bride-to be with acne, pigmentation , tanning and uneven skin tone.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>4) MESOBOTOX-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>In this treatment, a fine needle is used to distribute diluted botulinum toxin with a high amount of skin hydrating agents like vitamins and minerals through a wide face area into the dermis of the skin, which gives immediate results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Advantages of this treatment are- </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Glow in the skin</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces pore size</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Tightens the elasticity of the skin</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces fine lines</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>5) SKIN BOOSTERS-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-boosters/\">Skin boosters</a> are made up of stabilised hyaluronic acid which is a hygroscopic molecule naturally present in our body. It is injected through a wide face area in microdoses in the dermal layer of the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This treatment provides deep skin hydration, improves elasticity of the skin and makes the skin soft and smooth with radiance.We recommend this treatment for those with dull and dry skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>6) SKINFINITY’S DERMARADIANCE TREATMENT-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>We recommend this treatment for those with uneven skin tone as in this procedure we use DERMAFRAC technology to infuse kojic acid which is a depigmenting agent.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>7)SKINFINITY DERMAPORE REFINER (DERMAPEN 4)-</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This treatment is recommended for those with concerns like enlarged pore size and acne scars.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermapen-4/\">Dermapen 4 </a>is  a microneedling device designed to create a safe healing response within the body to ignite collagen and elastin production from within the skin, along with minimal downtime thus resulting in healthier skin with refined pores, even toned and reduced wrinkles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>We usually recommend atleast 3 sessions once a month for the above mentioned indications.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>8) DERMAL FILLERS</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>-Under eye hollow is one indication which cannot be concealed even with a concealer. So, under-eye fillers work the best in such cases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>-Lip enhancement with <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler/\"><strong>dermal fillers</strong></a>, restructures and adds volume to the lips, thus drastically enhancing the facial appearance.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The effect usually lasts for 1.5 years.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hair Treatments for Bride-To-Be</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Mesotherapy-  We usually recommend atleast 3-6 sessions of mesotherapy before the wedding. In this procedure, with the help of electroporation we infuse meso solution containing essential peptides and vitamins into the hair roots. This ensures that your hair roots can withstand the damage caused by hair styling during the wedding days, thus resulting in minimal hair fall post-wedding.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>GFC (GROWTH FACTOR CONCENTRATE) & PRP (PLATELET RICH PLASMA)- These treatments are recommended for those presenting with active hair fall and poor density before wedding. Atleast 4 sessions are recommended before the wedding.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Body Treatments for Bride-To-Be</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Full body skin brightening-  In this treatment, <strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\">chemical peels</a></strong> are used according to the skin type to achieve the desired brightening. Generally 3-4 sessions are recommended.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Full body skin polishing and de-tan- In this treatment,<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong>microdermabrasion</strong> </a>is performed wherein the top most layer of skin is removed followed by application of solutions/serums which have a depigmenting action.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>IV Glutathione-</p>\r\n\r\n <p>Skin lightening through <strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/iv-glutathoine-therapy/\">IV Glutathione</a></strong> is also available. The dermatologist decides the dose, typically once weekly for the first two months, followed by maintenance sessions.</p>\r\n\r\n <p>If you are wondering about the<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/bridal-packages/\"> <strong>bridal packages cost in Noida</strong></a>, Skinfinity offers customized packages to suit different skin and hair concerns while being cost-effective and transparent.</p>\r\n\r\n <p>For any queries, get in touch with our <strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\">expert dermatologists in gurgaon</a></strong> at Skinfinity today and glow beautifully on your special day!</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/0dfadcb9379ed9f190f4c65cdef197de.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Pre-bridal treatments ', 'Pre-bridal treatments for the ravishing bridal glow', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-10-16 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(409, 'autumn-is-here', 'Autumn is here! What skin care routine should you follow? ', 'Does your skin appear flaky and bland? Seasonal changes are probably to blame since they cause dead skin cells to accumulate, which then traps oil and germs beneath the skin\'s surface and increases acne outbreaks.', '<p><strong>Does your skin appear flaky and bland? Seasonal changes are probably to blame since they cause dead skin cells to accumulate, which then traps oil and germs beneath the skin&#39;s surface and increases acne outbreaks.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>So it&#39;s time to incorporate a new skincare regime into your daily routine. For the finest skincare routine, continue reading.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>The essential skin care routine</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<h3>1.<strong>Cleansing</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>The first step in any skincare routine is cleansing. Before using any other products, the upper layers of the skin must be cleansed. </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Any milk or cream cleanser can be used as they are gentle enough to be used throughout the year. Drier skin types, however, may occasionally benefit from using richer balms or oils to help replenish lost lipids and lessen flakiness. Always wash your face with lukewarm water after using a cleanser.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>1. Moisturizing</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>You&#39;re likely to experience even more dryness as autumn transits into winter. When the temperature drops, using a good moisturizer becomes even more crucial as it forms a layer over the skin and prevents water from evaporating. You can even use leave-on moisturizing masks and balms for an extra moisture boost.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <h3><strong>Exfoliation</strong></h3>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Our skin becomes lustreless, dry and dull in the autumn. As a result, the skin may require exfoliation in the form of scrubs, microdermabrasion or peels to make it look young and vibrant.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Exfoliating frequently promotes cellular renewal and eliminates dead skin cells that could prevent moisturizers or serums from being absorbed by the skin.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>When choosing a scrub, go for one that contains natural exfoliants like bamboo, clay, or pineapple. Ensure that it matches your skin type.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>4. Sunscreen application</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Winter and autumn sun exposure can be just as dangerous as summer exposure. Consequently, you must include a broad spectrum, water resistant sunscreen in your skincare routine along with physical protection.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <h3><strong>Serums as prescribed by the dermatologist</strong></h3>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Using a correct serum according to the skin type is very important. Hyaluronic acid serum contains a natural humectant, hyaluronic acid which binds to water molecules in the atmosphere, pulls them down to your skin, and retains them there; thus hydrating the dull and dry skin.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>While following the skin care regimen, we always forget to take care of our lips.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>As winter pops in, lips become extra dry and chapped. Always use nourishing lip balms with spf to keep lips hydrated, nourished and to prevent them from pigmentation. </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <h3><strong>Balanced diet and exercise</strong></h3>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Taking a balanced diet is not only good for your skin but also for your body. Fruits and vegetables like pumpkin, and green vegetables provide extra nourishment and help in detoxification.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Hence, when your body is fresh and clean, you get that automatic glow on your face. </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Consuming at least 2-4 liters of water each day is essential to keep the skin hydrated.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Follow a good skincare routine and take in everything that nature has offered! Also, if you’re facing some serious skin problems that require care, you can always rely on Skinfinity. Get in touch with us.</strong></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/9f0c2c76c6c819c650518acd5989960f.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Autumn is here!', 'Does your skin appear flaky and bland? Seasonal changes are probably to blame since they cause dead skin cells to accumulate, which then traps oil and germs beneath the skin\'s surface and increases acne outbreaks.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-10-10 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(410, 'clinical-facials-for', '3 clinical facials for radiant and glowing skin this festive season', 'Is your skin festive ready? Everyone wants to look their best around this time of the year. You must know that holistic approach is the secret to a radiant skin. Balanced diet, adequate hydration, exercise, sun protectio', '<p>Is your skin festive ready? Everyone wants to look their best around this time of the year. You must know that holistic approach is the secret to a radiant skin. Balanced diet, adequate hydration, exercise, sun protection and dermatologist recommended skin care regime are the most important principles for a healthy skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>With the festive season around, who doesn’t want a ravishing glow? Don&#39;t miss the chance to be the center of attention in your get-togethers.. In this post, we&#39;ll talk about a few procedures that will help you achieve a glam, festive-ready look.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Hydrafacial</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydrafacial is the talk of the town these days because of the instant glow achieved after the procedure.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydrafacial combines exfoliation, hydration, extraction, cleansing, and antioxidant protection. The benefits of hydrafacial are:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Rejuvenation</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Brightening</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hydration</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Exfoliation</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Brightening</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Extraction of black heads and white heads</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>3 main principles of hydrafacial are:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1 Cleanse : with a pH balanced cleanser</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Extract: The top most dead layer of skin is removed. The tip also removes debris from the pores, thus unclogging them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Hydrate: The third and final part of this treatment is to infuse and protect the skin with boosters or serums. In this process, uneven skin tone, hyperpigmentation, fine lines, wrinkles, and enlarged pores are also targetted.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Our advanced hydrafacial further includes anti-ageing steps like radiofrequency and ultrasound for skin tightening.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Laser toning/ Hollywood Peel</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Carbon laser peel is another name for laser toning. It is an efficient way to treat pigmentation and uneven skin tone. The best results are observed in 7-10 days after the procedure. It is a painless procedure with minimal downtime.The benefits of this treatment area-</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Improves skin texture</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces fine lines and wrinkles</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Tightens dilated pores</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces acne, post- acne marks and scars</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Stimulates collagen production</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Downtime minimal to zero</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Chemical peel</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Chemical peeling is one of the most commonly done procedures where chemical solutions are used to remove the top layer of your skin, thus boosting  your skin’s appearance. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>The benefits of this treatment are:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces acne</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Evens out the skin tone</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces fine lines</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Reduces pigmentation</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Improves rough and dull skin</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>About 88 percent of women don’t know the right products for their skin and use the wrong products on their skin. Please consult your dermatologist before receiving any treatment to ensure the procedure is safe for you and works the best on your skin. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>For any queries, get in touch with our <a href=\"https://g.co/kgs/FbceXbV\"><strong>expert dermatologists in noida </strong></a> at Skinfinity. </p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/f8a833a28d066107e0d77166d5c8bc37.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', '3 clinical facials for radiant and glowing skin this festive season', 'Is your skin festive ready? Everyone wants to look their best around this time of the year.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-10-05 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(411, 'is-hair-transplant-surgery-permanent', 'Is hair transplant surgery permanent?', 'Awareness about hair transplantation as an effective way of dealing with the hair loss problem has increased manifolds in the recent past.', '<p>Awareness about hair transplantation as an effective way of dealing with the hair loss problem has increased manifolds in the recent past. Whenever a sophisticated treatment process becomes accessible to people at large, it gives rise to many queries. Therefore, it is not surprising that more and more people now want to know more about various aspects of the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-transplant-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>hair transplantation clinic</strong></a> procedure. One such aspect is the durability of the transplanted hair. Almost everyone, who is considering the transplantation, wants to know whether the transplanted hair will be permanent or not.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Yes, hair transplantation is a permanent solution</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The answer is affirmative as hair transplantation is surely a permanent way to cure hair loss. This can be understood through a very simple reason. Anyone can observe that most of the bald people have good amount of hair at the back of their heads. These are most durable hairs on human head which are known for being DHT (dihydrotestosterone) resistant or hormone resistant. These are the hair follicles which are used in the transplantation when you choose either of the most widely used transplantation procedure FUE or FUT. Back of the head, from where these hairs are taken, is known as donor area while the bald area, where these are transplanted, is known as the recipient area. Since these hairs at the back of head are permanent by nature so once they are transplanted in the recipient area then any hair coming out of such transplanted root is also permanent in nature. Therefore there is hardly any chance of you losing these hairs in future and hence, it could be considered a permanent cure.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>It becomes a natural part your body</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Since the transplanted hair is extracted from your own body, therefore, it would always look natural and will perfectly suit you. You can do all the grooming and nurturing acts like washing, conditioning, cutting, shaving, dyeing and so on. Even when you cut or shave these will just grow again like your natural hair. However, there is one aspect of hair transplantation, knowledge of which can greatly help you in dealing with the procedure. There will be a temporary loss of the transplanted hair which may occur just after one month of the transplantation. It may continue for the following 2 months. However, there is no need to worry as it is a natural part of the treatment process about which all patients are educated and sensitized by the surgeon in advance. After 3 months of surgery your transplanted hairs will start growing at a normal rate. These new hairs will remain there for the rest of your life and you will not need any additional maintenance or medicines for that.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Be focused on the long term solution</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Being mindful of the fact about temporary loss of hair just after one month the treatment will help you immensely in dealing with the entire process. It is natural for our body’s immune system to respond to any injury or trauma in order to heal it. So when hair transplantation takes place the body takes it as trauma and the corresponding hair loss is a result of the body’s response. Such a loss of hair is known as shock loss. However this can also be reduced significantly if you get the transplantation done by a highly experienced surgeon. Once your transplanted hairs regrow at normal rate after 3 months there is hardly any scope of these hairs roots (follicles) getting lost or thin ever in future. However, old hairs present in the recipient (transplanted) area may continue to follow their natural loss pattern. You can very well prevent these losses by going for medication. For this you may get the advice of your surgeon who will be the most appropriate person to prescribe the right medicines.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Getting educated about processes helps</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Getting educated about the overall transplantation process and careful selection of the right surgeon for transplantation may help you have a permanent solution for the hair loss problem. Going blindly for the least costly transplantation may not be the right approach when you are looking for a permanent cure. Nowadays, you have a plethora of finance options like credit card EMI conversion and loans through which you can raise your affordability but you should ensure that you get the best treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you wish to know more about the process in detail you may contact your consultant who would be happy to help you clearing all doubts regarding hair transplantation.</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/1526a6b60026f606ddfcff7266a87b6e.png', 'permanent hair transplant', 'permanent hair transplant', 'Awareness about hair transplantation as an effective way of dealing with the hair loss problem has increased manifolds in the recent past.', 'permanent hair transplant', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"permanent hair transplant\"]', 0, 1, '2022-09-25 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(412, 'dealing-with-unwanted-hair', 'Dealing with Unwanted Hair? Try Laser Hair Reduction Treatments That Work', 'Tired of unwanted hair? Laser hair reduction offers safe, lasting results for all skin types. Explore expert treatments at Skinfinity Derma.', '<p><strong>Unwanted body hair</strong> can be frustrating, time-consuming, and even affect your confidence. While waxing and shaving offer temporary relief, they often lead to skin irritation, ingrown hairs, and fast regrowth. That’s where <strong>laser hair reduction treatments</strong> come in — offering a <strong>long-lasting, safe, and effective</strong> solution for men and women alike.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re looking for the <strong>best laser hair removal in Noida</strong>, this guide will walk you through everything you need to know — from <strong>benefits</strong> and <strong>pre-treatment tips</strong> to <strong>costs</strong> and why <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong></a> is a trusted choice.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2> <strong>Why Choose Laser Hair Reduction?</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Laser hair removal is a medically-approved procedure that uses focused light energy to target hair follicles, gradually reducing hair growth over several sessions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3> <strong>Top Benefits of Laser Hair Reduction</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Permanent Hair Reduction</strong>: Noticeable results in just <strong>6–8 sessions</strong>, depending on hair type and skin tone.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Precision & Safety</strong>: Targets only the hair follicle without damaging surrounding skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Quick Sessions</strong>: Small areas (like underarms or upper lip) can be treated in under <strong>15 minutes</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Less Pain, More Gain</strong>: Unlike waxing, this treatment is <strong>virtually painless</strong> with modern technology.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Improved Skin Texture</strong>: Over time, laser helps reduce ingrown hairs and pigmentation caused by traditional methods.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3> <strong>Pre-Treatment Tips for Best Results</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Before your laser hair reduction session, it’s crucial to follow proper skin preparation guidelines:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Avoid Sun Exposure</strong>: Stay out of direct sunlight or tanning beds for at least <strong>2 weeks</strong> prior.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>No Waxing or Plucking</strong>: Avoid methods that remove hair from the root 4–6 weeks before treatment. Shaving is allowed.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Cleanse the Area</strong>: Ensure the treatment area is clean and <strong>free of creams, deodorants, or makeup</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Consult First</strong>: Have a detailed one-on-one consultation with a certified dermatologist to evaluate your skin and hair type.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h3> <strong>Why Choose Skinfinity Derma for Laser Hair Removal in Noida?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong> is one of the most trusted names for <strong>advanced <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-removal-noida/\">laser hair reduction in Noida</a> </strong>known for its <strong>US-FDA approved technology</strong> and <strong>triple wavelength diode lasers</strong>, ensuring the highest safety and efficacy across all skin types.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here’s what makes Skinfinity stand out:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Experienced dermatologists & certified technicians</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Customized treatment plans based on individual needs</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Transparent pricing with no hidden charges</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Strict hygiene and safety protocols</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Positive client testimonials and consistent results</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What About the Cost?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Concerned about pricing? Laser hair removal is now <strong>more affordable than ever</strong>. While costs vary depending on the treatment area, <strong>Skinfinity Derma offers competitive full-body packages</strong> that provide better value than treating areas individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Want a detailed breakdown of full body laser hair removal costs?</strong><br>\r\nCheck out our complete guide:<br>\r\n<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/full-body-laser-hair-removal/\">Full Body Laser Hair Removal Cost in Delhi </a>(noida)</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Laser hair reduction is not just a cosmetic treatment — it’s an <strong>investment in your confidence</strong> and self-care routine. Say goodbye to razors, waxing strips, and painful hair removal methods.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Book your consultation with <strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong> today to get a <strong>customized hair reduction plan</strong> that suits your needs and budget.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3> Serving Locations:</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Laser Hair Removal in Noida</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Laser Hair Removal in Gurgaon</strong></p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/d9c70b0b48be27fd3a83ad7b10855848.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Dealing Unwanted Hair with Laser Hair Reduction Treatments', 'Dealing with unwanted hair can give you a hard time, and you need to look after that before you get started with anything', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-09-15 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(413, 'are-acne-marks', 'Are Acne Marks Permanent?', 'Acne are troublesome. Coming on good terms with these pimples is a rare thing.', '<p>Acne are troublesome. Coming on good terms with these pimples is a rare thing. If you are feeling sad about a tiny breakout on your special day, then you must know it is quite common and has happened with most of us.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne occurs due to clogged pores and excess secretion of sebum. It takes 3-4 days to resolve on its own. The aftermath of acne is the scars that are left behind. Post <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\">acne marks treatment in noida</a>  can be distressing. These scars fade away at a much slower rate and cause an uneven texture of the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What causes these acne scars?</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Inflammatory Acne: Acne due to hormonal imbalances like <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-and-hair-in-pcos/\">PCOS </a>or thyroidism develops as cystic or nodular growth, deep-seated in the skin tissue. This acne leaves a scar that often appears reddish in color.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Untreated CysticAcne: The untreated acnes penetrate deeper into tissue and cause scarring.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Excess touching or popping-out acnes: Touching your face transfers bacteria from your hands to face, thereby clogging pores and resulting in breakouts. These breakouts can be itchy, and some people tend to squeeze them. Squeezing out increases the size of the wound and pushes the contents of acne into adjoining tissue.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Poor hygiene: Hygiene is important because bacteria that cause acne multiplies in an unhygienic environment. Pillowcases and wipe cloth are the two most common places for bacteria to adhere and grow.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>What are the types of Acne Scars?</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Normal fine-line Scar: Appears as line and fades out quickly if appropriately treated.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hypertrophic Scar: Raised above the skin and appear as a small lump of healing tissue.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Atrophic scar: These scars are deep-seated on the surface of the skin, giving it an uneven texture.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Post Inflammatory Hyperpigmentation:</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A healed acne lesion appears as a brown patch. This PIH resolves with topical application of medication and adequate sun protection. This pigmentation is more prone in people with a habit of squeezing out acne.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Where can I get the best treatment?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity is the answer if you are looking for <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong>acne scar treatment in Noida</strong></a>. With a wide range of treatment options, a dermatologist can suggest the right one for your skin type. It is essential to work on the root cause of acne. A combination of therapies works best in the removal of acne scars for good.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Chemical Peels: Chemical peels are an excellent option for a start. These peels consist of mild acids which gently remove the outermost layer of skin and produce newer skin in 5-7 days. These peels are absolutely safe and painless. They also reduce the appearance of fine wrinkles, dead skin, and pigmentation. Regular sittings, as advised by dermatologists, promote glowing skin with reduced appearance of scars.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Derma-roller: It is best suited for mild to moderate scarring. These rollers induce pricking on the skin and induce the synthesis of collagen to improve overall texture of the skin and reduce the visibility of the scar tissue. It is not advised on wheatish or darker skin tones as it causes PIH (Post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation).</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Laser treatment for acne scars</strong>: Undoubtedly, the most popular<strong> treatment for acne scars</strong>. Laser treatments work best on active acne or acne scars. Fraxel DUO laser is the cutting-edge technology for skin resurfacing and reducing the appearance of scar tissue in 6-7 sessions. It can be used on any type of scarred tissue. It is also effective in combating the effects of sun damage, photoaging, pigmentation, uneven skin tone, uneven texture, and stretch marks.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Microdermabrasion: It effectively removes the shallow scars which appear as small pits on your skin surface. This procedure is ideally suited for the removal of teenage scars.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Collagen Therapy: Adjunction of collagen therapy with any above-mentioned procedures improves the elasticity of the skin. It also enhances the effectiveness of treatment procedures and diminishes the appearance of scar tissue.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne scars are not going to resolve overnight. You need to see an expert who can tell you which treatment is most suitable for you. Skinfinity has a team of highly trained and knowledgeable doctors who can help you get your glowing skin back. Our clinic is the best place for<strong> Acne Scar Treatment In Noida</strong>. Be ready to say goodbye to those stubborn acne scars.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/f3c62ba682b24b2a8509e2af5b88cb90.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Are Acne Marks Permanent?', 'Acne are troublesome. Coming on good terms with these pimples is a rare thing. If you are feeling sad about a tiny breakout on your special day, ', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-09-05 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(414, 'laser-facial', 'Laser Facial Rejuvenation: Everything you need to know!', 'What is the best laser treatment for aging skin? Is laser treatment good for face? How much does a laser treatment cost? ', '<p>What is the best laser treatment for aging skin? Is laser treatment good for face? How much does a laser treatment cost? Do you have similar questions regarding Laser Facial Rejuvenation? Let’s find out everything you need to know about laser facial rejuvenation.<br>\r\nWhat is laser facial rejuvenation? Why is facial rejuvenation done?<br>\r\nResurfacing the face using a laser to improve skin’s appearance or correct minor flaws is known as laser facial rejuvenation. It is done for facial skin issues like:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Aging skin<br>\r\nWrinkles<br>\r\nAging spots<br>\r\nUneven skin tone <br>\r\nDamage due to sun <br>\r\nScars due to acne </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Laser facial rejuvenation treatment can help get rid of these issues or treat them in such a way as to reduce visibility. <br>\r\nWhat to do if you’re preparing to get a laser facial rejuvenation?<br>\r\nAt Skinfinity, our experts will do a thorough checkup before suggesting you to go for a laser facial rejuvenation. This will include knowing about your medical history. This can include knowing about your past and current medications, any previous cosmetic surgeries you might have had, etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After this, our highly-experienced dermatologists will perform a physical examination of your face. This process consists of analyzing the tone and thickness of your skin so that the experts can decide the intensity of the treatment required. The area that needs to be treated will be thoroughly inspected for various physical aspects.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The third step we follow at Skinfinity is a proper discussion about what you want to achieve through the treatment. The experts will tell you the risks involved and the results you can expect. This will help you make an informed decision. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Once you’re done with these steps, we would recommend a few things you need to do before your laser facial rejuvenation. This includes taking medication if required, stopping smoking for a while, and avoiding direct sun exposure. For more details on sun protection, get in touch with your doctor and they’ll guide you. <br>\r\nWhat to expect from the laser facial rejuvenation: During and after the treatment<br>\r\nThe treatment requires a laser beam that is directed toward your skin. For this procedure, the staff at Skinfinity might have to sedate your face or numb the area that is supposed to undergo the treatment. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>The intense laser beam will destroy the epidermis of the skin (the outer layer) and heat the dermis (underlying skin) which will enhance collagen production in due course. The whole process can take anywhere between 30 minutes to 2 hours depending on the size of the area that is being treated. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>After the procedure, you might experience:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You might feel that the treated skin is itchy, dry, and swollen after the laser facial rejuvenation. <br>\r\nExperts at Skinfinity will apply a thick gel or ointment to the area that has been treated. This will seal the area and prevent air or water to damage the raw skin. <br>\r\nDoctors might recommend you to take painkillers or apply ice packs.<br>\r\nWhat to do after the procedure? What results can you expect?<br>\r\nAfter the procedure, take the necessary precautions and care of your skin as suggested by the doctor which includes not using cosmetic products, protecting your skin from direct exposure, etc. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Once your skin starts to heal, which can take a few weeks or a month, you’ll be able to see that the skin&#39;s appearance has improved. The effect of laser facial rejuvenation can last for years depending on your skin type. Skinfinity highly recommends using sun protection of at least SPF 30 after the process. Visit Skinfinity to know more about the procedure and the cost of laser facial rejuvenation.</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/b90b2462f6df16e96bf09f9f9103c3c2.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Laser Facial Rejuvenation: Everything you need to know!', 'What is the best laser treatment for aging skin? Is laser treatment good for face? How much does a laser treatment cost? Do you have similar questions regarding Laser Facial Rejuvenation?', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-08-20 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(415, 'give-your-skin', 'Give Your Skin The Best With Skinfinity’s Organic Hydrafacial ', 'Organic Hydrafacial is a process that works to deep-clean, exfoliate, and hydrate your skin. It is also known as hydradermabrasion as it uses a gentle form of microdermabrasion,', '<p>Organic Hydrafacial is a process that works to deep-clean, exfoliate, and hydrate your skin. It is also known as hydradermabrasion as it uses a gentle form of microdermabrasion, and employs jets of water?—instead of lasers or abrasive materials such as crystals?—to lightly exfoliate surface skin. It uses a patented device that employs a vortex swirling action to deliver hydration and it also removes dead skin, dirt, debris, and impurities while cleansing and soothing the skin. This allows the procedure to resurface and cleanse the skin without causing irritation. Unlike traditional facial treatments that can have different effects depending on your skin type, an <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/organic-hydrafacial/\"><strong>organic hydrafacial </strong></a>provides consistent results and can be used on all skin types. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>What To Expect During The Treatment? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cleansing and Exfoliation: This is the first process in the hydrafacial where your aesthetician will use a vortex cleansing and a hydra peel tip to gently cleanse and exfoliate your skin. This is done to remove dead skin and sebum and opens up the pores. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Chemical Peel: A chemical peel will be delivered to your skin using the same device. <strong>Organic Hydrafacials use</strong> a non-irritating mix of salicylic and glycolic acids for a gentle yet effective peel. The purpose of this step is to loosen deep pore debris.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Extraction: In this process, the device will use a strong, painless vortex vacuum suction in order to remove blackheads and impurities from the pores. The impurities are collected in a cup to be discarded later. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hydrating Serum: In the final step, a soothing proprietary antioxidative and hydrating serum with peptides and other beneficial nutrients will be applied to the skin. This helps to detoxify, rejuvenate, and hydrate the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What Are The Benefits Of Getting An Organic Hydrafacial? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>They work on all skin types. If you have acne-prone, highly sensitive, dry, or oily skin, the organic hydrafacial will still be suitable for you. <br>\r\nYou can achieve a consistently high-quality treatment every time since most of the treatment is controlled through organic hydrafacial technology. <br>\r\nThere is literally no downtime to getting an organic hydrafacial. You can go about your day just as you please. <br>\r\nOrganic Hydrafacials are non-invasive and show an immediate outcome. <br>\r\nThey also even out your skin tone and reduce hyperpigmentation. <br>\r\nThey reduce the appearance of enlarged pores on your skin. <br>\r\nThe combined forces of cleansing, exfoliating, and extraction present in this procedure help to reduce the appearance of acne and prevent future outbreaks.<br>\r\nOrganic Hydrafacials also help reduce the appearance of fine lines and wrinkles. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Are There Any Side Effects? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Organic Hydrafacials do not cause any pain or redness. Since it is a non-invasive procedure, it is mostly free of complications and side effects. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>How Often Should I Get An Organic Hydrafacial? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>In case you have never had an organic hydrafacial in the past, it is usually advisable to get it at least twice a month. Once a better baseline has been established for facial skin health, you will notice results even with a single appointment every month. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Why Choose Skinfinity? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity prioritizes your needs and places you under the care and supervision of Dr. Johri, who keeps up with the latest trends, methods, and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. Skinfinity uses only US FDA-approved products and lasers, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>For a detailed consultation, book an appointment now! <br>\r\n </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/fe37d251b8d0c361c426535953c9d417.jpg', 'Hydrafacial', 'Give Your Skin The Best With Skinfinity’s Organic Hydrafacial ', 'Organic Hydrafacial is a process that works to deep-clean, exfoliate, and hydrate your skin. It is also known as hydradermabrasion as it uses a gentle form of microdermabrasion,', 'Hydrafacial in Gurgaon, Dermatologist in Gurgaon , Hydrafacial', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Hydrafacial\",\"Hydrafacial treatment\",\"Hydrafacial benefits\"]', 0, 1, '2022-08-15 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(416, 'anti-aging-thread', 'Anti-aging: Thread Lift: Is It Better Than Facelift?', 'Has your skin started to loosen up or sag, especially around the areas like the jawline, eyebrow line, under the eye, cheeks, forehead, etc?', '<p><br>\r\nHas your skin started to loosen up or sag, especially around the areas like the jawline, eyebrow line, under the eye, cheeks, forehead, etc? Then, you might want to opt for<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/thread-lift\"><strong> thread lift anti-aging treatment</strong></a>. But are you confused about whether you should go for a thread lift or a facelift? Will the procedure have any side effects or complications? Let’s answer all your queries. But before that, let’s know some details about Thread Lift anti-aging process. <br>\r\nWhat is Anti-Aging: Thread Lift?<br>\r\nAs the name suggests, this<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\"> </a><strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\">anti-aging treatment </a>procedure</strong> lifts the skin instead of removing the loose skin. This is done with the help of medical-grade threads or sutures. These threads or sutures are inserted into the skin using needles and then the experts pull the skin to properly shape and texture the skin while reducing the sag. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>This process not only helps in anti-aging by just lifting it up using threads but also helps the body to do it naturally. Due to the body’s default response to something being inserted into the skin, a large amount of collagen is directed toward the area that is being treated. This helps in healing the skin naturally. <br>\r\nAnti-aging: Thread Lift vs Facelift | Are there any advantages of getting a thread lift?<br>\r\nLet’s list down the major advantages that thread lift treatment has over facelift:<br>\r\nThread lifts are relatively low risk when compared to facelifts. This is because thread lifts are very less invasive when compared to facelifts.<br>\r\nRecovering after a thread lift procedure is relatively easy as the process is performed under local anesthesia. The effect is very short-termed and patients can even drive themselves home.<br>\r\nThe recovery time after a thread lift surgery is way faster than a facelift. Patients undergoing facelifts have to be heavily sedated during the procedure. They also have to take 2-3 weeks off from work to recover from the process. Thread lift on the other hand is really fast when it comes to recovery from the procedure. <br>\r\nThread lifts are easier to perform when compared to facelifts thus making the process more affordable. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>What are the advantages of the thread lift <strong>anti-aging procedure</strong>?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Thread lift procedure offers a lot of benefits such as:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It enhances collagen production by triggering the body’s natural healing process.<br>\r\nThe process also improves skin textures as the increased collagen production increases the density of the skin.<br>\r\nIt can help reducing skin laxity.<br>\r\nThe process is non-invasive in nature, uses medically approved safe materials, and has long-lasting results. <br>\r\nIt helps in reducing wrinkles. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Where can you find the best thread lift treatment in Delhi NCR?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Although the <strong>thread lift anti-aging treatment</strong> is less risky, it does require high levels of expertise and precision. If you are looking for the<strong> best thread lift treatment in Delhi NCR </strong>at affordable prices, you should definitely trust Skinfinity Derma. At Skinfinity Derma, you get highly experienced and thoroughly trained staff along with experienced doctors. The infrastructure and equipment at Skinfinity are world-class and meet all the industry standards. We follow all the necessary protocols to ensure that you have a great experience and your skin feels new and rejuvenated.<br>\r\n </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/d90f604c3e665a8f9f60a313eeafa4ee.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Anti-aging: Thread Lift: Is It Better Than Facelift?', 'Has your skin started to loosen up or sag, especially around the areas like the jawline, eyebrow line, under the eye, cheeks, forehead, etc?', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-08-10 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(417, 'anti-aging-remedies', 'Anti-Aging Remedies For Wrinkles And Fine Lines ', 'We completely empathize with you when you tell us that aging is your worst enemy. After all, who doesn’t want youthful and younger-looking skin? However,', '<p>We completely empathize with you when you tell us that aging is your worst enemy. After all, who doesn’t want youthful and younger-looking skin? However, if only you knew that you could overcome aging one step at a time through a few <strong>anti-aging remedies</strong> that you could try at home, wouldn’t you be all in for that? So, let’s dive into this and find out how to reverse the signs of aging with a few simple tricks! </p>\r\n\r\n<p>But Firstly, What Is Anti-Aging? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anti-aging can be made possible when the process of regeneration is dominant over degeneration. While in degeneration, the existing skin cells replace themselves with weaker cells, in regeneration, the existing cells are replaced by stronger cells. This process of regeneration of skin cells is termed anti-aging. Here are some ways you can battle aging by getting rid of your wrinkles and fine lines. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>What Are The Home Remedies? </p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Honey: Honey exfoliates the skin to remove dead cells and promotes the regeneration of new cells. It is an antioxidant-rich compound that acts as a powerful anti-aging regimen. It also helps lighten the age spots, and vitamin B and potassium present in honey also help in improving skin elasticity and suppleness.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Fenugreek: A rich source of vitamin B3 and niacin that helps in recovering the damaged skin cells and promotes the regeneration of new cells and tissues, fenugreek seeds help in lightening age spots, hyperpigmentation wrinkles, fine lines, and crow’s feet that form on the forehead, and at the corner of eyes and lips.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Bananas: Bananas are a cheap, easily available, and natural anti-aging remedy. These are loaded with nutrients such as potassium, vitamin B, vitamin C, and vitamin E which makes it a complete remedy for all skin problems.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Aloe Vera: Malic acid present in aloe vera gel improves skin elasticity and reduces wrinkles and fine lines- the most evident signs of skin aging. Zinc present in the gel increases the youthfulness of the skin by shrinking the pores. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Olive Oil: The anti-aging properties of olive oil can be attributed to the polyphenols and oleic acid present in it. Powered with monounsaturated fats and Vitamins B and D, it prevents the appearance of new wrinkles and also tackles the existing ones.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Egg Whites: An egg white mask is an extremely effective way to lighten fine lines and wrinkles. By applying egg whites to the wrinkled area of the skin, the skin can be stretched and open pores can be shrunk to provide the skin with a smoother, younger, and youthful appearance. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Lemon Juice: Being a rich source of citric acid, lemon juice helps in exfoliating the skin, removing dead skin cells and impurities, and shrinking open pores to provide a smoother and younger appearance to the skin. It tightens the tissues and increases skin elasticity to reduce the appearance of wrinkles and fine lines.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Pineapples: Pineapple juice helps prevent premature aging. Being loaded with antioxidants such as potassium and vitamin C, pineapple juice helps in neutralizing the harmful effects of free radicals and oxidative stress of cells thus preventing premature aging of the skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Almonds: Almonds are loaded with nutrients such as vitamin E, iron, zinc, folic acid, and oleic acid that function as powerful antioxidants which prevent the degeneration of collagen fibers of the skin and delay aging process by treating wrinkles and fine lines.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Avocados: These help increase suppleness and youthfulness by increasing skin elasticity. It acts as a nourishing moisturizer for excessive dry skin that also helps in repairing damaged cells and promotes the regeneration of new cells. The antioxidants prevent premature aging. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Even though aging may cause wrinkles, fine lines, and other unpleasant visual effects, methods like anti-aging remedies do exist that can be utilized to slow down the development of these problems and in some cases, even reduce the appearance of existing issues that have already developed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Why Choose Skinfinity? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have tried these ways, but are unable to eliminate the signs of aging, visit us at Skinfinity. We have various treatments, ranging from PRP to Anti wrinkle injection, to help you get rid of all these signs. Skinfinity prioritizes your needs and places you under the care and supervision of Dr. Johri, who keeps up with the latest trends, methods, and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. Skinfinity uses only US FDA-approved products and lasers, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>For a detailed consultation, book an appointment now! </p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/e771b482ec7a8e21fc0edc2064959768.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Anti-Aging Remedies For Wrinkles And Fine Lines ', 'We completely empathize with you when you tell us that aging is your worst enemy. After all, who doesn’t want youthful and younger-looking skin? However', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-08-05 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(418, 'how-to-get-fuller', 'How To Get Fuller, More Defined Eyebrows With Microblading', 'Fuller, more defined eyebrows are a huge part of our facial beauty. As women get older, their eyebrow growth slows down,', '<p>Fuller, more defined eyebrows are a huge part of our facial beauty. As women get older, their eyebrow growth slows down, and they become thinner. But the good news is, there&#39;s an easy fix for this! By using microblading, a professional can give you fuller and more defined eyebrows in just one session. Depending on your preferences, you can keep your brows natural or add color. This service has been proven to last up to a decade, and it&#39;s safe to use!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Why do You Need Full Eyebrows?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The second rule of brows comes down to a single question: Does it matter if you don&#39;t have full brows? The answer is yes. In the same way that no one wants to be known as the ugly bald guy, no one wants to be the bald guy without eyebrows. So what is eyebrow growth? Eyebrow growth is the process by which you add new hair to your forehead, which is a necessary part of growing your hair. But there&#39;s a problem: if you grow your eyebrows, you need to take measures to keep the hairs on your forehead from falling out.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What Is Microblading?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Microblading is a popular semi-permanent hair tattoo that can be used to fill in bald spots and cover scars and other areas of your skin that need some camouflage. Microblading uses tiny hair strokes to fill areas where the hair has been removed. The strokes are typically very small, measuring about 0.25 mm, and are only visible under a magnifying glass. They look natural and give the appearance of having hair in the area.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How Can I Get Microbladed Eyebrows?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>To keep up with the times, some people have had the option of getting microblade eyebrows. However, with the rise of the Internet, finding the proper information has been much easier than it was back in the day. With the popularity of the Internet, it is easy to find reviews of different places and techniques. In addition to online research and videos, many clinics now provide the option of getting microblade brows.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Should I Go Through With It?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes! For many women, microblading is the perfect way to add some definition and color to their eyebrows without looking unnatural. While it may seem intimidating initially, if you take the time to read the instructions carefully and follow the steps, you&#39;ll be a pro at it in no time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Remember: Microblading is essentially permanent makeup, but it&#39;s temporary in the sense that it can be removed. So it&#39;s not something you should rush into. You&#39;ll want to do your research and see if you want to invest the time and money.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Where Can I Get It Done?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Many of us spend hours trying to make our eyebrows perfect, and some even consider it an art form, but not all of us can afford the pricey eyebrow pencils or even the high-quality brow products. With microblading, you simply have a machine that applies pigment to your skin, making the shape of your eyebrows perfectly defined. You can get microblading done anywhere, from a dermatologist to a beauty salon. It&#39;s a fast and affordable way to achieve beautifully shaped eyebrows.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In conclusion, if you&#39;re tired of looking at those droopy, saggy eyebrows that just make you look old, you may want to try microblading. If you want the look of naturally full eyebrows but don&#39;t want to have to pluck hairs or have any scars after your procedure, then this is a great choice for you. Microblading is a highly sought-after procedure that enhances and redefines the shape and definition of eyebrows. We know that eyebrows play a huge role in our overall appearance and can completely change the entire look of our faces. Microblading is a great, affordable way to get fuller, more defined eyebrows, and it&#39;s painless, too. Here&#39;s how it works.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To find out more about Seborrheic dermatitis or to schedule an appointment with a dermatologist near you, visit <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">https://www.skinfinityderma.com/</a> or call +91 98999 61629</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/2cf5e951d970aff6fcae4e1b1c743e00.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'How To Get Fuller, More Defined Eyebrows With Microblading', 'Fuller, more defined eyebrows are a huge part of our facial beauty.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-07-29 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(419, 'growth-factor-therapy', 'Growth Factor Therapy ', 'It\'s a highly beneficial treatment for hair as well as skin as it contains a highly concentrated amount of growth factors. Therefore, it has a long-lasting effect on hair and skin.', '<p>It&#39;s a highly beneficial treatment for hair as well as skin as it contains a highly concentrated amount of growth factors. Therefore, it has a long-lasting effect on hair and skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How is Growth Factor therapy Beneficial for Hair?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A person&#39;s very own plasma extracted out from their blood has a tremendous effect on the hair growth, as Growth Factor therapy is superficially injected into the hair roots. It gives strength to the roots and boosts the growth of hair. It also improves the texture of hair by thickening every hair follicle.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How is Growth Factor therapy Beneficial for Skin?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The growth factors and proteins of plasma rejuvenate the skin deeply as well as superficially thus helps in reducing fine lines, hyperpigmentation spots, acne scar and it gives a refreshing natural healthy glowing skin with every session. It has a permanent anti-aging effect as it boosts collagen production in the skin. Collagen is the criss-cross structured protein fiber of the skin that tightens the skin, reduces open pores and makes the skin look younger and glowing. Male and female candidates of any age group can get this treatment done, as it&#39;s a natural therapy.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How it is prepared?</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>STEP 1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Collection of blood: 8-10 ml of blood is collected and is mixed with the anticoagulant solution in a specialized standard Growth Factor therapy tubes.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>STEP 2</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Separation of plasma: is carried out in a highly advanced centrifuge machine that revolves at a speed of 3600 rpm. The blood gets separated into cell and plasma.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>STEP 3</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Now we collect the plasma containing high growth factors and proteins into an sterile syringe. Within 20 min of preparation, Growth Factor therapy is superficially injected into the scalp or face.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How much time does it take for a complete session?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It takes around 45 min to 1 hour for a complete session of Growth Factor therapy.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Do i have to do any preparation before coming for growth factor therapy session?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>On the day of Growth Factor therapy make sure to wash and shampoo the hair.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How many sessions of growth factor therapy do I need?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Generally, a patient requires 6-8 sessions of Growth Factor therapy at monthly interval without any gap, if one is suffering from hair fall issues due to change in lifestyle, improper diet, stress, workload then these sessions are sufficient for you. If someone is at a very young age and due to the genetic history of baldness facing hair fall issue then maintenance sessions at 6 month or 1-2 year interval are recommended.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Is it a permanent solution?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If at an early stage of AGA i.e Androgenic alopecia one opts for Growth Factor therapy, then it will retain the hair and delay baldness for at least 10-15 years, and prevent the need of hair transplant surgery.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Is there any side effect of growth factor therapy ?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>It is the safest procedure because no chemicals are being used in Growth Factor therapy, a person&#39;s own blood is regenerating the cells of the body.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Is it a painful procedure?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Use of local anesthesia before Growth Factor therapy in form of local anesthetic cream, spray or L.A. block is applied on the scalp, thus numbing the area to be injected making it a comfortable process.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Use of microneedling in Growth Factor Therapy </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Dermaroller and dermapens are used for microneedling along with Growth Factor therapy as it increases the absorption of Growth Factor therapy deep into the scalp by 8 times and it also increases the blood circulation thus enhancing the effect of Growth Factor therapy by many folds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Find advanced skin & hair treatments with our trusted experts:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Dermatologist in Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Dermatologist in Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/87ca55f676627b8cfb6972b0169aaf91.jpg', 'Growth Factor Therapy', 'Growth Factor Therapy ', 'It\'s a highly beneficial treatment for hair as well as skin as it contains a highly concentrated amount of growth factors. Therefore, it has a long-lasting effect on hair and skin.', 'Growth Factor Therapy ', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/growth-factor-therapy/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Growth Factor Therapy\"]', 0, 1, '2019-10-03 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(420, 'what-is-ringworm', 'What Is Ringworm, And How Do You Get It?', 'Learn what ringworm really is, how this common fungal infection spreads, and the key signs to watch for. Discover causes, symptoms, and prevention tips to protect your skin from infection.', '<p>\"Ringworm\" is a very common name for various fungal infections that cause itching, redness, and inflammation. Ringworms are a common cause of skin irritation and itching. Several different types of fungi cause Ringworm. Fungi are simple, single-celled organisms that reproduce through spores. If you come in contact with fungi in your environment, your body can break it down and create antibodies to fight off the infection. Some people are more susceptible to Ringworm because their immune systems may not be able to fight the infection off effectively.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. The Cause of Ringworm</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are a couple of theories as to why Ringworm occurs, but most scientists agree that a fungal infection of the skin causes it. The fungus typically lives on people&#39;s feet, especially between toes, and the fungus lives in small, moist crevices near the body&#39;s surface. It is most common in people exposed to the outdoors and wearing sandals or socks on their feet.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ringworm is an infection of the skin caused by a fungus that can cause an outbreak on the scalp, eyebrows, or face. It is commonly called \"tinea,\" but dermatologists call it Ringworm because it creates a ring-like pattern of patches around the infected area. It typically takes weeks for people to notice the symptoms but can be treated quickly using topical medications, such as ketoconazole shampoo. It is most common among children.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Ringworm Prevention</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>You want to prevent any skin disease before they start. When you have a skin disease, you might be tempted to ignore it and hope it goes away. But it never goes away if you do nothing. So prevention is the way to go. You can use these tips to help you prevent any skin disease:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>The most important thing you can do to prevent skin disease is to keep your hands clean. It would be best if you washed your hands often.</li>\r\n <li>If you have a skin disease, you should also ensure that you get medical treatment as soon as possible.</li>\r\n <li>It will help your skin disease to heal faster.</li>\r\n <li>Wash Your Hands with Soap; many different types of soaps are available today. They all work equally well at washing your hands.</li>\r\n <li>You should use good quality soap and lather up your hands thoroughly.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>3. Ringworm Treatments</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Ringworm can be challenging to treat since it is a fungal infection. One of the most important first steps is identifying and treating Ringworm. It includes washing the skin thoroughly and using topical antifungal medications. If this fails to get rid of the Ringworm, consider using oral antifungal medications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>And a good doctor will begin when a patient presents with Ringworm. They will treat the infection with an antibiotic cream and keep treating it for up to two weeks. If any sign of infection spreads, the doctor will then apply some antifungal solution to the infected area. Most people don&#39;t have Ringworm anymore; it was once a common childhood ailment, but it&#39;s not nearly as common anymore. However, if your dog or cat does get Ringworm, it will need to be treated just like a human would.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In conclusion, Ringworm is a highly contagious fungal infection that causes inflammation and redness of the skin. The ringworm fungus lives on the surface of the body. To treat this infection, you must soak a towel in the prescribed medicine and apply it to the infected area for several days. Once you treat this infection, it takes about two weeks to disappear completely. However, if the person does not respond to the treatment, he will have to visit a dermatologist.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Please don&#39;t put off treatment until it has spread to other parts of your body. Get in touch with us for more details, and we&#39;ll be happy to help.<strong> </strong>consult a<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> <strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong></a><strong> </strong>or if you are from noida<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\">  dermatologist in noida</a></strong> then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.Visit <strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">https://www.skinfinityderma.com/</a> </strong>or call +91 98999 61629</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/33999fd2825eab178c7aec190b01e76f.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'What Is Ringworm, And How Do You Get It? ', 'Learn what ringworm really is, how this common fungal infection spreads, and the key signs to watch for. Discover causes, symptoms, and prevention tips to protect your skin from infection.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-07-15 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(421, 'are-you-Itching', 'Are You Itching All Over? You Might Have Scabies', ' Are you itching all over? Do you feel like you can\'t shake a cold? Do you scratch and burn at night and find little spots all over your body? Does everyone around you have a red, itchy rash? ', '<p>Are you itching all over? Do you feel like you can&#39;t shake a cold? Do you scratch and burn at night and find little spots all over your body? Does everyone around you have a red, itchy rash? If so, then you might have scabies. Scabies is a fungal infection that affects both children and adults, but it&#39;s especially common in babies and toddlers because it usually starts as a diaper rash. While there&#39;s no cure, you can get relief if you learn how to treat scabies effectively.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What is scabies?</h3>\r\n\r\n<h3>Most people know that they itch, but do you know why?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Scratching is one of the most common ways we humans try to relieve an itching sensation. But in fact, scratching can make the problem worse.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>During an average day, your <em>skin might see something nice like sandals</em> or rough shoes. But it can also come into contact with <em>things like straw</em> or cotton dust, dry cleaning chemicals, food additives, perfume, and dander.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All these things can be allergens, and when your body reacts to them, they cause a mild rash or hives. Chemicals put out by plants, such as pollen or mold spores, may even trigger a reaction from your scalp.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>But many don’t realize that scaly patches can happen for reasons other than allergies. Scratches can worsen the irritation, preventing any precise diagnosis, so avoid scratching unless you have a doctor-recommended treatment plan.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Also, although chafing between legs is usually caused by friction against pants seams or fabrics, it can be due to <em>several factors related</em> to exercise. Muscle soreness and fatigue (lower leg pain) have been known to affect athletic performance, and some studies suggest that <em>hot showers help reduce muscle aches</em>.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Who gets scabies?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Symptoms of <em>scabies usually include itching</em> with or <em>without skin sores</em>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The itch is caused by an infestation of mites and parasitic worms that burrow through your skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can get scabies from other people only if you touch their faces or hands. You can <em>also get scabs</em> at least once in your life if you go to work or visit friends who don’t know how to treat their symptoms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A doctor must diagnose scabies; however, there are some simple things you can do to look like you’re taking care of it. These include washing your body daily after touching someone else, <strong>using cleaning soap</strong> and water for hand washing, and not sharing utensils or food with someone who has just been treated for scabies.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How do you get scabies?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>An infestation of scabies bugs can be tough to eradicate. These parasites drive the symptoms – if not enough worms are produced, there is no itch. Once they have checked into your skin, <em>scabies mites begin</em> to burrow into your superficial layers, making treatment challenging.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>How it spreads</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are three ways scabies has been documented to spread; via touch, through air contact, and (less often) via personal items such as clothing or towels.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Prevention depends on treating all new things in your area and avoiding touch with others once you know you’re infected. Treatment for <strong>scabies includes applying a saline solution</strong> or <em>cream treatments daily</em> until the itch disappears. Sometimes antibiotics may be used alongside this for better effect.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What happens when you have scabies?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>When you have scabies, <em>tiny mites invade</em> your skin. They bite into your epidermis (the top layer of skin). Your body reacts by <strong>creating red bumps</strong>. Then, over time, these become sores or blisters.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>How do I know if I am infected with scabies?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Look for itchy rashes. A defining characteristic of scabies is an itch that runs through its entire length. The irritation comes and goes and can be triggered by any number of reasons.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Scratching leaves behind open wounds and doesn’t help reduce the severity of the rash. Scratching too much can damage the <strong>skin tissue causing scarring</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What can you do?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>People with <strong>scabies itch</strong> because of an infection in the skin called Peridermitus. The bacteria that cause the scab is not killing them; it’s feeding off their blood. Once the condition has been treated, your dermatologist will <em>prescribe one</em> or more medications to kill any remaining bacteria.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It <em>kills two birds</em> with one stone: Not only does this stop the scratching, but it also reduces the inflammation caused by the itching.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In conclusion, if you’re suffering from an itchy rash on your body, it might be scabies. Scabies is caused by mites living on the skin. Although the mites don’t cause harm, they irritate and spread through the skin. Scabies can appear anywhere on your body, especially on the hands and feet, between the fingers and toes, and around the scalp. If you’re itching all over, contact your doctor right away. The sooner you seek treatment, the better.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Apart from providing a wide range of options, Skinfinity carries out all treatments under the care and supervision of Dr. Ipsita Johri, the<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/best-dermatologist-in-delhi-ncr/\"> best dermatologist in Delhi NCR</a>,</strong> who keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root.  consult a<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> <strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong></a> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong> dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To find out more about Scabies or to schedule an appointment with a dermatologist near you, visit <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">https://www.skinfinityderma.com/</a> or call +91 98999 61629</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/51eb5a74b40b7710625ba0ee0fbceea6.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Are You Itching All Over? You Might Have Scabies', 'Are you itching all over? Do you feel like you can\'t shake a cold? ', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-07-10 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(422, 'what-is-seborrheic-dermatitis', 'Seborrheic Dermatitis: What is It and How Can You Treat It?', 'What is It and How Can You Treat It?', '<p>This skin condition is common in people over age 40, and it causes redness, scaling, thickened skin, itching, and bumps on the scalp, arms, legs, neck, back, and chest.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Many dermatologists say that seborrheic dermatitis is an age-related skin disease that begins with genetic predisposition, environmental triggers, and emotional stress. In other words, this condition has a lot to do with your lifestyle.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>History of Seborrheic Dermatitis</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Germany&#39;s first medical description of seborrheic dermatitis appeared in the early 1800s. In the mid-1800s, physicians coined the term \"seborrhea\" to describe the condition. In the early 1900s, it was named seborrheic dermatitis because it was observed on people with \"dandruff.\" Today, seborrheic dermatitis is often described as a condition caused by an overgrowth of the fungus Malassezia. However, there are still many unanswered questions about the exact cause of the state.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Seborrheic dermatitis is a condition that affects your scalp. This condition causes skin problems on your scalp. The cause of this condition is unknown. You may get this problem if you have dandruff. Many factors can cause dandruff. You might have an allergy to some products in your hair or skin. You may also have a yeast infection. Some people think that a virus causes this condition. However, scientists don&#39;t know what causes this condition. You may be allergic to a particular chemical found in your skin. People with this problem may have redness, scaling, and itching on the scalp.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Types of Seborrheic Dermatitis</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are several different types of seborrheic dermatitis. Sometimes they are caused by a fungal infection; at other times, they are caused by a bacterial infection. In the most severe cases of seborrheic dermatitis, a person cannot keep their skin clean. They may start with a rash and have sores all over their body.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are two types of seborrheic dermatitis: tinea versicolor and seborrhea eczema. Tinea versicolor is not contagious; it does not spread. It is only caused by yeast, so if you wash your hands after using the restroom, you will not get dermatitis. A person with this type of skin disease may not even have symptoms. Sometimes, a person might only have a spot on their forehead. In some cases, a person might get an itchy red rash.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Causes of Seborrheic Dermatitis</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>There are several possible causes of seborrheic dermatitis, including genetics, the quality of your diet, stress, skin care products, and more. The most common cause of seborrheic dermatitis is an allergy to a fungus, but there are many other causes. People with a weak immune system, particularly those older, tend to get more cases of seborrheic dermatitis.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One reason why you may have seborrheic dermatitis is because of your diet. Your diet consists of the foods you eat and the drinks you drink. You eat meat, cheese, milk, bread, cereal, fruits, vegetables, nuts, and oils. The beverages you drink include beer, wine, and milk. Certain foods can trigger allergic reactions to bacteria, fungi, pollen, or viruses found on the skin&#39;s surface. The fungi you&#39;re allergic to may be from your diet or environment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The most common cause of seborrheic dermatitis is an allergy to a fungus. The fungus may be airborne or spread through skin-to-skin contact. An allergy to the fungus makes your skin oily and itchy. The condition is more likely to occur in men than women. You can avoid the fungus by washing your hands often and wearing gloves. Also, keep your hands clean. Use antiseptic soap and moisturize your hands regularly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatments for Seborrheic Dermatitis</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dermatologists usually recommend topical treatments to help prevent or treat the condition. Several kinds of topical treatments include ointments, lotions, creams, shampoos, and soaps. All have specific ingredients. It&#39;s important to know what the active ingredient is in these products.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Topical treatments include ointments, lotions, creams, shampoos, and soaps. These products help to protect your skin and keep it clean. These products&#39; ingredients may help remove certain substances from your body. The active ingredient in topical treatments varies with different products. The active ingredients include ingredients like moisturizers, emollients, and sunscreens. You might also find elements that help to calm your skin. It&#39;s essential to use a safe amount of a product. Be careful about what you use. You might overuse the product and make your skin feel worse.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How to Deal With Seborrheic Dermatitis</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>One way of dealing with eczema is to avoid allergens. Make sure that you are eating a healthy diet. If you know that certain foods cause eczema, avoid those foods and include more fruits and vegetables in your diet. Eating healthy is one of the best ways to treat your eczema.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When trying to avoid a problem food, you may find that you can&#39;t eat it very often. You may even think that you don&#39;t like it anymore. That&#39;s ok, as long as you try to eat it in moderation and smaller portions. When you are flaring up, trying to cut out the problematic food for a while is essential. This can help you to avoid having a bigger problem. You may not be able to stop eating this food, but you can cut down on the amount you eat. When you have a flare-up, it is essential to drink plenty of water, so you don&#39;t feel dehydrated. You may have diarrhoea. This may be due to dehydration. Don&#39;t forget to stay hydrated. Eating right and staying hydrated are essential in keeping yourself healthy. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Seborrheic dermatitis is a condition that is caused by a fungus called Malassezia. This fungus is the one which causes dandruff. Dandruff and seborrheic dermatitis are both widespread conditions many people suffer from, so you must know how to treat them. To treat it properly, it is essential to differentiate between seborrheic dermatitis and other skin conditions such as psoriasis. The key to this is learning to recognize the symptoms and signs you experience. Once you can do this, it will allow you to start working on the proper treatment and avoid making costly mistakes. To learn how to treat seborrheic dermatitis, check out the article.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Why choose Skinfinity Derma </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Apart from providing a wide range of options, Skinfinity carries out all treatments under the care and supervision of Dr. Ipsita Johri, the<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/best-dermatologist-in-delhi-ncr/\"> <strong>best</strong> <strong>dermatologist in Delhi NCR</strong></a><strong>,</strong> who keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root.  consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong> dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To find out more about Seborrheic dermatitis or to schedule an appointment with a <a href=\"https://g.co/kgs/cEjhnsa\"><strong>dermatologist near you</strong></a>, visit <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">https://www.skinfinityderma.com/</a> or call +91 98999 61629</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin and hair experts await at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> are here:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/b0e98acc037f966b8437665b73afb25e.png', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'What is Seborrheic Dermatitis and What Are the Symptoms?', 'Get the best Seborrheic Dermatitis Treatment with the top natural remedies. Learn more about the symptoms and the causes.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-07-04 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(423, 'surprising-causes-of', 'SURPRISING CAUSES OF SKIN AGING', 'As we become older, our skin is exposed to a variety of factors, including the sun, severe weather, and unhealthy habits.', '<p>As we become older, our skin is exposed to a variety of factors, including the sun, severe weather, and unhealthy habits. We can, however, take precautions to keep our skin supple and youthful-looking.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Your skin&#39;s aging process is influenced by a number of variables, including your lifestyle, nutrition, heredity, and other personal habits. Smoking, for example, can cause free radicals, which are once-healthy oxygen molecules that have become hyperactive and unstable. Free radicals harm cells, causing premature wrinkles among other things.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are other factors as well. Normal aging, sun exposure (photoaging), pollution, and loss of subcutaneous support are all major contributors to wrinkled, spotty skin (fatty tissue between your skin and muscle). Stress, gravity, everyday face movement, obesity, and even sleep posture are all factors that contribute to skin aging.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What Kinds of Skin Changes Do You Get As You Get Older?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As we become older, we go through changes like these:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. The surface of the skin gets rougher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Skin lesions, such as benign tumors start to form.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. The skin gets saggy. The lack of elastic tissue (elastin) in the skin causes it to hang loosely as it ages.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. The skin appears to be more translucent. The epidermis is thinning, which causes this (surface layer of the skin).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5. The skin becomes more delicate. A flattening of the region where the epidermis and dermis (the layer of skin underneath the epidermis) meet causes this.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6. The skin becomes more prone to bruises. This is because the blood vessel walls are thinner.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>As we become older, we notice changes beneath the skin as well. They are as follows:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Fat loss beneath the skin in the cheekbones, temples, chin, nose, and eye region can cause a thinner appearance, looser skin, sunken eyes, and a \"skeleton\" aspect.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. After the age of 60, bone loss, particularly around the mouth and chin, can cause puckering of the skin around the mouth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. The loss of cartilage in the nose causes the nasal tip to drop and the bone structures in the nose to be highlighted.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Did you realize that your obsession with your smartphone, your urban lifestyle, and even your sweet indulgences may be contributing to your wrinkles and other signs of aging? Here are five unexpected causes of aging, as well as ways to avoid them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Sugar- </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>The Cause: </p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you consume too much sugar, you are more than likely to get wrinkles. What causes this to happen? When you consume sugar, it enters your circulation and attaches to a protein, resulting in Advanced Glycation End-products (AGEs). Collagen is damaged by AGEs, and the skin&#39;s integrity is weakened, resulting in drooping tissue and wrinkles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Solution:</p>\r\n\r\n<p> Refined sugar, which is present in most processed meals, is a no-no and should be taken in moderation, but high-glycemic fruits like strawberries, melons, bananas, and white breads and pastas should also be avoided. Instead, receive your daily nutrients from low-glycemic foods like apples, blueberries, cranberries, and whole grain breads and pastas. Enhance your skin care regimen by adding creams and serums that feature potent components like sophisticated stem cell technology and retinol to counteract the effects of sugar on collagen levels.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Smog- </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>The Cause: </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin aging is frequently caused by air pollution. Smog chemicals, in fact, produce reactive oxygen species and free radicals similar to those produced by sunshine (the usual aging culprit). These industrial particles impair your skin&#39;s shine and can cause dark spots and wrinkles when they settle in.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Solution:</p>\r\n\r\n<p> The first step in combating the wrinkling effects of pollution particles is to cleanse your skin as soon as you reach home. The second step is to use an antioxidant-rich skin lotion every morning to boost your skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Sleeping Position- </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>The cause: </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sleeping on your side or stomach with your face pressed against a cotton pillowcase puts more pressure on your skin. Collagen breakdown and wrinkles can occur as a result of this continual strain.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Solution:</p>\r\n\r\n<p> Use a night lotion every night (especially better if it contains retinol to boost collagen formation) and switch up your sleeping positions. Swap your cotton pillowcase with a silk or satin one if you can&#39;t adjust your sleeping habits.</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Tech neck- </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The Cause: </p>\r\n\r\n <p>The tech neck is on the rise, and it&#39;s not a good thing. Skin laxity and wrinkling at the neckline are a serious concern after gazing down at your laptop and smartphone all day, especially because the skin around the neck is thinner.</p>\r\n\r\n <p>The Solution: </p>\r\n\r\n <p>The best way to avoid tech neck is to avoid it in the first place. While surgical cosmetic enhancements and firming lotions are possibilities, the easiest strategy to protect the skin on your neck from sagging and wrinkling is to hold your smartphone or place your laptop at a higher level (so you&#39;re not continually gazing down).</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Stress- </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The Cause: </p>\r\n\r\n <p>Cortisol levels rise when you&#39;re stressed or nervous, and this is the cause of stress. This hormone induces inflammation and has a detrimental impact on the tissues that help the skin keep its suppleness and tightness over time.</p>\r\n\r\n <p>The Solution:</p>\r\n\r\n <p> Schedule time to unwind and relax. Schedule a regular yoga class, practice meditation, or simply conclude your day with a peaceful hour to read a book or sip herbal tea. Better still, incorporate a firming face mask into your relaxation practice to significantly reduce tension and wrinkles.</p>\r\n\r\n <p>If Everything Else Fails...</p>\r\n\r\n <p>Consider a non-surgical, radio frequency-based wrinkle reduction treatment to help reduce the look of fine lines and wrinkles. This treatment works by administering consistent heat beneath the skin&#39;s surface to increase collagen formation and elastin fibers. After only a few short, painless treatments with minimal downtime, the outcome is visibly smoother skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p> consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Book your visit at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, home to the best <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/a0ed5f1e4a97aea0049413e644aed551.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Surprising causes of skin aging', 'As we become older, our skin is exposed to a variety of factors, including the sun, severe weather, and unhealthy habits. We can, however, take precautions to keep our skin supple and youthful-looking.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-06-30 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(424, 'acne-treatments-for', 'ACNE TREATMENTS FOR ADULTS: WHAT WORKS BEST?', 'Have you ever looked in the mirror and said to yourself', '<p>Have you ever looked in the mirror and said to yourself, \"I don&#39;t think I should have wrinkles and pimples on the same face!\" If that&#39;s the case, you&#39;re not alone. Acne isn&#39;t simply a problem for youngsters. Adult acne affects many people well into their 30s, 40s, and even 50s.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re like most women, you assumed that after you got through adolescence, you&#39;d be rewarded with smooth, clean skin. So it&#39;s a great bummer when you&#39;re past braces and school dances but still have to deal with skin issues. If you&#39;re like most women, you assumed that after you got through adolescence, you&#39;d be rewarded with smooth, clean skin. So it&#39;s a great bummer when you&#39;re past braces and school dances but still have to deal with skin issues. If this describes you, you&#39;re not alone; acne isn&#39;t only an adolescent problem.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are so many different ways to cure acne breakouts that determining which is the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\">best acne treatment in noida</a>  for your skin can be difficult. Even if you&#39;ve had acne your whole life, the pimples we get as adults may be different from the acne we had as teenagers, and they may be more difficult to clear up, depending on factors such as hormones, changes in skin type and texture, and scarring.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Because life is difficult enough without always worrying about the status of our skin, SELF consulted with experts to find out which <strong>acne treatments </strong>work best for various types of pimples.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Continue reading to find out <strong>what causes acne</strong> in the first place, as well as the finest<strong> acne treatments </strong>and drugs worth your money. It&#39;s worth mentioning that speaking to a dermatologist is always your best choice, whether you&#39;re wanting to merely decrease some annoying blackheads or you&#39;re suffering with anything more serious like cystic or inflammatory acne. They&#39;ve been trained to recognize acne kinds just by looking at them, and they have access to many more treatment alternatives than your local drugstore.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Is adult acne the same as the acne that plagued us as teenagers?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Adult acne is quite similar to the acne we associate with our adolescent years. It may also happen to adults, and it&#39;s very frequent. When most people think of a pimple, they picture a raised, pink, inflammatory bump, but that&#39;s only one form. Pimples, blackheads, whiteheads, pustules, and more severe acne, such as nodulocystic acne, are all included in the word \"acne.\" </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What are the causes of acne?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne can be induced by hormonal fluctuations, especially in women. Our estrogen levels tend to drop as we get older. Male hormones such as testosterone and dihydrotestosterone, which we all have, rise at the same time. Because there are less female hormones in our body to block the effects of male hormones, the impacts of those hormones become more noticeable. You may notice an increase in oil production, as well as a thickening of the oil generated by your face. Your pores may appear to be bigger. This can result in blocked pores and an increase in acne.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Stress is also a factor. Certain hormones, such as cortisol, can be elevated by stress. This can cause additional irritation, which can aggravate acne and make it worse.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Adult acne is very different from the pimples you had as a teenager, both in appearance and treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hundreds or thousands of microscopic lumps, blackheads, or whiteheads on the skin of the face, especially the forehead, as well as cysts on the chest and back, are common among teenagers. That&#39;s because teen skin is a touch stickier than adult skin, and they&#39;re more prone to blocked pores than adults.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What is the most effective acne treatment?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Cleaning your face twice a day is good for eliminating old oil and makeup layers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To clear pores and exfoliate the skin, I frequently suggest a topical retinoid cream. Retinoids also have some anti-inflammatory properties and speed up the division of our skin cells. This aids in the rapid healing of the skin. Retinoids are included in several over-the-counter medications. Acne can also be treated with topical anti-inflammatories like dapsone gel. Spironolactone, an oral prescription drug, can help to lessen the effects of male hormones. If you want to clean up acne faster, chemical peels and blue light therapy can assist.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What qualities should you seek in a cleanser?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Avoid extremely harsh and forceful cleansers in general, especially if you&#39;re also taking a prescription topical component. A creamy cleanser may be a better choice for dry and sensitive skin. A mild, foamy cleanser may be preferable for oily skin. Salicylic acid, which searches out oil and unclogs pores, might be beneficial if someone has a lot of blackheads. Antibacterial properties of benzoyl peroxide can also aid in the removal of dead skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What changes can you make to your diet to help with acne?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Excess sweets, pastries, and drinks should be avoided.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In terms of healthy meals, leafy greens and a well-balanced diet rich in vitamin C and beta-carotene-rich fruits and vegetables can be beneficial because these nutrients have anti-inflammatory properties. In addition, several studies have linked the use of specific dairy products to the <strong>development of acne.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h2>When should you think about taking medication?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>If your acne has been bothering you for more than a few months, is creating scarring, and topical treatments haven&#39;t worked, it&#39;s time to explore a systemic therapy, such as an antibiotic.  consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.<br>\r\nTrust <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong> for expert dermatology care—find the <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<strong>Location:  </strong><a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/47eb30f9d96bc8c92e3a58f8a9262173.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Acne treatments for adults: what works best?', 'Have you ever looked in the mirror and said to yourself, ', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-06-23 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(425, 'are-you-considering', 'ARE YOU CONSIDERING SKIN WHITENING? HERE\'S WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW', 'Skin whitening is the process of reducing the pigment melanin in the skin to get a whiter complexion. Melanin is more abundant in people with dark complexions, and the amount of melanin affects the color of a person\'s skin.', '<p>What is Skin Whitening and How Does It Work?</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Skin whitening</strong> is the process of reducing the pigment melanin in the skin to get a whiter complexion. Melanin is more abundant in people with dark complexions, and the amount of melanin affects the color of a person&#39;s skin. Melanin is produced by cells known as melanocytes. The amount of melanin in a person&#39;s skin is determined by their genetic makeup. Exposure to the sun, the degree of skin injury, and chemical exposure all influence melanin formation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-lightening-and-spots/\"><strong>Skin whitening treatments</strong></a> are frequently used to treat issues such as freckles, age spots, scars, moles, acne, and birthmarks, as well as by those who want to have light skin, particularly those with a darker skin tone.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Bleaching creams, fading creams, chemical peels, and laser therapy are examples of whitening or lightening treatments used by people.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>These products act by interfering with the tyrosinase enzyme, which is necessary for melanin formation, and thereby lowering the quantity of melanin in the skin. Melanocyte cells, which produce melanin, are found at the very bottom of the epidermal layer of the skin. Overproduction of the melanin pigment can result in a variety of hyperpigmentation issues.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What is glutathione and how does it help in skin whitening?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Glutathione, an antioxidant found in human cells, is extremely beneficial to the human body. It works by scavenging free radicals, improving immunity, and aiding in bodily detoxification.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>By inhibiting the enzyme tyrosinase, it aids in the conversion of melanin to a light hue and the creation of melanin pigment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>How can I quickly whiten my skin?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The following are some quick techniques to whiten your skin:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Use freshly squeezed lemon juice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Applying a lightening cream to the skin</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. By putting on a face mask.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. Quit smoking</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5. Drink lots of water.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6. By following a healthy diet.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>How is the skin whitening procedure done?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The first step towards a skin whitening procedure would be to schedule an appointment with a dermatologist and tell him/her what kind of skin tone you have in mind. You may</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult with a plastic surgeon after consulting with your dermatologist. You may also show him the photo so that he understands exactly what you desire.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Following consultations with both a dermatologist and a plastic surgeon, you choose an option depending on your health, requirements, and financial situation: you may go for a skin bleaching therapy or something more expensive like surgery. Skin whitening operations are not only incredibly costly, but they are also quite painful, and you must be prepared for both.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After your procedure, you&#39;ll need to prepare for recovery time; laser treatments and chemical peels take a few weeks, while permanent skin whitening surgery takes longer. Following treatment, you must maintain your skin with the use of certain maintenance products. Sunscreen is essential for avoiding sunburns and reducing the risks of your skin becoming darker.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What is the mechanism of action of skin whitening products?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin whitening agents diminish the amount of melanin produced and the concentration of melanin in the skin. Melanin is a pigment found in the skin that provides it color as well as protecting it from the sun.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Is skin whitening a long-term solution?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes, skin whitening is permanent, but it may also be painful, harmful, and costly. As a result, extreme caution should be exercised before undergoing a permanent skin lightening procedure.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Who isn&#39;t a candidate for treatment?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>People with a history of heart problems, recurrent fevers or cold sores, or a proclivity for scarring should avoid chemical peels for skin whitening. Deep chemical peels are also not indicated for those with extremely dark skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What is the best drink for fair skin?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin that is healthy and fair is a sign of excellent health. It is essential to have a healthy diet in order to have excellent skin. Our skin is a reflection of our overall health, and it is entirely dependent on the foods we eat. This necessitates the consumption of fruits and vegetables. The following are three amazing beverages that may do wonders for our skin:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Beetroot and carrot juice</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Pomegranate with green apple juice</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Juices of papaya, lemon, and cucumber</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A well-balanced diet is essential for healthy health and skin. As a result, it&#39;s important to eat nutritiously on a regular basis. Fresh fruits and vegetables such as carrot, beetroot, lemon, cucumber, and others make up these essential elements.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Is it possible to whiten your skin using ice?</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ice is beneficial to the skin in a variety of ways. It can improve the appearance of the skin and lessen the likelihood of acne or pimples developing on the face. It reduces puffiness around our eyes and delays the effects of aging. If we massage ice cubes on our faces on a frequent basis and make it a daily facial routine, our faces will have a lovely peachy shine.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It can increase blood circulation on our faces, reducing indications of irritation if any are present. It can help to reduce facial fatigue and hence improve the health and appearance of our skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Home remedies are effective at treating common skin issues and improving skin texture. Ice is one of them, and it is the most popular cure for improving skin radiance by stimulating blood circulation across the face.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Does glycerine help to whiten the skin?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Glycerine is necessary for the skin&#39;s moisture retention. It&#39;s an important element in many skin cosmetics since it acts as a humectant, which keeps the skin hydrated and avoids dryness. Apart from these benefits, glycerine has antibacterial qualities that protect the skin against microbial infections and skin illnesses such as psoriasis and eczema. It aids in the correct healing of the skin in the event of a cut or damage, and so aids in skin restoration.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Every skin-conscious individual thinks about glycerine when it comes to maintaining good skin. Because it is a humectant, it maintains moisture in the skin and keeps it properly moisturized, which is essential for glowing skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What are the after-care instructions?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Following the skin whitening treatment, the affected area should be washed with chemical-free soaps and dabbed very gently. It is recommended that you use certain maintenance products, such as aloe vera gel or petroleum jelly, on a regular basis to provide a soothing and cooling effect. Because a layer of scabs and crusts may form on the treated region, it&#39;s best not to touch or pick it. To minimize swelling, take pain relievers. Because the skin at this time becomes particularly sensitive, wear sunscreen for at least six months to avoid discoloration or sunburn.  consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Clear skin is possible with <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—book with a <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/ddd2d7327f1fdd2f51b5bb8c33789427.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Are you considering skin whitening? Here\'s what you need to know', 'Skin whitening is the process of reducing the pigment melanin in the skin to get a whiter complexion.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-06-16 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(426, 'get-glowing-skin', 'GET GLOWING SKIN WITH THESE TIPS FROM TOP DERMATOLOGISTS', 'The dermatologist-recommended skin care methods below can help you avoid a slew of issues in the future and give you naturally glowing skin', '<p>The dermatologist-recommended skin care methods below can help you avoid a slew of issues in the future and give you naturally glowing skin. Dermatologists from all around the world swear by these beauty recommendations for bright skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>These doctor suggestions for beautiful skin, which range from applying sunscreen to properly cleaning your face every day, can help you avoid aging and skin damage.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>10 Dermatologist Tips for Glowing Skin- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>The following advice will show you how to acquire glowing skin according to a doctor. These are straightforward yet quite effective.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Put on your armour- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Your skin requires defense!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re fighting the sun&#39;s damaging rays and the harsh climate on a regular basis, a sunscreen is your best ally. Skin care advice from specialists throughout the world suggests that sunscreen, as a face and general skin care product, is a must-have in every home, and that using a sunscreen with an SPF of 30 or higher is essential. Why? A sunscreen, on the other hand, protects you from sunburn, skin cancer, pigmentation, premature aging, and other problems. Apply sunscreen to your face, neck, hands, and other sun-exposed areas.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. Cleansing is a must- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Get rid of the dirt!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you want everlasting bright skin and healthy looking skin, you must cleanse your face, no matter how sloshed you are after a party or how inviting the bed appears after a long day.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cleaning your face guarantees that all debris, oil, and makeup are eliminated, and your skin can breathe again, according to dermatologists. It keeps acne and other bacterial illnesses at bay. Use a soap-free cleaner if possible. Follow these steps to maintain your skin&#39;s natural radiance and bloom.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Don&#39;t forget to use a moisturizer- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Goodbye, dull skin!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This one point will appear in every article or book on <a href=\"https://g.co/kgs/cEjhnsa\"><strong>dermatologist skin care advice</strong></a>. Every dermatologist recommends using a moisturizer twice a day to seal in all of the natural oils and moisture that your skin need in today&#39;s climate. If you have oily skin, don&#39;t skip the moisturizer since your skin will manufacture even more oil to compensate.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4. Yoga saves the day- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Work up a sweat!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Exercise is important because it eliminates toxins from your body; but, too much high-intensity cardio will inhibit collagen formation, which can lead to sagging.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>According to some physicians, activities like Bala-asana, downward facing dog stance, and Sun salutations increase circulation, which results in glowing skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A simple beauty technique that can leave you with bright skin and good overall health!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5. Remain cool and manage your stress levels-</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Keep stress at bay!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>High levels of stress and anxiety have been shown in studies to degrade the quality of your skin. It has also been proven to increase hormones linked to skin diseases like psoriasis in excessive circumstances. Take time out during the day to study de-stressing skills and ward off stress. Those dark circles and wrinkles will go completely. Get a massage or spend time with your family, whichever you choose!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6. Stick to a skin-care routine before going to bed- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Upkeep is a virtue!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After cleansing and toning, pamper your skin with essential hydrating mists, serums, night creams, or any retinol cream or anti-aging products at night. Your skin goes into repair mode while you sleep, and providing it with an ingredient that boosts collagen production and skin cell turnover is preventative skin care at its best.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>7. Food is also vital-</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Keep an eye on what you consume!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Our folks had us eat those soaked almonds for breakfast all the time. If you didn&#39;t have a reason to eat them before, now you have! Its high content of essential fatty acids protects the skin against irritation, fine wrinkles, and sagginess. Other foods, such as salmon and tuna, are also good suppliers. Reduce your intake of sweets and sugary foods, as they deplete the collagen that keeps your skin firm. Follow these easy beauty methods for your face at home to see your skin reborn and glowing like never before.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>8. Don&#39;t smoke or consume alcohol- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>It&#39;s time to wear a no-smoking tag!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Smoking and drinking harm your health not just from the inside but also from the exterior. It accelerates the aging process and exacerbates skin disorders such as acne and psoriasis. You&#39;re much than likely to develop a persistent bag under your eyes, wrinkles, a lack of sleep, and dull skin. Why? Smoking, on the other hand, obstructs the blood flow that maintains skin tissue supple and healthy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>9. Get at least 8 hours of sleep-</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It&#39;s true that beauty sleep exists!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Getting adequate sleep is the most prevalent dermatological recommendation, and for good reason. After UV or sunshine exposure, lack of sleep is the second leading cause of wrinkles. This is perhaps one of the most crucial dermatologist advice since your body need time to</p>\r\n\r\n<p>heal and revitalize, which can only be achieved via adequate sleep. After supper, put your electronic gadgets away and do some light reading to prepare your mind and body for sleep.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>10. It is critical to stay hydrated all over- </p>\r\n\r\n<p>It&#39;s crucial to stay hydrated!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It will never be adequate to just use face skin care products as a topical treatment. Your skin need nourishment from the inside out just as much as it does from the exterior. So, in addition to drinking enough of water, apply face skin care products that are designed to profoundly feed your skin from the inside out. Hydrating sprays may be quite beneficial to your skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For skin that glows from the inside out!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dermatologists advise that you acquire and utilize products that are tailored to your skin&#39;s needs for a better appearance and feel. So, if you have oily skin, utilize oily skin products, and vice versa for other skin types and concerns like dry skin, acne prone skin, and so on. If required, see a dermatologist.  consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity Derma Clinic offers trusted skincare with the <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\nLocation :  <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/e0fc9facdf7245a29067c03fdf8343a4.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Get glowing skin with these tips from top dermatologists', 'The dermatologist-recommended skin care methods below can help you avoid a slew of issues in the future and give you naturally glowing skin. Dermatologists from all around the world swear by these beauty recommendations for bright skin.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-06-14 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(427, 'skin-reflects-your', 'Skin Reflects Your Overall Health - Take Care Of It!', 'Skin that is healthy is an indication of general well-being', '<p>Skin that is healthy is an indication of general well-being. When we notice anything wrong with our skin, we become more aware of it and look for ways to enhance its health. We all want to look our best, so it&#39;s only normal to be concerned about our skin&#39;s health. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Perhaps you saw something odd in the mirror when you woke up one morning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Because you look at your face every morning, it was tough to see the difference. You come upon an old photograph from college or perhaps five years ago. \"My skin used to be so smooth and firm!  Where did that droopy, additional skin behind my chin originate from?\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dealing with skin problems may be emotionally draining. When we have a large, red pimple on our nose or more dark patches and less firmness in our skin, we feel self-conscious. It is the first thing that people notice, and we can&#39;t disguise it in most cases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Keep these skin-healthy suggestions in mind for skin that glows with vitality.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Exfoliation Is Crucial -</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Many individuals, particularly males, overlook the need of exfoliation. While exfoliating may appear to be a girlie phrase only for women&#39;s magazines, we all have dead skin cells that need to be removed. You also don&#39;t need to use a specific exfoliator. While you&#39;re in the shower, gently massage your face in a circular manner. You may use a towel or sugar scrub to assist slough off dead cells on tougher regions like your elbows, feet, and knees.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Orange Juice in the Morning – </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Vitamin C-rich orange juice can help maintain your skin smooth and collagen-rich. But be cautious. Because orange juice is heavy in sugar, consume other foods high in vitamin C, such as berries and bell peppers.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Keep your hands out of your face-</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re always on your phone or resting your chin on your palm, you&#39;re certain to get dull skin and breakouts. To prevent bacteria and germs from accumulating, keep items away from your face as much as possible. If your employment requires you to chat on the phone all day, consider wearing headphones.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Keep an eye on your diet-</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>You are what you eat, therefore don&#39;t expect to have model-like skin by eating ice cream and junk food. To receive all the nutrients your skin need, eat a diet rich in fruits and vegetables. Include beta-carotene-rich fruits and vegetables in your diet, since they can help your skin heal itself and prevent premature aging.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Obtain Enough Rest- </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Your skin, like the rest of your body, need adequate sleep to restore itself. When you don&#39;t get enough sleep, your circulation suffers, which is why you may seem pale or washed out in the morning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>We all desire nice skin for cosmetic reasons, but healthy-looking skin also indicates that our insides are in good shape. If your skin is looking a little dull or unappealing, it&#39;s an indication that you need to make some changes to your health.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What your skin can tell you about your overall health? </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin, hair, and nail problems can be signs of a variety of problems, ranging from general weariness to Parkinson&#39;s disease.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Despite the fact that your skin is on the exterior of your body, it may provide a startlingly clear view into what&#39;s going on within. Looking at someone&#39;s skin might reveal a lot about them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The health of your skin, maybe most plainly, can reveal your lifestyle to a dermatologist&#39;s expert eye.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When a dermatologist examines someone, one of the first things they can assess is how much outdoor exposure they&#39;ve had based on the appearance of sun damage for their age. Wrinkles, blotches, uneven pigmentation, and elasticity loss can all be clearly identified.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>People&#39;s skin might also be a sign that they are sleep deprived. Fatigue might be indicated by droopy, sagging, dark circles beneath the eyes. Dermatologists can even identify if patients are staying hydrated by looking at their skin. Sunken-looking skin around the eyes is one of the indicators of dryness and the skin of smokers frequently reveals their habit. Smokers&#39; complexion is usually paler or sallow in tone, and they have wrinkles around their lips. Skin, in addition to disclosing lifestyle patterns, may also assist doctors in diagnosing a variety of ailments. Your board-certified dermatologist can help you figure out if the symptoms listed below are indicative of anything more serious.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ITCHY, DRY SKIN</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It&#39;s typical to have dry or itchy skin, especially in the winter. Short baths and showers, followed by moisturizing while your skin is still damp, may typically keep this problem at bay. These symptoms are more common and severe in those with chronic skin diseases such atopic dermatitis (eczema). However, some individuals itch as a result of an underlying condition, such as lymphoma, which can make the skin more prone to scratching. Itching can also be caused by opioids and other drugs. Thyroid problems can make your skin dry. Dermatologists have the training to determine when a blood test should be performed and when a patient should be evaluated more fully.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> IRRITATED HANDS</p>\r\n\r\n<p>During the coronavirus pandemic, constant hand washing and the use of alcohol-based hand sanitizers can take a toll on your hands. This widespread condition may generally be solved with moisturizing hand lotions or ointments. however, the issue isn&#39;t always that widespread. Dermatomyositis, a disorder that causes red spots on the backs of the hands and is caused by irritation or over washing, can seem like hand dermatitis. Dermatomyositis</p>\r\n\r\n<p>is an autoimmune illness that is related to lupus. When irritated-looking hands are truly something more, only a dermatologist can tell that. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>DANDRUFF</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Seborrhea is the medical term for ordinary scalp dandruff (and sometimes around the nose). Medicated shampoos or prescription medicines are typically effective. Even dandruff, though, might be a sign of underlying sickness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Severe seborrhea is more common in patients with neurological disorders such as Parkinson&#39;s disease or stroke. Seborrhea is also more common among HIV patients.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ACNE</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Breakouts are common throughout youth and can last far into adulthood. Acne flare-ups can also be exacerbated by using a face mask. However, new acne, or very severe acne that you haven&#39;t had previously, can sometimes be a sign of a hormonal imbalance, such as polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS) in women.  consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Get expert help at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> can assist:<br>\r\n<strong>Locations:</strong> <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/fad73983f664667f3e85444dd50dcfbb.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Skin Reflects Your Overall Health - Take Care Of It!', 'Skin that is healthy is an indication of general well-being.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-06-12 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(428, 'how-long-can-you-hide-baldness', 'HOW LONG CAN YOU HIDE BALDNESS?', 'Hair loss is a common concern among males, but it also affects women. The sight of a comb or brush coated with stray hair may be extremely stressful for anybody.', '<h1>How Long Can You Hide Baldness? Explore Your Options at Skinfinity</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Hair loss is a common concern among men, but it also affects women significantly. The sight of a comb or brush filled with stray hair can be extremely stressful. Experiencing hair loss at a young age often impacts confidence and self-esteem, making the question <strong>“how to stop hair loss”</strong> a constant worry.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Before starting any treatment, it’s crucial to identify the root cause of hair loss. Medical issues should always be addressed first.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Healthy hair not only improves your appearance but also uplifts your mood. On the other hand, thinning hair or bald spots can cause daily stress and tension.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Understanding Hair Loss</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>On average, humans shed <strong>50–100 strands of hair daily</strong>. Losing more than this may indicate hair loss.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Common Causes of Hair Loss</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Hot Water:</strong> Strips natural oils, leaving hair dry, brittle, and frizzy.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Chemical Hair Products:</strong> Harsh products damage follicles and disrupt oil balance, leading to thinning.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Improper Combing:</strong> Rough combing causes breakage, split ends, and weakens roots.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Home Remedies for Hair Loss</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Several natural remedies have been traditionally used to manage hair loss:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Mustard Oil & Henna Leaves:</strong> Boil together, filter, and massage regularly on bald spots.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Fenugreek Paste:</strong> Blend seeds with water, apply for 40 minutes daily for a month.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Cold Water Scalp Massage:</strong> Improves circulation and hair growth.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Onion & Honey:</strong> Rub onion juice on bald spots until red, then apply honey.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Egg Yolk & Honey:</strong> Apply mixture on scalp for 30 minutes before washing with mild shampoo.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Curd, Lemon & Gram Powder:</strong> Apply for 1 hour as a natural shampoo alternative.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Amla, Reetha & Shikakai:</strong> Boil in water and use as a herbal hair rinse.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Hair Loss Treatments for Men</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Men have multiple effective solutions to tackle baldness:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Medications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n <ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p><em>Finasteride</em> (tablet) and <em>Minoxidil</em> (lotion) reduce hair loss and promote regrowth.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n </ul>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Therapies</strong></p>\r\n\r\n <ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Combination of oral medicines, lotions, shampoos, and ointments, tailored to the patient’s condition.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n </ul>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Hair Transplant Surgery</strong></p>\r\n\r\n <ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Transplants DHT-resistant follicles from the back of the scalp to bald areas.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Provides permanent results for male pattern baldness.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n </ul>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Laser Combs</strong></p>\r\n\r\n <ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Emit focused light that stimulates hair follicles.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Works best when combined with other treatments.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n </ul>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h2>Hair Loss Treatments for Women</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Women also face hair thinning and baldness, with several treatment options available:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Minoxidil:</strong> Most common topical lotion for women; shows results within weeks.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Finasteride & Dutasteride:</strong> Sometimes prescribed in rare cases for women.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Spironolactone:</strong> Helps regulate excess fluid and hormonal imbalance contributing to hair loss.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>PRP Therapy (Platelet-Rich Plasma):</strong> Boosts hair regrowth by using patient’s own growth factors.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Laser Light Therapy for Hair Loss (Men & Women)</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Low-Level Laser Therapy (LLLT)</strong> stimulates hair follicles and prevents further hair loss.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Uses near-infrared radiation to activate follicles.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Encourages new growth and speeds up repair of damaged follicles.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Works for both men and women.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Can be combined with other medical or surgical treatments for enhanced results.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Baldness Treatment at Skinfinity Derma</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>At <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, we provide advanced and customized solutions for both men and women struggling with hair loss and baldness:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Medical treatments (Finasteride, Minoxidil, Spironolactone)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>PRP Therapy for natural hair regrowth</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Advanced <strong>hair transplant surgeries</strong> with natural-looking results</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Laser therapy</strong> and other innovative treatments</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Whether you’re looking for a <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or a <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>, Skinfinity Derma offers expert care with state-of-the-art technology.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<p>At Skinfinity Derma, we aim to provide our patients with the best hair loss treatment<br>\r\nin Noida. Our team of dermatologists and hair specialists address your hair loss<br>\r\nproblems and prepare a customized treatment plan for you. Our techniques are<br>\r\ntargeted towards catering the best hair growth treatment to our patients, keeping in<br>\r\nmind their individual preferences.  consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/3721f3648514c822151096b4f138b026.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Baldness & Hair Loss Treatment: Explore Options at Skinfinity in Noida & Gurgaon', 'osing hair? Discover natural remedies, medications, PRP, laser therapy & transplant solutions for baldness at Skinfinity Derma in Noida & Gurgaon.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-05-28 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(429, 'red-scaly-patches-on-your-skin', 'RED SCALY PATCHES ON YOUR SKIN?', 'Rashes, pimples, and blemishes are all common. It\'s difficult to find out what\'s wrong with your skin when you discover something on it. Many factors can produce rashes and they might seem similar.', '<h1>Parapsoriasis: Symptoms, Types, and Treatment</h1>\r\n\r\n<p>Rashes, pimples, and blemishes are common, but it’s often difficult to know what’s wrong with your skin when you discover something unusual. Many factors can cause rashes, and they might look similar. To make it more complicated, two patients with the same illness may show very different symptoms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One such uncommon skin condition is <strong>parapsoriasis</strong>—a group of disorders that resemble psoriasis but behave differently.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What is Parapsoriasis?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The word <em>parapsoriasis</em> refers to a set of rare cutaneous lymphoproliferative dermatoses that mostly affect middle-aged adults. Men account for two-thirds of the cases.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Because of its diverse presentation and lack of specific histological findings, parapsoriasis is often hard to define. Typically, it appears as <strong>red, scaly patches</strong> ranging from 1–5 cm. The condition is long-term and frequently resistant to therapy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To confirm diagnosis, doctors often recommend a <strong>skin biopsy</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Symptoms of Parapsoriasis</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Parapsoriasis usually presents as a <strong>spotty rash</strong>, similar to psoriasis.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Spots are typically <strong>pink or red</strong>, but may also appear <strong>brown or yellowish</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>They may be <strong>scaly, wrinkled, elevated, or rough</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Commonly form on the <strong>chest, stomach, and back</strong>, but may also occur on the <strong>arms and legs</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Usually <strong>round or oval</strong>, varying in size.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Doctors diagnose parapsoriasis by examining the <strong>appearance and location</strong> of plaques. A <strong>biopsy</strong> is often done to rule out other conditions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Types of Parapsoriasis</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>There are two main forms (with subtypes):</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. Small Plaque Parapsoriasis (SPP)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Lesions smaller than 5 cm, usually harmless.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Appear as <strong>pink to yellow-brown patches</strong> (2–5 cm), round or oval, with scaling.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Most commonly seen on the <strong>trunk, sides, and proximal extremities</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microscope findings: mild spongiosis, parakeratosis, and small lymphocyte infiltration.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>A variant called <strong>digitate dermatosis</strong> appears as elongated, atrophic patches resembling cigarette paper, aligned with skin cleavage lines.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Large Plaque Parapsoriasis (LPP)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Lesions are larger, irregular, and darker (red or brown).</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Often occur on <strong>non-sun-exposed areas</strong> like thighs, buttocks, lower trunk, breasts, and flexural surfaces.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Associated with <strong>epidermal atrophy</strong> and lymphocyte infiltration.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Some cases may progress to <strong>mycosis fungoides</strong>, a type of cutaneous T-cell lymphoma (skin cancer).</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Considered by some as a distinct illness, while others view it as an early stage of lymphoma.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Causes and Risk</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The exact cause of parapsoriasis is unknown. Research suggests:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>SPP and LPP</strong> may represent stages on a spectrum ranging from chronic dermatitis to cutaneous T-cell lymphoma.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>T-cell clonality is more common in LPP, but this doesn’t always increase the risk of malignancy.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Diagnosis</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>A conclusive diagnosis requires:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Clinical examination</strong> of lesions.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Punch biopsy</strong> (samples the full skin thickness).</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Multiple biopsies from different sites, sometimes repeated over time, especially in suspected LPP.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Treatment for Parapsoriasis</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Treatment depends on whether it is <strong>SPP or LPP</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Small Plaque Parapsoriasis (SPP)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Treated with <strong>topical corticosteroids</strong> (moderate to high potency) for 8–12 weeks.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>If response is poor, <strong>phototherapy</strong> (2–3 times weekly) may be added.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Patients are generally monitored <strong>once a year</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Large Plaque Parapsoriasis (LPP)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Treated with <strong>very high potency topical corticosteroids</strong> for around 12 weeks.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Phototherapy</strong> is commonly used in the initial stage for widespread lesions.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Patients require <strong>6-monthly follow-ups</strong> due to cancer risk.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Regular <strong>biopsies</strong> may be required to check progression into lymphoma.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>General Management</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Steroid creams</strong> or other prescriptions to reduce inflammation.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Light therapy</strong> or natural sunlight may help.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Moisturizers</strong> improve skin appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>SPP</strong> may resolve on its own but requires monitoring.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>LPP</strong> does not resolve naturally and needs regular testing.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Parapsoriasis Treatment at Skinfinity Derma</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>At <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, we provide specialized care for rare skin conditions like parapsoriasis. Our dermatologists offer:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Customized treatments for <strong>red scaly patches</strong>, <strong>non-itchy skin rashes</strong>, <strong>skin allergies</strong>, and <strong>red spots on the skin</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Advanced technology and experienced specialists for accurate diagnosis and long-term management.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Personalized follow-up schedules to ensure timely detection of any progression.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> <strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.Location :-  <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon link</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida link</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/b427d8e3bcd875cfa09cfe61599d6360.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'RED SCALY PATCHES ON YOUR SKIN', 'Rashes, pimples, and blemishes are all common. It\'s difficult to find out what\'s wrong with your skin when you discover something on it.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-05-22 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(430, 'vitiligo-treatment-noida-gurgaon', 'Vitiligo Treatment – Causes, Symptoms, and Best Options in India', 'Get expert vitiligo treatment in Noida & Gurgaon at Skinfinity Derma. Advanced phototherapy, medical & surgical options for white patches. Book your consultation today.', '<h1><strong>Vitiligo Treatment – Causes, Symptoms, and Best Options in India</strong></h1>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Vitiligo</strong> is a chronic skin condition in which certain areas of skin lose their natural pigment, resulting in white patches. This happens when <strong>melanocytes</strong>—the pigment-producing cells—are destroyed or stop functioning. Vitiligo can develop at any age, in any gender, and on any part of the body, including the face, hands, arms, scalp, and even inside the mouth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>While the condition is <strong>not contagious or life-threatening</strong>, it can have a significant <strong>emotional and social impact</strong>, especially because of its visible nature.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Understanding Vitiligo</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Around <strong>1\% of the global population</strong> is affected by vitiligo. The patches may spread slowly or progress rapidly, and in some cases, they remain stable for years.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Vitiligo is often linked to <strong>autoimmune activity</strong>, where the immune system mistakenly attacks healthy melanocytes. Other contributing factors include <strong>oxidative stress, genetic predisposition, and environmental triggers</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Types of Vitiligo</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <pre>\r\n<strong>Non-Segmental Vitiligo (NSV)</strong></pre>\r\n\r\n <ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <pre>\r\nThe most common form.</pre>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>White patches appear symmetrically on both sides of the body.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Commonly affects face, hands, knees, and elbows.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n </ul>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <pre>\r\n<strong>Segmental Vitiligo</strong></pre>\r\n\r\n <ul>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <pre>\r\nPatches appear on one side or a specific area of the body.</pre>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>Progression usually slows after 1–2 years.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n  <li>\r\n  <p>More common in younger individuals.</p>\r\n  </li>\r\n </ul>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Causes and Risk Factors</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The <strong>exact cause</strong> of vitiligo is still unknown, but researchers believe it is linked to:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Autoimmune response</strong> – immune system attacks pigment cells.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Genetics</strong> – certain gene variations increase risk.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Oxidative stress</strong> – imbalance of antioxidants and free radicals damages melanocytes.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Environmental triggers</strong> – sunburn, skin injury, or exposure to chemicals.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Emotional stress</strong> – may worsen the progression.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>While vitiligo can occur in anyone, <strong>people with darker skin tones</strong> may notice it more prominently.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Associated Conditions</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Vitiligo patients are generally healthy, but there may be a higher risk of:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Thyroid disorders</strong> (hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Other autoimmune diseases</strong> like type 1 diabetes, alopecia areata, or lupus</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Is There a Cure for Vitiligo?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Currently, <strong>there is no permanent cure</strong> for vitiligo. However, <strong>treatments can help restore pigment or even skin tone</strong>, improving appearance and self-confidence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The right treatment depends on:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Age of the patient</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Extent and location of patches</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Speed of progression</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Impact on daily life</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Vitiligo Treatment Options</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n<strong>1. Camouflage Therapy</strong></pre>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <pre>\r\n<strong>Sunscreen</strong> (SPF 30+ with UVA & UVB protection) helps prevent tanning and reduces contrast between normal and affected skin.</pre>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Cosmetic camouflage</strong> – makeup and self-tanners to blend skin tone.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Hair dyes</strong> – if vitiligo affects hair.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Depigmentation therapy</strong> – for widespread vitiligo, <strong>monobenzone</strong> can lighten remaining pigmented skin to match white patches.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n<strong>2. Medical Treatments</strong></pre>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Topical corticosteroids</strong> – help restore pigment, especially in early stages.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Topical calcineurin inhibitors</strong> (tacrolimus, pimecrolimus) – effective on face and sensitive areas.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Vitamin D analogues</strong> – support melanocyte function.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n<strong>3. Light Therapy (Phototherapy)</strong></pre>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Narrowband UVB phototherapy</strong> – most effective for widespread vitiligo; usually given 2–3 times per week.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Can be combined with topical treatments for better results.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Older <strong>PUVA therapy</strong> (psoralen + UVA light) is less common due to side effects.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<pre>\r\n<strong>4. Surgical Options</strong></pre>\r\n\r\n<p>If medical therapy fails and vitiligo is stable for at least 6–12 months:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Skin grafting</strong> – transferring healthy pigmented skin to affected areas.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Blister grafting</strong> – using blistered skin layers for transplantation.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Cell transplantation</strong> – transplanting melanocytes from normal skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Emerging & Future Treatments</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Research is ongoing, and new therapies are showing promise:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Afamelanotide</strong> – an injectable implant that stimulates melanocyte production.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Prostaglandin E2 gel</strong> – being tested for localized vitiligo.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Janus kinase (JAK) inhibitors</strong> – oral and topical forms under clinical trials.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Living with Vitiligo – Self-Care & Coping Tips</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Protect skin from sunburn – <strong>always use sunscreen</strong>.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Avoid skin trauma or injury, which can trigger new patches.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Manage stress through meditation, yoga, or counseling.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Join support groups to connect with others living with vitiligo.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Vitiligo Treatment in Noida & Gurgaon</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>At <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong></a>, our team of expert dermatologists offers <strong>personalized <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/vitiligo/\">vitiligo treatment in noida</a> </strong>combining the latest medical technology and compassionate care.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Whether you need <strong>phototherapy, medical creams, or advanced surgical options</strong>, we ensure treatment is safe, effective, and tailored to your skin type.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Why choose Skinfinity Derma for vitiligo treatment?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Experienced dermatologists with proven results</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Advanced phototherapy units & surgical facilities</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Holistic approach – medical + emotional support</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Customized treatment for all skin tones</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Visit us in Noida or consult our <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\">dermatologist in Gurgaon</a></strong> to discuss the best treatment for your condition.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Quick FAQ on Vitiligo</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q. Is vitiligo contagious?</strong><br>\r\nNo, vitiligo is not contagious. It is an autoimmune condition.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q. Can diet help with vitiligo?</strong><br>\r\nWhile no specific diet cures vitiligo, a healthy, antioxidant-rich diet supports skin health.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q. How long does treatment take?</strong><br>\r\nRepigmentation may take several months to years, depending on the treatment and severity.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Final Word</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Vitiligo may not have a cure yet, but with <strong>early diagnosis, the right treatment plan, and proper skincare</strong>, it is possible to manage symptoms effectively and restore skin confidence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>At <strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong>, we are committed to offering the<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/vitiligo/\"> <strong>best vitiligo treatment in Noida and Gurgaon</strong></a>, ensuring both medical success and emotional well-being.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Personalized skin treatments at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—visit our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/c87b59da90441859b1e3413b57367b83.jpg', 'Vitiligo Treatment', 'Vitiligo Treatment in Noida & Gurgaon | Best Dermatologist for White Patches', 'Vitiligo Treatment', 'Vitiligo Treatment', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Vitiligo Treatment\"]', 0, 1, '2022-05-12 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(431, 'facial-sculpting', 'Facial Sculpting\'s Development', 'Facial Sculpting\'s Development The history of cosmetic surgery and the progress of facial sculpting go hand in hand with the evolution and history of medicine.', '<p>The history of cosmetic surgery and facial sculpting goes hand in hand with the evolution of medicine and beauty standards. For both men and women, physical appearance has always been the most visible part of identity. Since ancient times, people have sought ways to enhance their looks to improve confidence, self-perception, and overall quality of life.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Beauty Through History</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Evidence shows that more than <strong>5,000 years ago, Egyptians</strong> used natural remedies such as oils, salt, alabaster, and sour milk to improve skin appearance. Over time, beauty ideals have shifted, but one truth has remained constant: symmetry and proportion play a vital role in perceived attractiveness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What was considered a beautiful physique in earlier centuries differs greatly from today, yet the pursuit of balance and harmony in appearance has always been universal.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>The Golden Ratio and Facial Sculpting</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Studies have revealed that <strong>symmetry, harmony, and proportion</strong> are timeless aspects of beauty. The “Golden Ratio of Beauty” (1.62), also called Phi, is a mathematical principle of symmetry used to measure attractiveness.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Leonardo da Vinci</strong> was the first to apply this equation in anatomy, showing that faces closer to this ratio are perceived as more beautiful.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The same ratio appears in nature—in sunflowers, seashells, pinecones, and even art and architecture—making it a universal standard of harmony.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Today, aesthetic treatments allow individuals to get closer to the Golden Ratio, enhancing natural features while maintaining balance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What is Facial Sculpting?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Facial sculpting</strong> includes both <strong>surgical</strong> and <strong>non-surgical cosmetic procedures</strong> designed to reshape and enhance facial features.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Surgical methods</strong> (like facelifts, liposuction, implants) are more invasive, require anesthesia, and involve longer recovery.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Non-surgical treatments</strong> (dermal fillers, botulinum toxin, thread lifts, chemical peels) are minimally invasive, safer, quicker, and cost-effective.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>This shift towards <strong>non-invasive procedures</strong> has made facial sculpting widely popular, as they deliver natural results with minimal downtime.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Popular Non-Surgical Facial Sculpting Treatments</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are some of the most effective treatments for achieving balance and symmetry:</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. Cheek Sculpting (Cheek Fillers)</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Enhances cheekbone prominence, smoothens folds, and lifts the face for a youthful, defined look.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Chin Sculpting</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Ideal for those with a weak or small chin. Fillers balance the profile and enhance overall facial harmony.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>3. Brow Lifting</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Low brows can make eyes look heavy. Non-surgical brow lifting highlights the eyes and creates a youthful appearance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>4. Non-Surgical Rhinoplasty</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Reshapes the nose with dermal fillers, improving proportions without invasive surgery. Often combined with chin sculpting for better balance.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Evolution of Facial Sculpting</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Earlier, facial contouring was only possible through surgery. Today, thanks to advanced techniques and changing cultural attitudes, <strong>minimally invasive treatments</strong> dominate.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The modern goal is not drastic change, but <strong>enhancing natural features</strong> while maintaining symmetry, harmony, and proportion. This is why facial sculpting continues to grow in popularity worldwide.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Advanced Techniques in Facial Sculpting</h2>\r\n\r\n<h3>Laser-Assisted Facial Contouring (AccuLift)</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Uses energy to melt fat, which is then removed or absorbed naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Tightens skin while reshaping facial contours.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Minimally invasive, requiring only local anesthesia.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>What to Expect from AccuLift</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Can be combined with fillers, CO2 laser resurfacing, or facelift surgery.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Minimal downtime with only slight swelling or bruising.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Natural-looking enhancement with long-lasting results.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Why Choose Facial Sculpting?</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Restores youthful balance and proportion</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Enhances natural features without altering identity</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Boosts confidence and self-esteem</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Offers both quick results (fillers, botox) and long-term improvement (laser, sculpting)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Facial Sculpting in Noida & Gurgaon – Skinfinity Derma</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are searching for <strong>facial sculpting treatment in Noida</strong> or looking for an experienced <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong>, <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong> offers customized solutions including:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Dermal fillers</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Anti-ageing treatments</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Non-surgical rhinoplasty</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Facial sculpting & facelift procedures</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Our team ensures natural results while following the highest medical standards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Book your consultation today with a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong></a> or <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong></a> at <strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong> to begin your journey toward balanced, youthful, and confident beauty.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Advanced skincare is available now at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—visit our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<strong>Location : </strong><a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/37a0c58906e9a11542ffb41accffb49b.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'Facial Sculpting\'s Development', 'The history of cosmetic surgery and the progress of facial sculpting go hand in hand with the evolution and history of medicine.', NULL, NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-05-05 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(432, 'advanced-hair-loss-solutions-for-men', 'Don\'t look 37 when you are 27 - Advanced Hair Loss Solutions for Men', 'The hair cycle is a natural process that happens to all of us. Don\'t look 37 when you are 27. Read this blog to know about advanced hair loss solutions for men.', '<p>The hair cycle is a natural process that happens to all of us. It&#39;s a never-ending process where the hair falls out, grows back, and then falls out again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The hair follicle goes through three phases:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>The Anagen Phase: This is the growth phase, which lasts for two to six years.</li>\r\n <li>The Catagen Phase: This phase lasts for two to three weeks and it&#39;s when the hair follicle shrinks and stops producing new cells, but it doesn&#39;t completely die off just yet.</li>\r\n <li>The Telogen Phase: This is the resting phase, which can last anywhere from one to four months before the hair falls out and a new one starts growing in its place.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>People who are suffering from excessive shedding are often going through hormonal complications and age-related issues. Hair Shedding can also be the result of any other illness in your body.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Now, First, let&#39;s talk about ways to prevent hair loss:</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li><strong>Diet is important.</strong> Good nutrition is critical for optimal health, and healthy hair is no exception. If you&#39;re losing your hair or starting to go bald, start by looking at your diet. Did you know that male pattern baldness can be triggered by stress? It&#39;s true! Not only that but hair loss can also be triggered by nutrient deficiencies (like insufficient vitamin D) as well as some medications (like birth control pills). Of course, medical conditions like alopecia areata and lichen planus can also cause baldness.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Say no to bleaches and Color:</strong> Bleaches and other chemicals in hair products split up the protein called keratin which can trigger hair fall.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Use a mild shampoo.</strong> Sometimes using a harsh shampoo with lots of complex ingredients can irritate the hair follicle preventing new hair growth. So use a shampoo that comes with mild ingredients.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have tried everything to prevent hair loss but nothing seems to work, then it might be time to consider other solutions—like a wig!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Hair Transplantation</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-transplant/\">Hair transplantation</a> is a procedure that involves the taking of hair follicles from one area of the body, called the “donor site,” and placing them on another part of the body, called the “recipient site.” It is most often used to treat male pattern baldness. This method of hair restoration has become very popular in recent years because it offers permanent results and natural-looking hair. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Growth Factor Therapy for Hair</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Growth factor therapy for hair is a treatment that uses platelet-rich plasma (PRP) taken from your blood to stimulate hair growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Platelets are the cells in your body that contain growth factors, which trigger certain processes like cell regeneration. PRP is produced by collecting a patient’s blood, separating the platelets, and then re-injecting that concentrated liquid into the scalp.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Growth factor therapy for hair has been shown to increase hair count and thickness with minimal side effects. The procedure becomes less effective over time, meaning it must be repeated periodically to maintain results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Though there may be some discomfort during or after the treatment, this process should not interfere with daily life and patients can resume normal activities immediately afterward.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Mesotherapy</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Mesotherapy is a therapeutic technique that involves injecting substances into the skin. The injection of irritants, such as various plant extracts, vitamins, minerals, and other substances, are used to stimulate healing and improve the appearance of skin and hair.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The therapy is based on the concept that injecting substances into the skin will have a curative effect on deeper tissues or organs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Mesotherapy for hair loss is a new treatment for hair growth that has been gaining popularity in recent years. The therapy involves injections of natural plant extracts and vitamins into scalp tissue to stimulate hair growth with minimal side effects.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Scalp Microneedling</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Microneedles devices are covered with hundreds of tiny needles which penetrate through the top layer of the skin, stimulating hair follicles and improving and better blood circulation to the scalp. This results in new hair growth and collagen synthesis. The depth of microneedling depends on the type and condition of the hair scalp.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Well, you don&#39;t have to worry about your thinning hair as there are many treatment options available that regenerate hair growth. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>A dermatologist can suggest to you the best <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-loss-treatment-noidasg_popup_id2/\"><strong>hair loss treatment in Noida</strong></a> which will best suit your hair type and provide you with the most effective results. Get your dense hair back and stop worrying about thinning hair. consult a<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> <strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong></a><strong> </strong>or if you are from noida <strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"> dermatologist in noida </a></strong>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>At <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, say goodbye to skin worries with our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/d04a92ff3cf44a20419ca1fb14ac2d4a.jpg', 'Advanced Hair Loss Solutions for Men', 'Don\'t look 37 when you are 27 | Advanced Hair Loss Solutions for Men | Skinfinity', 'The hair cycle is a natural process that happens to all of us. Don\'t look 37 when you are 27. Read this blog to know about advanced hair loss solutions for men.', 'Advanced Hair Loss Solutions for Men, hair loss treatment in Noida', 'advanced-hair-loss-solutions-for-men', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Advanced Hair Loss Solutions for Men\",\"hair loss treatment in Noida\"]', 0, 1, '2022-04-27 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(433, 'dont-give-acne-a-chance-to-leave-permanent-mark-on-your-face', 'Keep Your Skin Mark-Free from Acne | Skinfinity Derma ', 'Acne almost hits everyone, but what is harder to deal with are the scars it leaves behind. Read this blog to know about acne problems and solution.', '<p>Don&#39;t let acne scar affect your confidence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne almost hits everyone, but what is harder to deal with are the scars it leaves behind.<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"> Acne scars treatmnet</a>  are rigid to let go, and as the skin ages, the scars become more visible as the skin loses collagen.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What is Acne Scar and why do they occur?</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The skin is the largest organ and is made up of many glands. Acne mostly occurs on the part of the skin where sebaceous glands are present in large numbers. Sebaceous glands are oil-producing glands that are mostly present in facial tissues, back, and neck. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne Scars occur when the acne blemishes get inflamed by irritants and as a result, the acne pore swells and due to the damage to the dermal tissues leads to scars.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Why can&#39;t scars heal on their own?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The scars can take two forms either they occur beneath the skin surface, known as depressed scars or it develops on the surface of the skin. Some Scars heal quickly while some spread to other tissues as well. That is why some kinds of scars can only get healed with proper<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong> treatment of acne  </strong></a>and care.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>How can you get rid of Acne Scars?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Now, numerous <strong>treatments guarantee to remove scars</strong> but it depends on the type of scars and the nature of your skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>1) Home Skin Care:</strong> First comes the home skincare. Having a good skin routine can also prevent acne and acne scars. Sunscreens can help and create a layer between the pores and the irritants. One can also use over-the-counter medicated creams containing hydroxyl acids or azelaic acid. If the problem does not heal or you face any irritation on the skin, consult your dermatologist.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>2) Laser Treatment:</strong> <strong>Laser Treatment</strong> is the most emerging and likable treatment option to get rid of acne scars. A laser can treat mild and moderate acne scars. The laser removes the first layer of the skin around the scars and tightens the middle layer of the skin. This results in smoother skin. This is done by a dermatologist and it is a non-invasive procedure. The procedure take usually between half an hour to two hours depending on your skin type and the depth of the scars.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The doctor applies a numbing cream before the procedure to have a smooth and painless experience. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Many people think laser treatment can have serious consequences for the skin; however, the technology being used nowadays offers a smooth and painless experience without any side effects. No matter what your skin type or whether you have darker skin, the l<strong>aser treatment works effectively to treat acne scars.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>3) Chemical Peel:</strong> Chemical peels work by removing the top layer of the skin and allowing new skin to appear. It is done by applying a chemical mask on the skin and then removing the top layer of the skin. This procedure lightens the scar. A chemical peel works best for raised scars rather than depressed scars. <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\">Chemical peels</a> smoothen the texture and the tone, it lightens the dark spots and unclogs the pores.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>4) Microdermabrasion:</strong> In this process, the dead cells are removed from the skin, and the top layer is removed from a handheld rolling device. The scars may be completely removed or appear less visible. This process should be done by a certified and experienced dermatologist as the wrong procedure can lead to redness, itching, and other problems with the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>5) Subcision and threads:</strong> Subcision is a procedure that releases scars that have become stuck to the deeper tissues and bound down. When a scar forms, new collagen is produced. Subcision helps to improve any condition in which the skin is being pulled downwards by scar tissue.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne Scars are difficult to eradicate. Some scars heal on their own while some are permanent. There are numerous treatment options to choose from that can completely eradicate acne scars. A dermatologist can help you with the right kind of <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong>acne scar treatment in Noida</strong></a> according to your skin type and get scar-free skin. consult a<strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> dermatologist in gurgaon</a></strong> or if you are from noida<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong> dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Related Skin & Aesthetic Services We Offer</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/dark-circles-treatment\"><strong>Dark Circles Treatment</strong></a> – Reduce under-eye pigmentation, puffiness, and tired appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/hydrafacial-treatment-in-noida\"><strong>HydraFacial</strong></a> – Deep cleansing and hydration without harsh exfoliation.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/chemical-peel-treatment\"><strong>Chemical Peel</strong></a> – Brighten and rejuvenate your skin with mild, sensitive-skin-friendly formulas.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/dermal-fillers-treatment\"><strong>Dermal Fillers</strong></a> – Restore volume and enhance facial features naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/botox-treatment\"><strong>Botox</strong></a> – Smooth fine lines and wrinkles for a refreshed look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/skin-pigmentation-treatment\"><strong>Pigmentation Treatment</strong></a> – Even skin tone and reduce dark spots.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/acne-pimple-treatment\"><strong>Acne & Pimple Treatment</strong></a> – Calm breakouts and prevent future flare-ups.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/melasma-treatment\"><strong>Melasma Treatment</strong></a> – Target stubborn pigmentation with advanced dermatology solutions.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/freckles-treatment\"><strong>Freckles Treatment</strong></a> – Fade freckles and achieve a clearer complexion.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://skinfinityderma.in/prp-treatment-for-skin-rejuvenation\"><strong>PRP Skin Rejuvenation</strong></a> – Use your body’s own growth factors to boost skin repair.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> All treatments are dermatologist-approved and tailored to sensitive skin needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin and hair experts await at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> are here:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/a30c253ad03ce842617bbc93e46c5a58.jpg', 'acne scar treatment in Noida', 'Don\'t give Acne a chance to Leave Permanent Mark on your Face | Skinfinity', 'Acne almost hits everyone, but what is harder to deal with are the scars it leaves behind. Read this blog to know about acne problems and solution.', 'acne scar treatment in Noida, acne problems and solutions', 'dont-give-acne-a-chance-to-leave-permanent-mark-on-your-face', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"acne scar treatment in Noida\",\"acne problems and solutions\"]', 0, 1, '2022-04-19 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(434, 'feel-free-yourself-from-shaving-and-waxing', 'Laser Hair Removal: Break Free from Shaving and Waxing Forever', 'Say goodbye to razors and painful waxing. Discover how laser hair removal offers smooth, long-lasting results at Skinfinity Derma.', '<p>Do you feel stressed out every time you see your hair? Do you wish that you had hairless skin? Do you have a lot of hair on your legs and underarms? Are you often embarrassed by your hair? If you answered “yes” to any of the questions above, you might want to consider getting laser hair removal to get rid of your hair and feel more confident about your appearance. Here are a few points that will convince you why laser hair removal is the best way to get rid of body hair.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>It works on all skin types</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Laser hair removal is safe and effective for nearly all skin types, including sensitive and acne-prone skin. In fact, the majority of people who have this procedure done have excellent results and don’t have to go back for any touch ups in the future. Many dermatologists recommend this for people who are more concerned about their appearance than about their specific skin type. It’s also a great option for people who have sensitive skin as waxing can irritate the skin but laser hair removal removes hair without irritating the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>No pain</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Since laser hair removal is performed with high-intensity light, it doesn’t generate any heat or burning sensation. In fact, many people who have the procedure done for the first time report feeling nothing at all. This can be a huge benefit for those who don’t like to be invasive with their skin or who are sensitive to pain. You can also get other laser hair removal treatments that create a feeling of cold, heat, or tingling, so there’s really no reason to avoid it just because it doesn’t hurt.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>It’s a long-term solution</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>While there are some treatments that can be used a limited number of times, laser hair removal is a long-term solution. You won’t need to keep going back to the doctor or salon to get treatments every few weeks or months. You can maintain your hair-free skin indefinitely with maintenance regimens and aftercare products. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>It’s affordable</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A lot of people get laser hair removal as a preventative measure for when they are older. This is especially true for women who are in their 40s and 50s since these are the years when hair tends to grow the most. This procedure is an affordable skincare solution for those who want to maintain their hair-free look as they age. It’s also a good option for people who are on a tight budget. The waxing cycle has to be done every month whereas laser hair removal is a long-term solution thus being very cost-effective.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Considering Full Body Laser Hair Removal?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re constantly juggling hair removal routines for different parts of your body—legs, arms, underarms, back, chest, or bikini area—<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/full-body-laser-hair-removal/\"><strong>full body laser hair removal</strong></a> might be your best solution. It’s not only convenient but also <strong>cost-effective</strong> in the long run.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>By treating all areas in one go, you save time, reduce the number of sessions, and enjoy <strong>smoother, more even-toned skin</strong> with minimal maintenance. Plus, the results are long-lasting, with many clients noticing a significant reduction in hair growth after just a few sessions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>At <strong>Skinfinity Derma</strong>, we use FDA-approved technology suited for all skin types, ensuring safety, comfort, and visible results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Want to know how much full body laser hair removal costs in Delhi?<br>\r\nWe&#39;ve created a complete guide that breaks down pricing, packages, and what to expect.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Read Now: <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/full-body-laser-hair-removal/\">Full Body Laser Hair Removal Cost in Delhi</a> (Noida)</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>It’s permanent</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Hair removal methods that simply fade or temporarily reduce hair growth all the time are ephemeral. They require constant maintenance, and the results are always temporary. Laser hair removal, on the other hand, is a permanent solution. Once the treatment is complete, you’ll never need to worry about having hair on your legs or arms again. This is a huge relief for many people who feel self-conscious or anxious about having hair.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Conclusion</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Laser hair removal is a fast, efficient, and painless way to get rid of unwanted hair. It’s also a long-term solution to hair removal, so you won’t need to repeatedly visit the doctor or spa for maintenance treatments. The procedure is also affordable, and relatively safe. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>However, one should only get this treatment from a dermatologist as they will curate the treatment of <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-removal-noida/\"><strong>laser hair removal in Gurgaon</strong></a> according to your skin type. Also, it is important to follow aftercare treatment after the procedure to avoid the side effects. Laser hair removal treatment is safe, effective, and works on all skin types. consult a<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"> <strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong></a> or if you are from noida<strong> </strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong> dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Book your visit at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, home to the best <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/5a2fa2ecbb82e22aac7c5fa33658b6eb.jpg', 'Laser Hair Removal In Gurgaon', 'Laser Hair Removal - Feel free yourself from Shaving & Waxing | Skinfinity Clinic', 'Do you feel stressed out every time you see your hair? Do you wish that you had hairless skin? Read this blog to know about laser hair removal and feel free yourself from shaving & waxing.', 'Laser Hair Removal In Gurgaon, Laser Hair Removal treatment', 'feel-free-yourself-from-shaving-and-waxing', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Laser Hair Removal In Gurgaon\",\"Laser Hair Removal treatment\"]', 0, 1, '2022-04-12 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(435, 'suffering-from-nail-discoloration', 'Suffering From Nail Discoloration? Here’s How You Can Treat And Prevent It!', 'Nail discolouration, which causes the nails to appear white, yellow, or green, can be caused by a variety of diseases and skin problems. Read this blog to know more about nail discoloration.', '<p>Nail discolouration, which causes the nails to appear white, yellow, or green, can be caused by a variety of diseases and skin problems. Discolored nails are caused by infections with common fungus present in the air, dust, and dirt in around half of the cases. Fungi can harm your nails in a variety of ways.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The appearance of the nails can also be affected by chronic medical disorders. Changes in nail color can indicate diabetes, as well as problems with the liver, kidneys, heart, or lungs. This is why, during a typical physical check, doctors pay special attention to the nails.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What Are Some Common Causes And Their Treatments? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>1. Fungal Infections:</strong> One of the most common reasons for nail discoloration is this. Fungal infection frequently causes discolouration in the toenails. Dermatophyte, a form of fungus, commonly affects the nails. Yeast or mold can also cause these infections. They feed on the keratin in your nails to survive. Depending on the type of illness, the color of the nails can range from yellow to green to reddish-brown to black. It starts at the nail&#39;s tip and spreads as the infection worsens. You are more susceptible to these diseases if you have a low immunity and weak blood circulation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment:</strong> For certain reasons of nail yellowing, there are viable treatment options. To control fungal growth, start with over-the-counter ointments. If the infection has progressed to the point where your nail is crumbling or thickening, you should consult a dermatologist.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>2. Injuries:</strong> You&#39;ve probably observed that stubbing your toe or jamming your finger in a hinge causes your nails to turn blue or blackish. This form of discolouration can be caused by even poorly fitting shoes. This is due to a blood clot under the nail called a subungual hematoma. The color of the nails can even change from blue to purple or red in a matter of seconds. In these circumstances, you will experience discomfort and soreness in the affected area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment:</strong> In the vast majority of cases, these injuries heal on their own. Resting the affected area and using basic treatments like wrapping an ice pack will quickly resolve the problem. Although the damage heals and you are pain-free and relieved, the discolouration can take up to 6 months to entirely disappear.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>3. Nail Polish:</strong> It&#39;s always a good idea to choose your nail polish brand carefully. When you use low-quality nail polish on a regular basis, it is likely to leave a long-term mark in the shape of discolouration on your nails. It can also cause discolouration if used too regularly. The pigments in these nail paints frequently sink into your nails&#39; lower layers, producing significant discoloration.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment:</strong> In some circumstances, the only way to address nail discolouration is to take a break from coloring or other treatments. You can restore the natural color of your nails by eliminating nail paint for a few weeks.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>4. Yellow Nail Syndrome: </strong>One of the most common reasons for yellowing nails is this dermatological disorder. Yellowing of the nails is sometimes accompanied by a bent look, slower growth than typical, ridges and indentations, cuticle removal, or black or green coloration.Lung disease, pleural effusions, lymphedema, chronic bronchitis, rheumatoid arthritis, autoimmune diseases, and sinusitis are just a few of the underlying health issues linked to this type of nail discolouration.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment:</strong> There is no one-size-fits-all treatment for yellow nail condition. It either goes away on its own or is treated by diagnosing the underlying health problem. If the discoloration lasts for a long period, the best course of action is to see a doctor as soon as possible.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>5. Medications:</strong> Discolored nails can also be caused by some medications. In some people, the ingredients in these drugs can produce side effects such as yellowing of the nails.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment:</strong> Consult your doctor if you find that the discoloration occurs after you take specific medications. They might be able to suggest alternatives or other treatments for your nail discoloration.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Where To Seek Help? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>At Skinfinity, you will be under the care and supervision of the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/best-dermatologist-in-delhi-ncr/\"><em><strong>best skin specialist in Delhi NCR</strong></em></a>. We use only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all our patients. At Skinfinity, the patients are provided with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>or if you are from noida  <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Trust <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong> for expert dermatology care—find the <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/5435716e0b3c18e10467ad6f87865285.jpg', 'Suffering From Nail Discoloration', 'Suffering From Nail Discoloration? Read More | Skinfinity Derma Clinic', 'Nail discolouration, which causes the nails to appear white, yellow, or green, can be caused by a variety of diseases and skin problems. Read this blog to know more about nail discoloration.', 'Suffering From Nail Discoloration, skin specialist in delhi ncr', 'suffering-from-nail-discoloration', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Suffering From Nail Discoloration\",\"skin specialist in delhi ncr\"]', 0, 1, '2022-04-04 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(436, 'suffering-from-skin-pigmentation', 'Suffering From Skin Pigmentation? We Got You!', 'Changes in skin pigmentation can lighten or darken the color of your skin. If you are suffering from skin pigmentation, read this blog to know more.', '<p>Melanin levels (natural pigment) in your skin and your natural skin color are affected by skin pigmentation disorders. Changes in skin pigmentation can lighten or darken the color of your skin. Pigmentation disorders include <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/melasma-treatment/\">melasma treatment</a> , <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/freckles-and-lentigens/\">freckles</a>, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/vitiligo/\">vitiligo</a>, and pigmented birthmarks, to name a few.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Sun damage is the most common cause of hyperpigmentation. It could, however, reflect underlying issues or be caused by pharmaceutical adverse effects. If you&#39;ve gotten hyperpigmentation as a result of poor skin care or sun exposure, you can try several home remedies to help remove the pigmentation. While they may not be as effective as medical therapies, the results may be noticeable over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What Are The Symptoms?</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Pigmentation frequently has obvious signs and symptoms. Pigmentation is a frequent skin condition that can be caused by a variety of factors. Melasma, a skin disorder that causes <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-lightening-and-pigmentation/\">pigmentation</a>, is one of these reasons.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Melasma causes dark and discolored areas.</li>\r\n <li>Melasma causes dark and discolored areas on the face that are symmetrical and have a nearly identical pattern on both sides.</li>\r\n <li>These patches can be found on the neck, forearms, and other regions of the body that are exposed to the sun.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>How Is Skin Pigmentation Caused? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>UV radiation is the most common cause of excessive melanin synthesis. UV rays, however, do not cause instant harm. So, if you&#39;ve suddenly gotten pigmentation on your face, it&#39;s most likely the result of skin damage from a decade ago.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Do not be perplexed if you have used sunscreen your entire life and yet have skin discoloration. Other factors that may contribute to skin pigmentation include:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Injury to the skin results in skin damage (also called post-inflammatory pigmentation)</li>\r\n <li>Changes in hormones during pregnancy (melasma)</li>\r\n <li>Rashes on the skin (rosacea, psoriasis, eczema, contact dermatitis)</li>\r\n <li>Infections of the skin (acne, ringworm, tinea versicolor, candidiasis)</li>\r\n <li>Medical problems ( Lupus, cyanosis, untreated or undiagnosed diabetes)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Actinic keratosis, squamous cell carcinoma, basal cell carcinoma, and melanoma are among skin malignancies that can produce skin pigmentation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you detect any changes in your skin color, you should see a doctor. At Skinfinity, consult the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/about-us/\"><strong>best skin specialist in Delhi NCR</strong></a>. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What’s At Skinfinity? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Even though you can try out home remedies to<strong> get rid of skin pigmentation</strong>, they may not fade the pigmentation spots completely. These home remedies also provide slow results. You must check in with your doctor to get an opinion on whether your condition is medical or not. In case it is, we at Skinfinity are here to provide you with a wide range of options. These include: </p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li><strong>Microdermabrasion:</strong> For its usage and long-term outcomes on all skin tones, microdermabrasion for hyperpigmentation is a highly recommended treatment. Microdermabrasion is also gentler on the skin since it doesn&#39;t use harsh chemicals – instead, it uses a water-soluble component like glycolic acid that doesn&#39;t cause tissue damage; it has a faster recovery time after the procedure; and it could be one of the most affordable treatments available.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Chemical Peels:</strong> Chemical peels are a great way to get rid of hyperpigmentation. Chemical peels, also known as THE PERFECT DERMA PEEL, are a combination of salicylic acid, kojic acid, TCA, retinoic acid, Phenol Glutathione, and Vitamin C. It works wonders for aged skin, acne, melasma, and hyperpigmentation.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Laser Treatments:</strong> Hyperpigmentation can be reduced with a number of laser treatments. The majority of them do so by directing laser beams at the skin&#39;s afflicted area. This procedure uses ablative lasers to renew the skin by resurfacing its upper layers, allowing new skin to grow while also boosting collagen production.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Intense Pulsed Light (IPL) Treatment:</strong> The IPL therapy decreases sunspots, freckles, uneven skin tone, and surface pigmentation by using targeted pulses of broad-spectrum light. IPL treatment for pigmentation reduction is, without a doubt, one of the quickest and most straightforward methods of treating skin imperfections. IPL also targets a dark pigment known as melanin. The treatment removes dark spots, freckles, and other discoloration caused by UV exposure by breaking up melanin cells. Following therapy, the black patches may either scab over and flake away, or the lymphatic system will naturally remove them.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Why Choose Skinfinity? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Apart from providing a wide range of options, Skinfinity carries out all treatments under the care and supervision of Dr. Ipsita Johri, the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/best-dermatologist-in-delhi-ncr/\"><em><strong>best dermatologist in Delhi NCR</strong></em></a>, who keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root.  consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>or if you are from noida  <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Related Skin Treatments We Offer</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Enhance your skin health and achieve a flawless complexion with our range of specialized treatments:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Dark Circles Treatment</a> – Reduce under-eye pigmentation, puffiness, and tired appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Acne Scar Treatment</a> – Fade scars, smooth skin texture, and boost confidence.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Chemical Peel</a> – Exfoliate, brighten, and rejuvenate your skin naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Laser Skin Resurfacing</a> – Improve skin tone, refine texture, and reduce fine lines.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Anti-Aging Treatment</a> – Minimize wrinkles and restore youthful elasticity.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Pigmentation Treatment</a> – Even skin tone and fade dark spots effectively.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Botox Treatment</a> – Smooth dynamic wrinkles for a refreshed, youthful look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"#\">Freckles Treatment</a> – Lighten freckles with advanced laser and peel technology for an even tone.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Clear skin is possible with <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—book with a <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/250af4c26f0c047b8c6e9b073ce35eee.jpg', 'Suffering from Skin Pigmentation', 'Suffering from Skin Pigmentation? Read More | Skinfinity Clinic', 'Changes in skin pigmentation can lighten or darken the color of your skin. If you are suffering from skin pigmentation, read this blog to know more.', 'Suffering from Skin Pigmentation, skin specialist in delhi ncr,', NULL, 'neha', NULL, '[\"Suffering from Skin Pigmentation\",\"skin specialist in delhi ncr\"]', 0, 1, '2022-03-25 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(437, 'makeup-hacks-for-sensitive-skin', 'Makeup Hacks For Sensitive Skin', 'You have sensitive skin doesn\'t mean you can\'t use cosmetics. Here are some tips for you to put on make-up even when you have sensitive skin. Read more.', '<p>People with sensitive skin must adjust to particular situations and routines that are not necessary for people with normal skin. However, just because you have sensitive skin doesn&#39;t mean you can&#39;t use cosmetics. Cosmetics businesses may now design products that are beneficial to persons with sensitive skin thanks to technological advancements. You only need to experiment with a few different formulas and routines until you find one that works for you.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Here are some tips for you to put on make-up even when you have sensitive skin:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>1. Choose The Right Formula:</strong> When using cosmetics on sensitive skin, the formulation is the most important factor to consider. Hypoallergenic and non-comedogenic products are less likely to bother your skin. They do not, however, guarantee safety. Identifying the elements that cause your allergies to flare up is a better way of determining which formulation will work for your skin. Retinol, benzoyl peroxide, salicylic acid, glycolic acid, talc, phenol, camphor, and ammonia are the most prevalent skin irritants. You must figure out which of these compounds causes your skin to respond unfavorably. Certain chemicals can be disguised in hypoallergenic face creams, so be sure to read the labels carefully.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>2. Prep Your Skin:</strong> Experts advise that sensitive skin be adequately hydrated before applying makeup. It&#39;s more than just slathering on some moisturizer. Spraying thermal water on your face before applying moisturizer and makeup is a good idea. Also, elements like chamomile can help to soothe sensitive skin, so search for it in your moisturizer.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>3. Checking Expiration Dates:</strong> People frequently overlook expiration dates. The product has a small indicator on it that indicates how long it will last when you open it. Once your skincare and cosmetic items have reached the end of their useful life, replace them. Now is the time to check your drawers! </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>4. Avoid Highly-Pigmented Makeup:</strong> The higher the pigments in your cosmetics, the more colors you have. Avoid eyeshadows, for example, because they contain a lot of pigments. Make an effort to select cosmetics with less pigments. If you have an adverse reaction to highly pigmented makeup, stick to neutral tones like beige, cream, and bronze. Lipsticks work on the same premise. The more red the lipstick, the more probable it is to trigger allergies and skin irritation. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you love putting on makeup but have highly sensitive skin, consider using these hacks. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Consult us at <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><em><strong>Skinfinity</strong></em></a> for more such skincare tips and tricks! consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>or if you are from noida  <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com\"><strong>dermatologist in noida</strong> </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Related Skin & Aesthetic Services We Offer</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dark-circle-treatment/\" target=\"_new\">Dark Circles Treatment</a> – Reduce under-eye pigmentation, puffiness, and tired appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/organic-hydrafacial/\" target=\"_new\">HydraFacial</a> – Deep cleansing and hydration without harsh exfoliation.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\" target=\"_new\">Chemical Peel</a> – Brighten and rejuvenate your skin with mild, sensitive-skin-friendly formulas.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler/\" target=\"_new\">Dermal Fillers</a> – Restore volume and enhance facial features naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/botox-treatment-gurgaon/\">Botox</a> – Smooth fine lines and wrinkles for a refreshed look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-lightening-and-pigmentation/\" target=\"_new\">Pigmentation Treatment</a> – Even skin tone and reduce dark spots.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\" target=\"_new\">Acne & Pimple Treatment</a> – Calm breakouts and prevent future flare-ups.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/melasma-treatment/\" target=\"_new\">Melasma Treatment</a> – Target stubborn pigmentation with advanced dermatology solutions.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/freckles-and-lentigens/\" target=\"_new\">Freckles Treatment</a> – Fade freckles and achieve a clearer complexion.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hairfall-treatment-noida/\" target=\"_new\">PRP Skin Rejuvenation</a> – Use your body’s own growth factors to boost skin repair.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><em>All treatments are dermatologist-approved and tailored to sensitive skin needs.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity Derma Clinic offers trusted skincare with the <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/c6cf9b2eb0e4fafed29d40ff89c28668.jpg', 'Makeup Hacks For Sensitive Skin', 'Makeup Hacks For Sensitive Skin | Skinfinity Derma Clinic', 'You have sensitive skin doesn\'t mean you can\'t use cosmetics. Here are some tips for you to put on make-up even when you have sensitive skin. Read more.', 'Makeup Hacks For Sensitive Skin,', 'makeup-hacks-for-sensitive-skin', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Makeup Hacks For Sensitive Skin\"]', 0, 1, '2022-03-21 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(438, 'different-types-of-hair-loss', 'Different Types of Hair Loss: Causes, Treatments & How to Stop Hair Fall', 'Learn about the different types of hair loss, main causes, and the best treatments to stop hair fall and regrow hair naturally. Get expert advice today!', '<p>Hair loss is a common concern affecting millions of people worldwide, regardless of age or gender. While it’s normal to shed 50–100 hairs per day, excessive hair loss can be distressing and impact self-confidence. Understanding the different types of hair loss can help you identify the cause and choose the right treatment. If you’re experiencing constant shedding or thinning, exploring <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-fall-treatment-gurgaon/\"><strong>hair fall treatment in Gurgaon</strong></a> can be a great first step toward restoring healthier, fuller hair.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In this article, we’ll break down the main types of hair loss, their causes, and possible solutions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What Is Hair Loss?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Hair loss, also known as alopecia, refers to a partial or complete loss of hair from the scalp or other parts of the body. There are various types of hair loss, and each has different underlying reasons, from genetics to lifestyle factors.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>1. Androgenetic Alopecia (Pattern Baldness)</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This is the most common type of hair loss, affecting both men and women.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In men, it often begins with a receding hairline and thinning on the crown (known as male pattern baldness).<br>\r\nIn women, it usually presents as diffuse thinning on the top of the head.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Causes:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Genetics</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hormonal changes (e.g., DHT sensitivity)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment options:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Minoxidil (topical solution)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Finasteride (oral medication for men)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hair transplant surgery</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>PRP (Platelet-Rich Plasma) therapy<br>\r\n  </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>2. Telogen Effluvium</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Telogen effluvium is temporary hair shedding that occurs when a large number of hair follicles enter the resting (telogen) phase at the same time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Causes:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Physical or emotional stress</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Illness or surgery</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Sudden weight loss</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Nutritional deficiencies</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Post-pregnancy (postpartum hair loss)<br>\r\n  </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment options:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Addressing the underlying cause</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Nutritional support</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Gentle hair care<br>\r\n  </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>3. Alopecia Areata</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Alopecia areata is an autoimmune condition where the body’s immune system attacks hair follicles, leading to patchy hair loss.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Causes:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Autoimmune reactions</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Genetic predisposition</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Stress<br>\r\n  </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment options:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Corticosteroid injections</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Topical immunotherapy</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>PRP therapy</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>4. Traction Alopecia</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This type of hair loss is caused by prolonged tension on the hair due to tight hairstyles like ponytails, braids, or extensions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Causes:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Frequent tight hairstyles</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hair accessories causing stress on roots<br>\r\n  </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment options:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Avoiding tight hairstyles</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Scalp massage and gentle hair care</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hair restoration treatments in severe cases</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>5. Anagen Effluvium</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This occurs due to sudden interruption of the hair growth phase (anagen), commonly seen during chemotherapy or exposure to toxic chemicals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Causes:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Chemotherapy</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Radiation therapy</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Severe infections</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Treatment options:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hair typically regrows once treatment stops</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Scalp cooling caps during chemotherapy (to reduce hair loss)</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>When Should You See a Hair Specialist?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you notice sudden, severe, or patchy hair loss, it’s important to consult a dermatologist or hair specialist. Early diagnosis helps prevent further hair thinning and improves treatment outcomes.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How Can a Hair Loss Clinic Help?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A specialized hair loss clinic can provide personalized assessments, advanced diagnostics, and treatments like PRP, mesotherapy, and hair transplants. Choosing the best hair clinic near you ensures you get expert advice and the most effective solutions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Final Thoughts</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Hair loss can be emotionally challenging, but understanding its types and causes is the first step toward regaining your confidence. Whether it’s pattern baldness, telogen effluvium, or alopecia areata, there are effective treatments available today.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re struggling with hair loss, consult a trusted specialist to discuss your options and find a treatment plan tailored to you.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Should I Consult A Doctor? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you are experiencing hair loss, it is always advisable to consult your doctor. Skinfinity provides the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-fall-treatment/\">best hair loss treatment in Noida</a>. We prioritize the beauty and wellness of our clients, and with our cutting-edge technology, we always strive to achieve the best results. With our team of highly qualified and experienced specialists, and international standards of technology, infrastructure, clinical care and modern medicines, we help our patients achieve all their dreams of beauty and wellness. consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\">dermatologist in gurgaon </a>or if you are from noida  <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">dermatologist in noida </a>then and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Get expert help at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> can assist:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/4096f92fd5424a3baa058fae817169aa.jpg', 'types of hair loss', 'Know About The Different Types Of Hair Loss | Skinfinity Hair Clinic', 'Hair loss could be attributed to a person’s genetics, although many medical and behavioral conditions may interrupt the growth cycle and cause hair loss. Read this blog to know more about hair loss.', 'types of hair loss, hair loss treatment', 'different-types-of-hair-loss', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"types of hair loss\",\"hair loss treatment\"]', 0, 1, '2022-03-15 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(439, 'bikini-and-underarm-brightening-treatment', 'Bikini And Underarm Brightening', 'You can easily get rid of hyperpigmentation with Skinfinity’s bikini and underarm brightening treatment. Continue reading to find out more.', '<p>Hyperpigmentation in the armpits and the bikini area could sometimes be a nuisance as it may keep you away from wearing those sexy and comfortable sleeveless shirts. As these areas are more delicate and sensitive than others, the negative impacts of hyperpigmentation are more visible here. However, you can easily get rid of this darkening by opting for Skinfinity’s <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/bikini-and-underarm-brightening\"><strong>bikini and underarm brightening treatment</strong></a>. Continue reading to find out more! </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What Are The Causes? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Shaving:</strong> Shaving does not remove the hair from the root, giving an unsightly stubble to your skin, making it appear as if you have darker underarms. Ingrown hair also contributes to this problem. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Heredity:</strong> The effects of hyperpigmentation are hereditary in some people and are accelerated due to frequent shaving and waxing. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Deodorants and Antiperspirants:</strong> These also result in darkened skin, so you must refrain from using them. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Diabetes/ PCOS:</strong> Imbalance in the insulin levels and insulin resistance also causes hyperpigmentation, which consequently darkens the skin. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What’s At Skinfinity? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity provides a range of treatments for lightening the underarm and bikini area. These are: </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Laser Hair Removal:</strong> The adverse effects of waxing and shaving are not unknown, and when done frequently, it leads to pigmentation which is extremely difficult to get rid off. However, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-removal-noida\">laser hair removal</a> is safe and free of risks and side effects, thus helping in skin lightening.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Microdermabrasion:</strong> In microdermabrasion, dead cells are removed from the skin through vacuum technology, therefore removing the pigmented dark skin. It also clears the blackheads in the bikini area that happen because of ingrowing hair. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Skin Lightening Peel:</strong> In this treatment, organic and fruit-based peels are used as the underarm and bikini area has sensitive and delicate skin. These help in removing the dead layer from the skin, thereby making the skin appear lighter and brighter. Peel also helps in treating boils, scars and spots in bikini and underarm area. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q switch and fraxel laser-</strong> For velvety hyperpigmentation, acanthosis nigricans due to pcos or hormonal imbalance, lasers work best in lightening the deep deposits of melanin causing dark underarms. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What Are The Benefits Of These Treatments? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>These treatments give you an even-toned skin in the armpits and bikini area, which matches the rest of your skin. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>You can wear sleeveless blouses and bikinis without any embarrassment. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>They reduce the risk of further darkening of armpits and the bikini area. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>They give long-lasting results and freedom from further hair growth in these areas. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Why Choose Skinfinity?</strong> </h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity prioritizes your needs and places you under the care and supervision of Dr. Johri, who keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products and lasers, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Related Skin Brightening & Pigmentation Treatments at Skinfinity Derma</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>At <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">Skinfinity Derma</a>, we offer a range of advanced skin treatments to address hyperpigmentation, uneven tone, and dullness:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/bikini-and-underarm-brightening/\">Bikini Brightening Treatments</a> – Reduce pigmentation and restore an even, radiant skin tone in intimate areas.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/bikini-and-underarm-brightening/\">Underarm Brightening Treatments</a> – Lighten dark underarms caused by friction, shaving, or hormonal changes.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-lightening-and-spots/\">Full Body Skin Brightening</a> – Enhance your skin tone and texture for an overall glow.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\">Chemical Peels for Pigmentation </a>– Gently exfoliate and fade stubborn dark patches.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser/\">Laser Pigmentation Removal</a> – Target and break down excess melanin for long-lasting results.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/iv-glutathoine-therapy/\">Glutathione Skin Brightening Therapy</a> – Boost skin radiance from within.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> <em>All treatments are performed by experienced dermatologists using safe, effective techniques tailored to your skin type.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<h2>FAQs </h2>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q1. What is the average bikini whitening treatment price?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nThe bikini whitening treatment price depends on the clinic, method, and sessions, usually starting from moderate to premium packages.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q2. Can I try bikini whitening treatment at home?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nYes, home remedies like aloe vera gel, yogurt, turmeric, and natural scrubs can help lighten the bikini area gradually.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q3. Which is the best bikini whitening treatment cream?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nThe best bikini whitening treatment cream usually contains natural brightening agents like kojic acid, licorice, or vitamin C.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q4. What is the best bikini whitening treatment for quick results?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\n Laser treatments and professional chemical peels are considered the best bikini whitening treatments for fast and visible results.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q5. Is there a permanent bikini whitening treatment?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nPermanent bikini whitening treatment is usually done through advanced dermatological methods like lasers and peels, but maintenance is required.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q6. What is the permanent skin whitening treatment price for intimate areas?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nThe price of permanent skin whitening treatment varies depending on the procedure, clinic, and number of sessions.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q7. How to whiten bikini area in a week?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nUsing lemon-honey masks, yogurt-turmeric packs, and exfoliation daily may help whiten the bikini area in a week.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q8. What is the bikini whitening laser treatment price?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nBikini whitening laser treatment price depends on skin type, pigmentation level, and clinic charges, generally higher than creams or home remedies.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q9. Can I do bikini pigmentation treatment at home?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nBikini pigmentation treatment at home includes natural remedies like aloe vera, cucumber, and turmeric packs for gradual lightening.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Q10. What are the best bikini pigmentation treatment options?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nThe best bikini pigmentation treatments include dermatologist-recommended chemical peels, laser therapy, and clinically tested creams.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Flawless skin starts with <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—consult our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/e9d92737f9741ea94867b178685e51d6.jpg', 'Bikini And Underarm Brightening', 'Bikini And Underarm Brightening Treatment | Get Rid of Hyperpigmentation', 'You can easily get rid of hyperpigmentation with Skinfinity’s bikini and underarm brightening treatment. Continue reading to find out more.', 'Bikini And Underarm Brightening, Bikini And Underarm Brightening treatment', NULL, 'ipshita', NULL, '[\"Bikini And Underarm Brightening\",\"Bikini And Underarm Brightening treatment\"]', 0, 1, '2022-03-07 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(440, 'remove-neck-wart', 'How to remove neck wart aid at home?', 'Warts are skin growths that are completely innocuous. Infections with the human papillomavirus (HPV) cause them.', '<p>Warts are skin growths that are completely innocuous. Infections with the human papillomavirus (HPV) cause them. Warts can be spread from person to person. They may go on their own, but it may take weeks, months, or even years. Chemical peels, surgery, freezing, and laser surgery are all common treatments, but they may be costly and cause skin discomfort. Another alternative is to use natural wart cures at home.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Apple cider vinegar</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>An acidic material formed from fermented apple juice is apple cider vinegar. It&#39;s supposed to function in the same way as salicylic acid, a traditional wart treatment that scrapes away contaminated skin and finally removes the wart, does.<strong> </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Banana peel</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Banana peel, according to anecdotal evidence, may aid in the removal of warts. However, there is no scientific proof that banana peels can heal warts or viral skin diseases, and there is no scientific evidence that banana peels can combat HPV. If you want to give it a go, cut a piece of banana peel and tape it over the wart before going to bed, making sure the inside half of the peel is in contact with your skin. Turn it on while you sleep and do it every day.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Garlic</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Garlic has traditionally been used to treat skin ailments such as psoriasis, keloid scars, and corns. It&#39;s also used to treat infections caused by bacteria, fungi, and viruses, such as warts. Garlic extract was found to cure warts in a previous trial in just four weeks. The warts did not reappear.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Orange peel</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Orange peel is another common wart treatment. It&#39;s a low-cost solution, but there&#39;s no scientific evidence to back it up. Once a day, dab an orange peel on the wart as a treatment. The wart is said to change colour, darken, and ultimately fall out. This might take up to two weeks.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Pineapple</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Bromelain, a blend of protein-digesting enzymes found in pineapple, may aid in the removal of dead and damaged skin. While there is some evidence that bromelain may be beneficial in treating a few medical ailments, there are no scientific studies that support its usage to eradicate warts.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Potato</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>People believe that potato juice may \"dehydrate\" a wart, however there are no studies to back this up. Cut a small potato in half to test this procedure. Rub the sliced side of the potato on the wart until it is completely saturated with juice. Repeat this process twice a day.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Dandelion weed</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Many people consider dandelions to be bothersome weeds. Dandelions, on the other hand, are used in ancient Chinese and Middle Eastern medicine for their therapeutic benefits. Dandelions contain antibacterial characteristics that might help with warts, but further research is needed to be sure.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Aloe vera</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Aloe vera gel is often used to treat burns and psoriasis on the skin. The gel may give relief if your wart is itchy or uncomfortable. Remove a leaf off an aloe vera plant and cut it open to utilise it. Apply the gel on the wart using a cotton swab. Rep on a daily basis. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Aspirin</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Salicylic acid, a prominent component in over-the-counter wart treatments, is found in aspirin. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>By scraping away the contaminated skin, salicylic acid helps to heal warts. This gradually eliminates the wart. Aspirin, on the other hand, is supposed to have a similar effect. Aspirin pills should be crushed and mixed with water, according to the instructions. Overnight, apply the paste on the wart and cover it with a bandage. consult with <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>best dermatologist in Noida</strong></a>, if you are from gurgaon then consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol. today!For any skin related issues, make an appointment at Skinfinity Derma, the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/best-dermatologist-in-delhi-ncr/\">best dermatologist in Delhi NCR</a>. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Related Skin Treatments We Offer</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/mole-removal/\"><strong>Mole Removal</strong></a> – Safe and scar-minimizing removal of unwanted moles.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Skin Tag Removal</strong> – Quick, painless removal of skin tags from face, neck, and body.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Corn & Callus Removal</strong> – Smooth, pain-free treatment for thickened skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/wart-removal/\">Wart Removal</a> (All Areas)</strong> – Laser or advanced medical removal of warts on face, hands, feet, or body.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Scar Revision</strong> – Minimize the appearance of scars for smoother skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser/\"><strong>Laser Skin Resurfacing</strong> </a>– Improve skin texture, tone, and overall clarity.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\"><strong>Anti-Aging Treatments</strong></a> – Botox, fillers, and skin tightening for youthful skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/melasma-treatment/\"><strong>MelasmaTreatment</strong></a> – Target dark spots, freckles, and uneven skin tone.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/organic-hydrafacial/\">HydraFacial</a> / <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/clinical-facials/\">MediFacial</a></strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/clinical-facials/\"> </a>– Deep cleansing, hydration, and rejuvenation in one session.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><em>All procedures are performed by experienced dermatologists ensuring safe, effective, and lasting results.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<h3><em>FAQS</em></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q1. How do you get rid of a wart in 24 hours?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>While complete wart removal in 24 hours is rare, treatments like cryotherapy or strong wart removers can help shrink it quickly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q2. What is the strongest wart remover?</strong><br>\r\nThe strongest wart removers usually contain salicylic acid or use freezing therapy for faster results.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q3. How can I remove warts on face naturally?</strong><br>\r\nNatural remedies like apple cider vinegar, garlic, or castor oil are commonly used for warts on the face, but always do a patch test first.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q4. How to remove warts on neck naturally?</strong><br>\r\nApplying tea tree oil, aloe vera, or castor oil regularly can help in removing neck warts naturally.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q5. How to remove massa from neck in Hindi?</strong><br>\r\nMassa ????? ?? ??? ????? ?? ??, ????? ?? ????? ?? ?????? ??? ???? ????? ???? ????? ??? ?? ???? ????</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q6. Which is the best warts removal cream?</strong><br>\r\nWarts removal creams with salicylic acid or herbal extracts are effective in reducing and eliminating warts.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q7. Is salicylic acid effective for warts?</strong><br>\r\nYes, salicylic acid for warts is one of the most recommended treatments as it peels away the infected skin layers gradually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q8. What are the best wart removal home remedies?</strong><br>\r\nHome remedies include apple cider vinegar, banana peel, garlic paste, and castor oil application.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q9. Can warts on the neck be removed permanently?</strong><br>\r\nYes, warts on the neck can be removed permanently using dermatological treatments or consistent natural remedies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Q10. Which method works faster – wart removal cream or home remedies?</strong><br>\r\nWart removal creams with salicylic acid usually work faster than home remedies, but natural remedies are gentler on the skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Expert skincare awaits at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic </strong>connect with our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/59dcd7b6df9bb5f80d7f912804186f26.jpg', 'Skin & Hair Care', 'How to remove neck wart aid at home? | Skinfinity Derma', 'Warts can be spread from person to person. They may go on their own, but it may take weeks, months, or even years. Read this blog to know about How to remove neck wart aid at home?', 'remove neck wart, How to remove neck wart aid at home', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[]', 0, 1, '2022-03-29 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(441, 'a-guide-to-non-surgical-hair-transplant', 'A Comprehensive Guide To Non-Surgical Hair Transplant', 'When you have thinning hair, it is natural to consider hair transplant as an option. However, hair transplant is an invasive and surgical process. But if you want to save your hair without going through a surgery, there are several non-surgical methods that would restore your hair to their original form with equal effectiveness.', '<p>When you have thinning hair, it is natural to consider hair transplant as an option. However, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-transplant-in-gurgaon/\">hair transplant</a> is an invasive and surgical process. But if you want to save your hair without going through a surgery, there are several non-surgical methods that would restore your hair to their original form with equal effectiveness. Stay glued to this comprehensive guide to learn all about your<strong> hair transplant options</strong>. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What Are Non-Surgical Hair Transplants?</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>A treatment that can regrow and regenerate your hair without the use of anesthesia, surgery, or any downtime, is called a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/non-surgical-hair-replacement/\">non-surgical hair transplant</a>. These treatments are FDA approved. However, it must be kept in mind that a non-surgical hair transplant does not work in cases of advanced or extreme hair loss. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What Are The Different Types Of Non-Surgical Hair Transplant Treatments?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Minoxidil:</strong> This is a common ingredient in Rogaine, which is an over-the-counter hair loss treatment. It is a topical treatment applied right to your scalp. Some doctors have access to pharmaceutical-grade minoxidil and customize their own mixture. This makes it the perfect treatment to add to your at-home hair care routine.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Finasteride:</strong> This is an oral tablet, which especially treats male pattern baldness. This prescription is only for men, as it works by reducing the hormone dihydrotestosterone (DHT) produced by your body, and this kind of therapy is not appropriate for women.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>PRP:</strong> Platelet-Rich Plasma, or PRP, is the most successful therapy for hair loss. It involves the use of platelets and growth factors from your own blood to assist inactive hair follicles to move back into the growth phase. It has gained popularity for treating patterned hair loss, thinning of the hair, and receding hairline. PRP is non-surgical and does not involve the addition of follicles in the target area. PRP helps with the reactivation of dormant hair follicles and stimulates hair growth, unlike a transplant, which provides dramatic results. Skinfinity offers the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-treatments\">best hair PRP treatment in Noida</a>. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Laser Treatment:</strong> Popularly known as red light therapy, a low level laser therapy exposes your scalp to photons. This heals the weak cells and helps in the regrowing of hair. The scalp becomes rejuvenated and refreshed through multiple low-level laser treatments because they increase circulation to your scalp and stimulate hair follicles to grow.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Microneedling:</strong> It is done with the help of derma rollers and it aims to improve the blood circulation in the scalp and promotes the growth of collagen fibers which enhance hair growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Skinfinity’s Non-Surgical Hair Replacement Patches:</strong> At Skinfinity, we analyze the scalp condition and existing hair, after which we measure the size of the bald area to make the patch of the same size so that it can fit you better. Simultaneously, a hair sample is taken to prepare a<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/non-surgical-hair-replacement/\"><strong> hair patch</strong></a> of similar hair color and texture to give you an original look.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Just as there are several treatment methods, experiences of the patients may also vary. It is not right for everyone to expect the same outcome. While some may be overjoyed with the results, others may regret their decision. Therefore, it is always advisable to consult your dermatologist before you select a treatment option to restore your hair back to its glory and beauty. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Why Should I Choose Skinfinity? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Skinfinity offers a 360 degree solution for all your hair problems.</li>\r\n <li>If you are looking for a non-surgical hair replacement process, then it is the right place for you. </li>\r\n <li>Skinfinity prioritizes your needs and places you under the care and supervision of Dr. Johri, the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">best dermatologist in Noida</a>.</li>\r\n <li>She also keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. </li>\r\n <li>Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. </li>\r\n <li>At Skinfinity, the hair of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs and recommending the most suitable treatment options. </li>\r\n <li>We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>For a detailed consultation, book an appointment now! </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Renew your skin’s health at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—discover the best <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<strong> Location : </strong><a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/6238856e1004aa7fe23e3712a8a9e45d.jpg', 'Hair Transplant', ' Hair Transplant', 'If you are looking for a non-surgical hair transplant process, then it is the right place for you. Read this blog to know more or call to our best dermatologist in Noida at Skinfinity.', ' Hair Transplant', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Hair Transplant\"]', 0, 1, '2022-02-23 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(442, 'minimize-stretch-marks-with-skinfinity-treatment', 'Minimize Those Stretch Marks With Skinfinity’s Treatments!', 'Dermatologically known as striae, stretch marks appear due to the rapid stretching of the skin. These initially appear over the skin as streaks of red or pink that may become white and scarlike over time.', '<p>Dermatologically known as striae, stretch marks appear due to the rapid stretching of the skin. These initially appear over the skin as streaks of red or pink that may become white and scarlike over time. Though not painful or harmful in any way, they make the skin look unappealing, especially if they develop over visible areas- such as shoulders, calves or arms. They may lead to you undermining your confidence in your beautiful body, disallowing you to embrace your beauty completely.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>However, at Skinfinity Clinic, you will be treated by the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">best skin specialist in Delhi NCR</a> who can reduce and remove those stretch marks, based on an individual’s skin repairing potential. The treatments opted for are the MNRF, PRP and Derma Roller treatment.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Can You Avoid Stretch Marks? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>By being on a diet which is rich in nutrients, you can avoid stretch marks. Such a diet includes a mix of eggs, whole wheat toast and berries, and helps boost the skin health. This diet also helps in balancing and maintaining the weight, as rapid weight gain and loss is the leading cause of stretch marks. Drinking lots of water and eating foods rich in zinc and vitamins also helps to avoid stretch marks. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Is It Possible To Treat Stretch Marks At Home? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Several remedies can be used to reduce the visibility of stretch marks at home. A few of these are listed below: </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Almond oil massage </li>\r\n <li>Hyaluronic acid </li>\r\n <li>Virgin coconut oil </li>\r\n <li>Aloe vera</li>\r\n <li>Cocoa butter</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The above-mentioned remedies have moisturizing properties which may not prevent them entirely but they do reduce their visible appearance. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What Are The Different Treatments? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>MNRF And Its Advantages</strong><br>\r\nMicroneedling Radiofrequency (MNRF) is an extremely effective technique to counter the problem of stretch marks. Even though MNRF takes place through a few sessions, results can easily be evaluated as changes can be noticed evidently after each session. The procedure uses very tiny microneedles so as to deliver safe radiofrequency energy into the deeper damaged skin, completely excluding the upper layer, or the epidermis from the process, and therefore letting it remain unaffected. The radiofrequency energy helps tighten the dermis, and triggers the activation of the collagen and elastin production within the body. Another benefit of this treatment is the lack of any downtime. The recovery period is minimum, and the patient obtaining this treatment can resume with their day-to-day activities almost immediately. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Easy And Affordable: The Derma Roller Therapy</strong><br>\r\nThe Derma Roller treatment is a natural skin regeneration and scar repair therapy which is used worldwide. At Skinfinity Clinic, we offer an advanced micro-medical skin-needling. This treatment stimulates the skin by pricking it first through micro-needles, which is followed by regeneration of the underlying tissue, causing the skin to repair itself naturally by producing new collagen. Over time, the stretch marks reduce in visibility and the skin appears smoother while the dark color caused due to the stretch marks gradually fades away. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>PRP Therapy For Cutting-Edge and Aesthetic Solutions</strong><br>\r\n<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platelet-rich_plasma\">Platelet Rich Plasma (PRP)</a> therapy is an effective treatment for stretch marks. Plasma contains white blood cells and platelets, which are rich in growth factors. These growth factors help stimulate the affected areas and help to repair the skin and minimize the appearance of stretch marks. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Why Choose Skinfinity? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Skinfinity prioritizes your needs and places you under the care and supervision of Dr. Johri, the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">best skin doctor in Noida</a>.</li>\r\n <li>She also keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. </li>\r\n <li>Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. </li>\r\n <li>At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs.</li>\r\n <li>We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. </li>\r\n <li>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>For a detailed consultation, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/book-appointment\">book an appointment now</a>!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Related Skin & Aesthetic Services We Offer</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Microneedling for <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/stretch-mark/\">Stretch Marks</a></strong> – Stimulates collagen to fade stretch marks naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Laser Stretch Mark Removal</strong> – Targets pigmentation and texture for smoother skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\"><strong>Chemical Peels</strong> </a>– Improves skin tone and reduces the appearance of marks.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Platelet-Rich Plasma (PRP) Therapy</strong> – Boosts skin repair and regeneration.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hifu/\"><strong>Skin Tightening Treatments</strong></a> – Firms loose skin post-weight loss or pregnancy.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Scar Reduction Treatments</strong> – Minimizes old scars and improves overall skin texture.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/organic-hydrafacial/\"><strong>Hydration & Glow Facials</strong></a> – Replenishes skin moisture for a healthier look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><em>We customize every treatment based on your skin type, stretch mark severity, and desired results for maximum improvement.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Personalized skin treatments at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—visit our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/eefddc0638a091b4d8a6ff3f0f7e3a69.jpg', 'minimize the stretch marks', 'Minimize Those Stretch Marks With Skinfinity’s Treatments | Skin Specialist in Delhi NCR', 'Stretch marks appear due to the rapid stretching of the skin. At Skinfinity Clinic, you will be treated by the best skin specialist in Delhi NCR who can reduce and remove those stretch marks. Read this blog to know more.', 'minimize the stretch marks, skinfinity treatments, skin specialist in delhi ncr, best skin doctor in noida', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"minimize the stretch marks\",\"skinfinity treatments\",\"skin specialist in delhi ncr\",\"best skin doctor in noida\"]', 0, 1, '2022-02-21 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(443, 'anti-aging-fillers-for-younger-skin', 'Is Your Age Showing On Your Skin? Get Those Fillers Now!', 'Aging is inevitable. However, it is for you to control how it shows on your skin. While many rely on anti-aging creams, they do not always show promising results and are not very affordable in the longer haul.', '<p>Aging is inevitable but how it shows on your skin is something you can control. While many people rely on anti-aging creams, these often fail to deliver promising results and can become costly in the long run. In such cases, opting for a professional <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler/\"><strong>fillers treatment in Noida</strong></a> can help you preserve that youthful glow for much longer. Stay with us to learn everything about dermal fillers!</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>What Are Fillers And How Do They Work? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>In the rapidly advancing field of facial rejuvenation, dermal fillers are a gift of science that help restore and optimize your youthful appearance. These are medical device implants approved by the FDA, and are injected into the skin. Dermal fillers are based on hyaluronic acid, a substance that naturally exists in your body. Dermal fillers are a soft injectable gel consisting of stabilized, non-animal hyaluronic acid. The gel is tissue-friendly and closely resembles the hyaluronic acid that exists naturally in the body. It is long-lasting but not permanent. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dermal fillers work by boosting the skin’s supply of hyaluronic acid. Dermal fillers revitalize and add volume to the skin, instantly diminishing the appearance of lines and wrinkles, and giving a natural softer look.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Why Opt For Dermal Fillers?</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A professionally done <strong>fillers treatment in Noida</strong> offers several advantages:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Dermal fillers help in balancing the symmetry of the face and bringing the external features into harmony. </li>\r\n <li>Dermal fillers also add volume and plumpness to the skin. </li>\r\n <li>They help treat wrinkles in the soft part of the face near your mouth. </li>\r\n <li>They can also reduce scars and wrinkles on hands. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What Are The Types Of Fillers Available? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li><strong>Temporary Fillers – </strong>Hyaluronic acid dermal filler comes under this type. When used in dermal filler treatment, hyaluronic acid is degraded slowly in the skin, making its results temporary.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Semi-permanent Fillers –</strong> Dermal fillers made from synthetic substances that are not absorbed by the body provide results that last longer than hyaluronic acid filler treatment.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Permanent Fillers –</strong> Such fillers offer a permanent solution for your wrinkles and for rejuvenating any sunken areas of the face, but they are not approved by the FDA due to safety concerns. Silicone and PTFE based fillers are common examples. The results are too evident and look artificial. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What Are The Benefits Of Dermal Fillers? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Collagen production decreases with age. In this case, dermal fillers help the body to stimulate more collagen production resulting in a younger and healthier looking skin.</li>\r\n <li>Dermal fillers provide instant results. You can notice the transformation as soon as you are done with the procedure. </li>\r\n <li>No downtime, and you can go back to your normal routine immediately. </li>\r\n <li>A minimally invasive procedure which requires no anesthesia. </li>\r\n <li>The results are subtle and natural-looking and last for a long period of time, with a few touch-ups every now and then. </li>\r\n <li>Fillers help reduce the appearance of scars on the skin, therefore boosting your self-confidence. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>To secure these benefits and get the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler\">best fillers treatment in Noida</a>, visit us at Skinfinity! </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>How Much Do Dermal Fillers Cost? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The cost of <strong>fillers treatment in Noida</strong> can range from anywhere between INR 20,000 to INR 1,00,000. The cost may also vary depending upon the type of filler being used, your location, and the experience and reputation of the dermatologist and the clinic. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Why Choose Skinfinity? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity prioritizes your needs and places you under the care and supervision of Dr. Johri, an expert injector with an advanced training in fillers and anti-wrinkle injections. She also keeps up with the latest trends, methods and techniques in cosmetology and dermatology. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity uses only US FDA approved products, thereby ensuring the safety and well-being of all its patients. At Skinfinity, the skin of the patient is carefully and thoroughly examined, thereby providing them with individualized care and a customized treatment to suit their needs. We aim to achieve long-lasting results by identifying the problem and treating it at the root. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol. For a detailed consultation, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/book-appointment\">book an appointment now</a>! </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Popular Filler & Skin Enhancement Treatments We Offer</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/lip-fillers/\"><strong>Lip Fillers</strong> </a>– Add volume, shape, and symmetry for naturally plump lips.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Cheek Fillers</strong> – Lift and contour cheekbones for a youthful structure.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Under-Eye Fillers</strong> – Reduce hollowness, dark circles, and tired appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Chin Fillers</strong> – Enhance chin shape and balance facial proportions.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Jawline Fillers</strong> – Define jawline for a sharper, more sculpted look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Nasolabial Fold Fillers</strong> – Soften smile lines for smoother skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Marionette Line Fillers</strong> – Lift sagging corners of the mouth.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Non-Surgical Nose Job (Liquid Rhinoplasty)</strong> – Reshape the nose using fillers without surgery.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Temple Fillers</strong> – Restore lost volume for a youthful forehead contour.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler/\"><strong>Full Face Rejuvenation with Fillers</strong></a> – Comprehensive anti-aging with strategic filler placement.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><em>All treatments are customized for natural-looking results, performed by skilled professionals using high-quality fillers.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Discover ideal skincare at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—book with our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> today:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/7eea949337e813f34c09587be3c2afcf.jpg', 'fillers treatment in Noida', 'Is Your Age Showing On Your Skin? Get Those Fillers Now | Skinfinity', 'Aging is inevitable and to control how it shows on your skin, read this blog. Get fillers treatment in noida at very affordable prices on Skinfinity.', 'fillers treatment in Noida, anti aging, skin problems, skinfinity', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"fillers treatment in Noida\",\"anti aging\",\"skin problems\",\"skinfinity\"]', 0, 1, '2022-02-18 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(444, 'anti-aging-remedies-to-try-out-at-home', 'Anti-Aging Remedies To Try Out At Home ', 'We completely empathize with you when you tell us that aging is your worst enemy. After all, who doesn’t want a youthful and younger-looking skin? However, if only you knew that you could overcome aging one step at a time through a few anti-aging remedies that you could try at home, wouldn’t you be all in for that?', '<p>We completely empathize with you when you tell us that aging is your worst enemy. After all, who doesn’t want a youthful and younger-looking skin? However, if only you knew that you could overcome aging one step at a time through a few <strong>anti-aging remedies</strong> that you could try at home, wouldn’t you be all in for that? So, let’s dive into this and find out how to reverse the signs of aging with a few simple tricks! </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>But Firstly, What Is Anti-Aging? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Anti-aging can be made possible when the process of regeneration is dominant over degeneration. While in degeneration, the existing skin cells replace themselves with weaker cells, in regeneration, the existing cells are replaced by stronger cells. This process of regeneration of skin cells is termed as anti-aging treatment. consult  <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>best dermatologist in Noida</strong></a>, if you are from gurgaon then consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol. today!</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What Are The Home Remedies? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li><strong>Honey:</strong> Honey exfoliates the skin to remove dead cells and promotes regeneration of new cells. It is an antioxidant rich compound which acts as a powerful anti-aging regimen. It also helps lighten the age spots, and vitamin B and potassium present in honey also helps in improving skin elasticity and suppleness.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Fenugreek:</strong> A rich source of vitamin B3 and niacin that helps in recovering the damaged skin cells and promotes the regeneration of new cells and tissues, fenugreek seeds help in lightening age spots, hyper pigmentation wrinkles, fine lines and crow’s feet that form on the forehead, and at the corner of eyes and lips.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Bananas:</strong> Bananas are a cheap, easily available, and natural anti-aging remedy. These are loaded with nutrients such as potassium, vitamin B, vitamin C and vitamin E that makes it a complete remedy for all skin problems.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Aloe Vera:</strong> Malic acid present in aloe vera gel improves skin elasticity and reduces wrinkles and fine lines- the most evident signs of skin aging. Zinc present in the gel increases the youthfulness of skin by shrinking the pores. </li>\r\n <li><strong>Olive Oil:</strong> The anti-aging properties of olive oil can be attributed to the polyphenols and oleic acid present in it. Powered with monounsaturated fats and Vitamins B and D, it prevents the appearance of new wrinkles and also tackles the existing ones.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Egg Whites:</strong> An egg white mask is an extremely effective way to lighten fine lines and wrinkles. By applying egg whites on the wrinkled area of the skin, the skin can be stretched and open pores can be shrinked to provide the skin a smoother, younger, and youthful appearance. </li>\r\n <li><strong>Lemon Juice:</strong> Being a rich source of citric acid, lemon juice helps in exfoliating the skin, removing dead skin cells and impurities and shrinking open pores to provide a smoother and younger appearance to the skin. It tightens the tissues and increases skin elasticity to reduce the appearance of wrinkles and fine lines.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Pineapples:</strong> Pineapple juice helps prevent premature aging. Being loaded with antioxidants such as potassium and vitamin C, pineapple juice helps in neutralizing the harmful effects of free radicals and oxidative stress of cells thus preventing premature aging of skin.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Almonds:</strong> Almonds are loaded with nutrients such as vitamin E, iron, zinc, folic acid and oleic acid that function as powerful antioxidants which prevent the degeneration of collagen fibers of skin and delay the aging process by treating wrinkles and fine lines.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Avocados:</strong> These help increase the suppleness and youthfulness by increasing the skin elasticity. It acts as a nourishing moisturizer for excessive dry skin that also helps in repairing damaged cells and promotes the regeneration of new cells. The antioxidants prevent premature aging. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Even though aging may cause wrinkles, fine lines and other unpleasant visual effects, methods like anti-aging remedies do exist that can be utilized to slow down the development of these problems and in some cases, even reduce the appearance of existing issues that have already developed.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For a detailed consultation, book an appointment at <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">Skinfinity</a> for more <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging\">Anti aging treatment in Noida</a>, anti-aging tips and tricks! </p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Popular Anti-Aging Treatments We Offer</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"http://www.skinfinityderma.com/botox-treatment-gurgaon/\"><strong>Botox Injections</strong></a> – Reduce dynamic wrinkles like crow’s feet and forehead lines.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/filler/\"><strong>Dermal Fillers</strong></a> – Restore lost volume in cheeks, lips, and under eyes.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/thread-lift/\"><strong>Thread Lift</strong></a> – Non-surgical facelift to lift and tighten sagging skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hifu/\"><strong>HIFU (High-Intensity Focused Ultrasound)</strong></a> – Stimulates collagen for firm, youthful skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/eyebrow-pigmentation/\"><strong>Microneedling with RF</strong></a> – Boost collagen, smooth wrinkles, and improve skin texture.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\"><strong>Chemical Peels</strong></a> – Improve tone, reduce fine lines, and enhance radiance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser/\"><strong>Laser Skin Resurfacing</strong></a> – Minimize wrinkles, pigmentation, and uneven skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/is-hydrafacial-worth-it/\">Hydrafacial </a>with <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\">Anti-Aging Boosters</a></strong> – Deep cleanse, exfoliate, and nourish aging skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/collagen-glow-photofacial/\"><strong>Collagen Induction Therapy</strong></a> – Stimulates collagen production for tighter skin.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong>Skin Tightening Treatments</strong> – Using advanced RF and ultrasound technology.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/eyebrow-pigmentation/\"><strong>Pigmentation & Age Spot Removal</strong></a> – Even out skin tone for a youthful glow.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Discover ideal skincare at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—book with our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> today:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/61492a323fb9a0db95f0463a70a2fce4.jpg', 'Anti aging treatment in noida', 'Anti-Aging Remedies To Try Out At Home | Anti Aging Treatment in Noida | Skinfinity', 'Even though aging may cause wrinkles, fine lines and other unpleasant visual effects. Read the anti aging remedies, tips and tricks or make an appointment to get anti aging treatment in Noida.', 'Anti aging treatment in noida, anti aging tips, anti aging remedies', NULL, 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Anti aging treatment in noida\",\"anti aging tips and tricks\",\"anti aging remedies\"]', 0, 1, '2022-02-14 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(445, 'know-about-prp-treatment-for-the-face', 'All You Need To Know About PRP Treatment For The Face', 'PRP, or Platelet Rich Plasma Treatment for the face, is popularly known as “Vampire Facial”. These have nowadays become increasingly famous due to the vast media attention that they have been receiving.', '<p>PRP, or Platelet Rich Plasma Treatment for the face, is popularly known as “Vampire Facial”. These have nowadays become increasingly famous due to the vast media attention that they have been receiving. PRP is a fast, effective, and natural way of combating the signs of aging as it uses your own blood product. We know you are intrigued, so continue reading to know all about the PRP treatment for the face! </p>\r\n\r\n<h1><strong>What Is PRP? </strong></h1>\r\n\r\n<p>PRP is a rejuvenation treatment for your skin, and is an alternative to a surgical facelift. The natural chemicals in your own PRP are injected onto your face and then micro-needled into the skin. Once the plasma is in, it begins to do its work of rejuvenating your entire face, tightening wrinkled areas, and smoothing the overall look. It’s able to do that because PRP’s essential chemical components stimulate collagen growth. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Choose the best for your skin and procure the services of the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\">best dermatologist in Noida</a> at Skinfinity. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>How Does The Treatment Work? </strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>A small sample of blood is taken and placed into the centrifuge. This spins the blood around, while separating the plasma and platelets from the red blood cells. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>In the next step, a topical cream is used to numb the treatment area. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>Then, hyaluronic acid is used to ensure your skin is free from pigmentation and fully hydrated before the plasma is spread across your face.</li>\r\n <li>After this, very small needles are used to ensure that the platelet rich plasma gets deep down into the skin. This process is known as microneedling and it stimulates collagen growth. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What Are The Benefits of PRP? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li><strong>Increased Collagen Production:</strong> Collagen production continues to decline as a person’s age increases. Thus, a PRP treatment is an excellent choice as it boosts the body’s natural collagen production, thereby reducing the appearance of fine lines, wrinkles, and other signs of aging of the skin. </li>\r\n <li><strong>Improved Skin Tone And Texture:</strong> Through PRP, your body produces new and healthier skin cells, thereby improving the overall appearance of the skin. It is a brilliant choice for those patients with surgical and acne scars, stretch marks, hyperpigmentation, scars from injury, and other forms of poor skin texture and tone. </li>\r\n <li><strong>Fewer Wrinkles And Facial Lines:</strong> Lines and wrinkles are slowly erased when the old skin cells are recycled and new skin cells with healthier elastin and collagen are formed. Different signs of aging caused by loose skin are eliminated once the skin starts tightening as a response to the micro incisions on the skin. The deeper folds in the skin also start to disappear and the hollow areas are plumped.</li>\r\n <li><strong>Fewer Risks And Side Effects:</strong> The procedure is minimally invasive and requires no surgery. Therefore, it is considered a low-risk treatment with no complications or side effects. </li>\r\n <li><strong>Painless Procedure:</strong> The patients may feel the device as it is applied to the skin, but there is no pain involved. </li>\r\n <li><strong>Long-Lasting Results:</strong> PRP facial rejuvenation provides high-quality results for up to a year. The results of vampire facial typically appear within a few weeks after the treatment.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>What To Expect After The Treatment? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Although there are no prolonged side effects, you can expect the following things to occur: </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>Minor swelling. </li>\r\n <li>Temporary bruises. </li>\r\n <li>Minor redness and itching. </li>\r\n <li>A sense of tingling. </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>These symptoms typically subside after a few days, but it’s better to consult the physician if the discomfort becomes unbearable.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><strong>Why Choose Skinfinity? </strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>At Skinfinity, we aim to provide our patients with the safest and most effective PRP treatment to enhance the appearance of their beautiful face. Our highly trained staff are experienced in performing PRP facial treatments that restore the skin’s firmness and youthful glow without using incisions or long downtimes. consult with <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>best dermatologist in Noida</strong></a>, if you are from gurgaon then consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol. today!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For the best <em>PRP face treatment in Noida</em>, <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/book-appointment\">book an appointment now</a>! </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skin issues? Visit <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—trusted <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> & <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> | <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/82cb9f34a8a9a7b7c8b528df1a4e2567.jpg', 'prp treatment', 'All You Need To Know About PRP Treatment For The Face | Skinfinity', 'PRP is a rejuvenation treatment for your skin, and is an alternative to a surgical facelift. Read this blog to know more about prp face treatment in Noida.', 'prp treatment, prp face treatment in noida, skinfinity', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/know-about-prp-treatment-for-the-face/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"prp treatment\",\"prp face treatment in noida\",\"skinfinity\"]', 0, 1, '2022-02-09 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(446, 'your-ultimate-guide-to-PRP-therapy', 'Your Ultimate Guide To PRP Therapy', 'Hair loss and hair fall affects both men and women and is one of the most common problems. While losing a few strands is natural, it gets concerning when you start noticing hair in large bunches all over your room', '<p>Hair loss and <strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-fall-treatment-gurgaon/\">hair fall treatment</a> </strong>affects both men and women and is one of the most common problems. While losing a few strands is natural, it gets concerning when you start noticing hair in large bunches all over your room. We know exactly what you feel about dealing with hair loss, and so we bring to you a once and for all solution. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What Is PRP? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>PRP, or Platelet Rich Plasma therapy involves the use of platelets and growth factors from your own blood to assist inactive hair follicles to move back into the growth phase. It has gained popularity for treating patterned hair loss, thinning of the hair, and receding hairline. Listed below are a few facts about PRP: </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Even though minimally invasive, PRP is mostly pain-free. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The treatment has next to no side effects. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The treatment is usually carried out in 6-8 sessions, each almost a month apart. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Prior to PRP, a blood test is mandatory. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The results are evident within 3-5 months. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The treatment can be opted for at any hair clinic. Skinfinity offers the best hair PRP treatment in Noida. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>How Is PRP Different From Hair Transplant? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Unlike hair transplant, PRP is non-surgical and does not involve the addition of follicles in the target area. PRP helps with the reactivation of dormant hair follicles and stimulates hair growth, unlike a transplant, which provides dramatic results. On account of being a non-surgical and minimally-invasive procedure, PRP does not work in cases of late stage of baldness or complete baldness. It works best on early stages of hair thinning in both men and women and is ideal for hair regrowth for people who have not reached a stage where they necessarily need a hair transplant. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Are There Any Side Effects? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The risks involved with PRP are minimal. However, any therapy which involves injections carries a risk of side effects. A few of them are:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Swelling. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Scalp tenderness. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Injury to blood vessels and nerves. ‘</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Headaches and itching. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Mild pain in the injected area. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Temporary bleeding at the injected site. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>When carried out under expert supervision, PRP has no risks. Therefore, choose your clinic wisely. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How Much Does It Cost? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>The average cost across India ranges from INR 5,000-15,000 per session. The price of the treatment depends upon: </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Experience of the dermatologist. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The reputation of the clinic. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Your own location, as prices are higher, but the treatment is more effective, in metropolitan cities. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Quality of the equipment used for the procedure. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Number of sessions required, based on the severity of your case. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The addition of nutritive components. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Is PRP Effective? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Patients who opted for PRP therapy have reported an increase in their hair volume. Global studies have indicated that PRP is the most effective non-surgical and minimally-invasive method to treat hair loss and thinning of the hair. As it boosts natural regrowth, it ultimately improves the overall scalp coverage. Most patients notice a reduction in hair loss after the initial sessions itself. Visible hair growth becomes evident generally after the third session itself. Considering the simplicity, safety and cost effectiveness of the treatment, dermatologists consider PRP the most feasible option to deal with hair loss in their patients. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>Where To Obtain The Treatment? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity provides optimum and ideal solutions for all cosmetic problems of the hair. With its unique and individualized approach, it caters to the needs of all patients with their expertise, experience and US FDA approved technology. Through an accurate diagnosis, Skinfinity aims to treat the root cause of all problems pertaining to the hair, thereby preventing recurrence. </p>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nFor more details on PRP therapy, contact Skinfinity and seek advice from the<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"> <strong>best dermatologist in Noida</strong></a>, if you are from gurgaon then consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol. today!</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Location :</strong> <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/c7b6b2dedc2a788d46d136c7dec8e228.jpg', 'Your Ultimate Guide To PRP Therapy', 'Your Ultimate Guide To PRP Therapy', 'Hair loss and hair fall affects both men and women and is one of the most common problems. While losing a few strands is natural, it gets concerning when you start noticing hair in large bunches all over your room', 'Your Ultimate Guide To PRP Therapy', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/your-ultimate-guide-to-PRP-therapy/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Your Ultimate Guide To PRP Therapy\"]', 0, 1, '2022-01-22 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(447, 'skincare-tips-for-dry-skin-in-winters', 'Skincare tips for dry skin in winters', 'Winters have their own charm. The cold weather, the warmth of the fireplace, snuggling blankets are just sheer bliss. As the temperature goes down, the sun becomes your best friend. The chilly winds, however, are not so skin-friendly.', '<p>Winters have their own charm. The cold weather, the warmth of the fireplace, snuggling blankets are just sheer bliss. As the temperature goes down, the sun becomes your best friend. The chilly winds, however, are not so skin-friendly. They dry out excess moisture causing itchiness.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Winters are a bit harsh on skin and hair. If you stay outdoors, chilly winds dry up your skin, and if you stay indoors near a fireplace or heaters, the excess heat dries up the moisture. No matter what you do, you are left with dry and itchy skin, which gradually becomes flaky.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p>There are numerous ways to combat these skin woes and keep your skin supple and fresh. Follow these tips to level up your skincare game:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Find out what is making things worse</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Find out what is spiking the itchiness in your skin, is it the hot shower, gel-based cleanser, staying outdoors for more extended periods or scrubbing off the dead skin? Based on your findings, start taking the right care of your skin. Let your skin acclimatise with your surroundings. Do not rush into scrubbing off as it rids your skin of its natural protective oils. Do not take hot showers as they tend to strip off excess moisture. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>2.  Layer your products properly</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Just like we layer up our clothes in winters, our skin needs layering too. Hot oil massages are an excellent choice for skin and hair. If you have extra dry skin you can pick the body butter and heavy moisturisers for the winter season. If you have oily skin you need to choose the right products to lock the moisture. Avoid alcohol-based cleansers and always carry a toner or hydrating mist. The lips and under-eye area require more attention. Lip balms heal dry and chapped lips and keep them soft and moisturised.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3.  Invest in a good humidifier</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Humidifiers are your best friends in all seasons, but especially in winters, as they help make the air less dry. Humidifiers are recommended with air-conditioners and heaters as well, especially since heaters remove the moisture in the air and lead to dry skin</p>\r\n\r\n<p>4.  Don’t forget your sunscreen.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Taking luxurious sunbaths during wintertime is hard to resist, as they provide respite from the biting cold. But we all have the tendency to forget the most essential thing, which is sunscreen! Sunscreen is not just for summers. Without protecting our skin from harmful UV rays, we risk hyperpigmentation, worsening our acne scars and so much more. Make sunscreen an essential part of your routine whenever you might have to go outdoors.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>5.      Eating right</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It’s hard to avoid a comforting mug of hot chocolate every now and then in winters or to fill up on carbs in some other way, but excessive intake of sugary foods can disrupt your insulin levels and have a detrimental effect on your skin.  Try to incorporate vegetables in a day. Broccoli, carrot, radish, cucumber are high in fibre and nutrients. Toss them in a salad bowl, sprinkle some salt and pepper, and your portion of goodness is sorted. Bon Appetit!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>6.  Comfortable clothing</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Winter requires lots of layers but you need to layer properly to avoid dry and itchy skin. try to wear cotton clothing on your bare skin as knitted wool can cause itchiness and irritation on the skin. Layering also helps the skin cells breathe and prevents skin from breaking.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If the dryness is beyond your control and the skin appears cracked, don’t hesitate to seek medical attention. A dermatologist can help you with suitable ointments to fix your concern. Dry and flaky skin is more prone to fungal and bacterial infections. Get the right suggestions for your skin type and needs at Skinfinity! We have the best skin specialists in Noida, who will help you in your quest for supple, nourished skin and brave the harsh winters. consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Related Skin Treatments We Offer</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Discover our expert treatments designed to target specific skin concerns and enhance your natural beauty:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dark-circle-treatment/\">Dark Circles Treatment</a> – Reduce under-eye pigmentation, puffiness, and tired appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\">Acne Scar Treatment</a> – Fade scars, smooth skin texture, and boost confidence.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\">Chemical Peel</a> – Exfoliate, brighten, and rejuvenate your skin naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser/\">Laser Skin Resurfacing</a> – Improve tone, texture, and reduce fine lines.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\">Anti-Aging Treatment</a> – Minimize wrinkles and restore youthful elasticity.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-lightening-and-pigmentation/\">Pigmentation Treatment</a> – Even skin tone and fade dark spots.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/botox-treatment-gurgaon/\">Botox Treatment</a> – Smooth dynamic wrinkles for a fresher look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/freckles-and-lentigens/\">Freckles Treatment </a>– Fade freckles effectively with advanced treatments like lasers and peels, tailored to your skin for a clearer, even tone.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/book-appointment/\">Book your consultation</a> today and find the right treatment for your skin.</em></p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n\r\n<p>Searching for expert care? Find the best <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> & <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong> at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/d42e2d31cfc7a494277b067863c9b98e.jpg', 'Skincare tips for dry skin in winters', 'Skincare tips for dry skin in winters', 'Winters have their own charm. The cold weather, the warmth of the fireplace, snuggling blankets are just sheer bliss. As the temperature goes down, the sun becomes your best friend. The chilly winds, however, are not so skin-friendly.', 'Skincare tips for dry skin in winters', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skincare-tips-for-dry-skin-in-winters/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Skincare tips for dry skin in winters\"]', 0, 1, '2022-01-15 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(448, 'why-laser-hair-removal-is-best', 'Why Laser Hair Removal Beats Every Other Method', 'Discover why laser hair removal is safer, smoother, and more lasting than waxing or shaving. Try it at Skinfinity Derma today!', '<p>Unwanted hair on the body has become a huge problem as it not only appears unattractive, but also destroys self-esteem and self-confidence, thereby affecting one’s social relationships as well. Nowadays, grooming of body hair has become an essential part of our lives. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>While there are several convenient methods for hair removal, such as waxing and shaving, these are all temporary methods, extremely time-consuming, and come with the added disadvantage of fast regrowth, and may cause pain, especially to those who have sensitive skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Thanks to the advancement of cosmetology, laser hair removal has made life so much easier for those with excessive or unwanted body hair. Continue reading to learn all there is about laser hair removal. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What Is Laser Hair Removal? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>This process uses intense pulses of light, targeting a particular area, thereby destroying hair follicles, leaving you hair-free for a longer period of time. The laser causes the hair shaft and the hair follicle to heat up, thereby interrupting the hair growth cycle, putting an end to regrowth. The light is specifically absorbed by the pigment in the hair and doesn’t make contact with the surrounding skin or other types of tissue in the treatment area. </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How Is It Beneficial? </h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Laser hair removal is a minimally-invasive method, and therefore less painful than other methods. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>This technique works best for target areas. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Laser hair removal destroys hair at the root, proving itself as the best method for people with ingrown hairs. ‘</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>This process is mostly permanent, and may require touch-ups every few years, making it very cost-efficient. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The process takes place in multiple sessions but these take a few minutes, establishing itself as a quick method. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Why Is Laser Hair Removal The Best Option? </h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Waxing: Although waxing leaves the skin smooth for around a month, it is ultimately a temporary solution. You may need a waxing session once a month, but laser hair removal requires less sessions than waxing. Laser hair removal is a better alternative because it reduces the speed of hair regrowth, therefore lasting longer. Waxing involves pain, but laser hair removal is a pain-free method. Redness and rashes are common side effects of waxing, but laser hair removal has no side effects. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Shaving: Being the most convenient and simple method, shaving fails when it comes to long-lasting results. This is because a razor removes hair only from the surface, while laser destroys the follicles, putting an end to regrowth. Laser hair removal is a one-time investment and may require a retouch every now and then, but you would have to shave every alternate day if you wish to maintain the smooth texture of your skin through shaving. Shaving has side effects, such as ingrown hairs, cuts and burns, but laser hair removal has no such effects. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Electrolysis: Even though it is a permanent hair removal procedure, it has a lot of cons. It is an extremely lengthy process and requires a lot of accuracy. Unlike laser hair removal, electrolysis is neither comfortable nor painless as it requires the use of needles, which give a stinging feeling. While lasers have no side effects, electrolysis may lead to scarring, redness, skin discoloration, and permanent skin damage. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Depilatory Creams: The chemicals in these creams have an increased pH and are harmful to the skin. These may lead to skin irritation, chemical burns and may have an allergic reaction. Unlike laser hair removal, this is a temporary solution as it does not destroy hair at the root. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Where To Seek Treatment? </h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity is your one-stop solution for all problems of the skin which also hamper your self-esteem and confidence. Through its unique and individualized approach, it looks after the requirements of all its patients, thereby providing them with optimum solutions. The technology used is US-FDA approved and all treatments are personalized to suit the individual requirements of the clients. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity uses a triple wavelength technology for <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-reduction/\">l</a><strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-reduction/\">aser hair removal</a>.</strong> The triple wavelength diode laser is the most advanced hair removal technology. The triple wavelength is 755nm, 808nm and 1064nm. 3 wavelength diode laser hair removal machines give the best results for all hair and skin types. Skinfinity also offers: </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Diode laser hair removal: This offers a longer wavelength, designated to penetrate the skin deeper. It is very effective for people with a darker complexion. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Alexandrite lasers: These emit high-energy light through the alexandrite crystals, making it very effective for epilation. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Long pulse laser: This is the most commonly used device. As LPL is less absorbed by melanin in the epidermis, it is more effective for hair removal in the darker skin types. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Considering Full Body Laser Hair Removal?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re tired of managing unwanted hair across multiple areas—legs, arms, underarms, back, chest, bikini line—then<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/full-body-laser-hair-removal/\"> <strong>full body laser hair removal</strong></a> is the most efficient and cost-effective option.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Not only does it eliminate the hassle of multiple sessions across different parts of the body, but it also offers better <strong>value per session</strong>, improved <strong>skin texture</strong>, and <strong>long-term results</strong> with minimal maintenance.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wondering how much it costs?</strong><br>\r\nWe’ve created a detailed breakdown just for you.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Read: <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/full-body-laser-hair-removal/\">Full Body Laser Hair Removal Cost in Delhi</a> (Noida)</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>For a detailed consultation, book an appointment with Skinfinity for the <strong>best laser hair removal in Noida or if you are from Gurgaon then </strong>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol., today!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Book your appointment with <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, home to a trusted <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon link</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida link</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/cb4493f4034783f56da8996513e6aecc.jpg', 'Laser Hair Removal Is The Best Hair Removal Technique! Here’s Why', 'Laser Hair Removal Is The Best Hair Removal Technique! Here’s Why', 'Unwanted hair on the body has become a huge problem as it not only appears unattractive, but also destroys self-esteem and self-confidence, thereby affecting one’s social relationships as well. Nowadays, grooming of body hair has become an essential ', 'Laser Hair Removal Is The Best Hair Removal Technique! Here’s Why', 'https://skinfinityderma.com/laser-hair-removal-is-the-best-hair-removal-technique-here-why/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Laser Hair Removal Is The Best Hair Removal Technique! Here’s Why\"]', 0, 1, '2022-10-07 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(449, 'is-your-food-responsible-for-your-acne', 'Is your food responsible for your acne?', 'Acne is a multi-faceted entity caused by numerous contributing factors like clogged pores, growth of bacteria, excess secretion of oil and sebum, hormonal changes occurring during pubertal development.', '<p>Acne is a multi-faceted entity caused by numerous contributing factors like clogged pores, growth of bacteria, excess secretion of oil and sebum, hormonal changes occurring during pubertal development. All of us have experienced these undesired break-outs at some point in time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Diet plays a pivotal role in causing breakouts or worsening acne. Yes, diet matters. Certain food products and beverages like white bread, soda, processed items like cheese, chicken sausages, salami are known to promote breakouts. On a lighter note, think about avoiding acne just by avoiding some foodstuff.</p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How does sugar harm your skin?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Excess sugar spikes the level of insulin in the blood. A chemical reaction is initiated with binds excess sugar to collagen and elastin. This bonded form of elastin and collagen is weak and breaks down, causing sagging and wrinkling of the skin. Consumption of high sugar foods boosts the production of sebum and causes acne.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Studies have shown a correlation of the following kind of foodstuffs, which tend to increase the incidence of acne.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Beverages: Soft beverages are loaded with high sugar content. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Fast-food: As tempting as it may be, they are loaded with refined carbs and sugar</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Omega 3 and 6: When it comes to acne, fish oils, walnuts, and omega-6 rich food-stuff are a big NO!</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Chocolates: Chocolates are full of sugar and you might have to avoid chocolates for a while.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Whey Protein: Whey protein helps to get an extra muscular appearance but you might have noticed the increased appearance of acne as well. This occurs because whey increases the levels of insulin in our bodies.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Alcohol: Alcohol tends to dehydrate your body, making your skin prone to breakouts. Dehydrated body cells tend to retain water and store toxins along with it,</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>What is the ideal diet plan for Acne?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>A healthy, glowing complexion comes from within. Feeding ourselves a healthy diet is the best thing we can do. It is essential to understand the nature of food items and should be consumed in moderation. The following food items help to combat the inflammation that <strong>causes acne:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Fruits and Vegetables- Green leafy vegetables are natural sources of fibre that aids in digestion. Fruits rich in Vitamin C like orange, papaya helps to reduce inflammation and detoxify the harmful toxins inside our bodies.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Water- water helps to flush out toxins and neutralizes the detrimental effect of all the food items that shouldn’t be consumed in the first place. Make sure to drink at least 5-6 glasses per day.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Probiotics- They aids in digestion by promoting healthy bacteria. How does that help acne</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Anti-oxidants: Green tea, flax seeds are rich in antioxidants which help to reduce the severity of acne.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h3>How to treat acne?</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Small changes in diet can keep all acne at bay. The<a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong> treatment of acne</strong></a> is based on the severity. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Mild acne can be managed by topical ointments and lotions containing salicylic acid and benzoyl peroxide. Lacto Calamine is a holy grail solution for reducing itchiness around acne helps them to dry out.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For moderate to severe acne, Skinfinity offers excellent options for <strong>Acne Treatment in Noida</strong>. 6-8 months of combination treatment which includes oral and topical medications, laser-based facials, skin resurfacing therapies have helped to reduce the appearance of the scar and give visible smooth skin.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Advanced skincare solutions by <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—visit our <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong>:<br>\r\n <a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/19f8a104db500c8790e895e8229398c8.jpg', 'Is your food responsible for your acne', 'Is your food responsible for your acne?', 'Acne is a multi-faceted entity caused by numerous contributing factors like clogged pores, growth of bacteria, excess secretion of oil and sebum, hormonal changes occurring during pubertal development.', 'Is your food responsible for your acne', 'https://skinfinityderma.com/is-your-food-responsible-for-your-acne/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Is your food responsible for your acne\"]', 0, 1, '2022-01-05 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(450, 'is-stress-causing-your-hair-to-fall-out', 'Is stress causing your hair to fall out?', 'Since the pandemic, we’ve all become used to feeling anxious. It’s a perfectly normal reaction to mental and physical stressors in our lives. But too much of it, and you have a case of chronic stress on your hands, which can be a lot to handle.', '<p>Since the pandemic, we’ve all become used to feeling anxious. It’s a perfectly normal reaction to the mental and physical stressors in our lives. But when it becomes excessive, it can turn into chronic stress — something far more challenging to manage. It can show up as irritability, insomnia, headaches, and even unexpected physical issues. One of the most common concerns people face today is increased hair fall. In fact, many individuals now seek <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-fall-treatment-gurgaon/\"><strong>hair fall treatment in Gurgaon</strong></a> as stress-induced hair loss becomes more prevalent.Hair growth occurs in three stages:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anagen: Called as the growth phase. In this phase, new hair develops out of the follicles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Catagen: Called as degeneration phase: In this phase, hair does not grow as it detaches itself from the blood supply inside the follicles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Telogen: Also called as resting phase. In this phase, hair is devoid of nutrition and tends to fall out.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How are stress and hair loss even related?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>“Telogen effluvium” is a form of stress-induced hair loss. This is absolutely reversible, and the condition improves by working on your nutrition and lifestyle.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Under chronic stress, the body releases several inflammatory agents that reduce the size of hair follicles. But wait, it doesn’t end there. It shrinks out the diameter of blood vessels as well. As a result, the hair strand is unable to get the required amount of nutrition and ultimately causes it to fall out.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Losing a sizable amount of strands everyday can increase stress and further aggravate the condition. Bald patches start to appear on the scalp. Before shedding, you may also experience thinning of hair strands. Thinning of hair can be an alarming signal for you to start looking out for yourself. The effect of stress on hair occurs in the initial stages. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How can it be prevented? </h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Fortunately, hair loss caused by stress gets recovered in a span of 4-7 months. If you are affected by stress-induced hair loss, here are a few steps that you can take:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Value yourself a bit more and try to avoid negative feelings. At first, avoiding negative thoughts can be difficult. Make time for your hobbies that makes you happy.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Diet plays a key role in regulating hair growth. Folic acid, iron, vitamin D, vitamin B12, and Biotin are the most important micronutrients that stimulate hair growth. Any minor deficiency in any of these could cause hair fall treatment .</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Stress can also be managed by guided meditation and yoga. Light exercise helps to improve blood flow and builds up resiliency.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Early intervention is essential as this is a reversible condition. As the hair follicles are still in a restored state, consulting a dermatologist can be your best move.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>How can it be treated?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Oral supplements along with non-surgical procedures have shown excellent results. Few therapies are mentioned below:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Laser Comb: A comb-like device that emits high-frequency infrared radiation to the follicles and improves blood circulation. It is a painless procedure with zero downtime.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Growth factor therapy: Highly beneficial and proves lasting results. Your own plasma is taken and enriched with growth factors which are later injected onto the roots superficially. Regular sittings provide strength to the follicles, <strong>reduce hair fall</strong> and improve the overall texture of the hair. If the therapy is taken at the early stages of hair loss, it can delay patterned baldness in males and females and eliminate the requirement of hair transplant.  </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fibroblast-rich serum therapy: Fibroblasts are growth factors that are injected into the roots along with the patient’s own plasma. This therapy aims to improve the density and texture while promoting new hair growth.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Stress can be one of the reasons for hair loss but it is not the only reason. The sooner you address the problem, the more likely you will be able to stop it. Skinfinity is an excellent and appropriate choice for the best hair loss treatment in Noida. Our experts can help find the root cause and prevent you from losing your luscious locks.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Trust your skin to <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, offering top <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong></a> services: </p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon link</a> | <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida link</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/6e2bf3ec3d1bc4aaca0dae006847a205.jpg', 'Is stress causing your hair to fall out', 'Is stress causing your hair to fall out?', 'Since the pandemic, we’ve all become used to feeling anxious. It’s a perfectly normal reaction to mental and physical stressors in our lives. But too much of it, and you have a case of chronic stress on your hands, which can be a lot to handle.', 'Hair loss treatment in noida, chronic stress, telogen effluvium, hair thinning', 'https://skinfinityderma.com/is-stress-causing-your-hair-to-fall-out/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Is stress causing your hair to fall out\"]', 0, 1, '2021-12-26 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(451, 'how-to-overcome-teenage-acne', 'How to Overcome Teenage Acne?', 'Acne occurs in most teens. The perception of acne in teenagers is beyond a skin problem. It has an undeniable emotional and psychological effect. A child’s teenage and adolescence are days of wonder, ', '<p>Acne occurs in most teens. The perception of acne in teenagers is beyond a skin problem. It has an undeniable emotional and psychological effect. A child’s teenage and adolescence are days of wonder, where they go through most of their major development and evolve emotionally, socially and psychologically<strong> <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\">Acne scar treatment</a></strong> , however, can greatly impact their self-esteem and confidence levels.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Let’s start with understanding the root cause</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Pimples can occur due to any of the following reasons:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Clogged pores by sebum or oil production.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Improper use of cosmetic products</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Touching your  face repeatedly with unclean hands</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hormonal imbalances that lead to excess sebum or oil production.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hair follicles get infected by bacteria or clogged due to excess sebum.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Can acne  be prevented?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Since acne is often caused due to hormonal changes in the body, it can’t always be avoided. But there are specific measures that help to reduce their severity:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Wash your face twice daily with a gentle cleanser. Overwashing your face can stimulate the cells to produce more sebum, which makes your skin oilier and tempts you to wash it again, creating a vicious cycle..</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Use products advised by a professional expert, as they would better understand your skin type and specific needs and recommend products that deliver better results than commercial alternatives.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Use fewer cosmetic products and always clean your applicators and brushes before and after use. Never go to bed with makeup on. As teenagers are more tech-friendly, always remember to wipe the screens of mobile phones with a suitable cleansing agent.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>No popping or squeezing the acne regardless of its size and shape. Squeezing can push the infected content into deeper tissue resulting in even bigger pimples.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Aloe vera provides a soothing effect, but it has a high amount of latex that can cause allergic reactions, so avoid it in its raw form and instead try products enriched with aloe vera.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Low sugar and a low carb diet help to improve the status of acne. Increased water intake can flush toxins out of the body. Green leafy vegetables help to replenish the micronutrients like zinc and selenium. High fiber diets and probiotics improve digestion and overall metabolism.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Do I need to see a doctor?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>A dermatologist can evaluate the condition of acne and can advise treatment accordingly. Over-the-counter medication helps to reduce the severity of acne and reduce scarring and pigmentation you can take <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong>Acne treatment</strong></a> also.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Commonly used medications for the same include:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Salicylic acid</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Benzoyl peroxide</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Glycolic acid</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Lactic acid</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Retinoids</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Cystic acne requires low-dose oral antibiotic therapy.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>However, use these only after prior approval from a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>skin specialist in gurgaon </strong></a>, as some of these can be harsh on your skin as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acne increases the overall sensitivity of your skin. As with all things, you have to give treatment some time before you see concrete results, and even a reasonably low dose and topical treatments can take 6-8 weeks before providing any visible results. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>Apart from just acne treatments, a healthy diet and regular workouts can help improve your metabolism and reduce the severity of your acne too.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br>\r\nAcne primarily appears on the face. Other areas of occurrence are neck, arms, shoulders, chest and back. Acne can rapidly spread due to touching or excessive rubbing of clothing.  Skinfinity offers the best pimple and acne treatments in Noida. Our treatment aims to prevent new breakouts reduce acne scarring.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2><strong>Other Skin Treatments You May Be Interested In</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Enhance your skin health and beauty with our wide range of advanced solutions:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dark-circle-treatment/\"><strong>Dark Circles Treatment</strong></a> – Brighten and refresh your under-eye area by reducing pigmentation and puffiness.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/acne-pimple-treatment-noida/\"><strong>Acne Scar Treatment</strong></a>– Smoothen uneven skin and fade stubborn scars for a flawless look.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/chemical-peel/\"><strong>Chemical Peel</strong></a> – Remove dead skin cells, boost radiance, and rejuvenate naturally.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/laser/\"><strong>Laser Skin Resurfacing</strong></a> – Target fine lines, improve skin texture, and achieve a youthful glow.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\"><strong>Anti-Aging Treatment</strong></a> – Restore firmness, reduce wrinkles, and slow visible signs of aging.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/skin-lightening-and-pigmentation/\"><strong>Pigmentation Treatment</strong></a>– Lighten dark spots and achieve an even, radiant complexion.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/botox-treatment-gurgaon/\"><strong>Botox Treatment</strong></a> – Relax facial lines for a smoother, younger appearance.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p><strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/freckles-and-lentigens/\">Freckles Treatment</a></strong>– Effectively lighten freckles and even skin tone using safe, modern techniques.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/book-appointment/\">Book your consultation</a> today and let us create a personalized skin treatment plan for you!</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Healthy, glowing skin begins at <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—expert <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong></a>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon link</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida link</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/b7654f658830bca852bad550f7f067ab.jpg', 'How to Overcome Teenage Acne', 'How to Overcome Teenage Acne?', 'Acne occurs in most teens. The perception of acne in teenagers is beyond a skin problem. It has an undeniable emotional and psychological effect. A child’s teenage and adolescence are days of wonder, ', 'pimple treatment in Noida, Acne, Pimples', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/how-to-overcome-teenage-acne/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"How to Overcome Teenage Acne\"]', 0, 1, '2021-12-17 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(452, 'eyebrow-microblading', 'Eyebrow Microblading - Procedure, Costs And Benefits ', 'You may not acknowledge this often or may sometimes remain indifferent to this, but eyebrows form an important aesthetic feature of your face. Your eyebrows reflect your age, and eyebrow restoration is now a part of anti-ageing procedures as well.', '<p>You may not acknowledge this often or may sometimes remain indifferent to this, but eyebrows form an important aesthetic feature of your face. Your eyebrows reflect your age, and eyebrow restoration is now a part of<strong> <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\">anti-ageing</a></strong><a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/anti-aging/\"> <strong>Treatment </strong></a>procedures as well. Here, the recent trend of microblading pops up into the picture. If you have come across this name, but aren’t fully aware of the procedure, look no further, for you are at the right place!</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What Is Microblading?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Microblading is a new technique in the field of permanent cosmetics for the restoration of your eyebrows. An esthetician uses microblades to apply color pigments that look like real hair. This allows you to walk with perfect eyebrows all day, every day without worrying about makeup. The procedure is non-invasive and applies semi-permanent eyebrows to your existing eyebrows. The coloring from microblading may last you up until 3 years as it uses a smaller quantity of pigment. Thus, touch-ups will be required to maintain your desired look. </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microblading is a semi-permanent cosmetic procedure as the pigment will fade over time. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>The pain and ultimate outcome entirely depends on your artist, so choose your artist wisely. Skinfinity offers the best microblading in Noida. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microblading takes place in two sessions. The first is the entire procedure and the second is the touch-up session which is not optional, as it locks in the results and makes them last longer. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microblading does not aim for perfect symmetry of your eyebrows. The results largely depend on the bone structure of your face.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What To Expect After The Procedure? </h2>\r\n\r\n<p>At least a week after the procedure, your eyebrows will appear darker. Due to scabbing and healing, they may also feel sharper. If you experience some redness and mild swelling, it is natural. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>A few instructions that will be issued by your esthetician are: </p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Gently wash over your eyebrows using your fingertip for about 10 seconds, rinse, and wipe dry. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Use a minimal amount of moisturizing ointment. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Avoid long showers and keep your eyebrows away from water for about a week to 10 days. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Keep the eyebrow area as clean as possible. This includes avoiding makeup. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Do not pick at the scabs. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Avoid direct sunlight for about a month.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Avoid using face scrubs or peels for a month. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Beware of sleeping on your face for at least 10 days after the procedure.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What Are The Benefits Of Microblading? </h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microblading allows immediate results. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>It is a convenient procedure. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microblading enhances the overall appearance of the face as eyebrows form an important facial aesthetic. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>It is a painful procedure as it is non-invasive. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>It is a low maintenance procedure and demands a touch-up very infrequently. </p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>How Much Does Microblading Cost? </h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Microblading is not cheap, and if you are planning to get it done, you should probably start budgeting yourself. In India, the <em><strong>cost may range from INR 25,000 to INR 50,000</strong></em> depending upon the location, experience, demand, and popularity of the esthetician. While everyone loves a good deal, low prices may seem dubious and may cost you your entire appearance in the longer run. Therefore, it is always advisable to do your research before making any definite decisions. </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Who To Consider For The Treatment?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity offers the best microblading in Noida with affordable prices and experienced estheticians. It prioritizes the patient’s needs and concerns and provides optimum solutions to all their skincare needs with the use of expert knowledge, accurate diagnosis, updated methods and tactics, and US FDA approved technology. With its unique and individualized approach, Skinfinity provides comprehensive solutions to all contemporary problems of the skin. <br>\r\nFor a detailed consultation on all your microblading queries, contact Skinfinity, the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>best skin specialist in Noida</strong></a>, or if you are from gurgaon then consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol. today!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For personalized skincare, consult with <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>—your trusted <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> or <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong></a>:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon branch</a> |  <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida branch</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Disclaimer:<br>\r\nThe content shared in this blog is for educational and awareness purposes only. It should not be considered a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always consult a qualified dermatologist or healthcare provider for personalised guidance regarding your skin concerns.</p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/fb7382168bdb42fa79c744f93f0eb3fe.jpg', 'Eyebrow Microblading - Procedure', 'Eyebrow Microblading - Procedure, Costs And Benefits ', 'You may not acknowledge this often or may sometimes remain indifferent to this, but eyebrows form an important aesthetic feature of your face. Your eyebrows reflect your age, and eyebrow restoration is now a part of anti-ageing procedures as well.', 'Eyebrow Microblading - Procedure, Costs And Benefits ', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/eyebrow-microblading/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Eyebrow Microblading - Procedure\",\"Costs And Benefits\"]', 0, 1, '2021-12-10 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24'),
(453, 'does-hair-loss-increase-in-winters', 'Does hair loss increase in winters?', 'Hair loss is undoubtedly the most common problem faced by most of us. Before we even realize it, a massive volume is already gone. Before long, you’ll find strands on your pillow, your clothes and clogging your drain.', '<p>Hair loss is undoubtedly the most common problem faced by most of us. Before we even realize it, a massive volume is already gone. Before long, you’ll find strands on your pillow, your clothes and clogging your drain. Hair loss can occur due to hormonal imbalance, nutritional deficiency, or aging. Decreased temperature, however, has a striking link with hair fall. Hair loss due to seasonal variation is very much a real thing. In India, it commonly occurs at the end of September and reaches its peak in January. This type of hair fall is gender-neutral. It can affect both males and females. The wide variation is seen in the hair loss pattern among men and women.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>But why specifically winters?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Cold weather tends to dry the scalp and hair strands. As a result, they lose all the moisture and become brittle. If you have long hair, then you might face hair breakage as well. ‘Hair breakage ‘ is a common term used when hair breaks from its shaft, not roots.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Dry weather removes the moisture from the outermost layer of the hair and weakens out the bond strength. Now, when this dry hair undergoes any chemical or hormonal changes, they tend to fall.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>The other reason for hair loss in winters are:</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Over-styling: Certain hairstyles exert terrible pressure on hair follicles that leads to shedding of hair. This type of hair loss is called ‘Traction Alopecia’.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Air-Pollution: The particulate matter in the air builds up on the scalp. This build-up is sticky in nature and attracts micro-organisms and dust. It also leads to dandruff and itchiness.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Washing with excessively hot water: Using hot water is not a great idea to wash your hair in winters. It removes the natural oils and moisture from the hair.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Stress: Stress is not good in any season. It decreases the blood supply and hair follicles do not receive enough nutrition which causes hair loss.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Diet: Poor nutrition is directly linked to hair fall. Increased intake of coffee and tea decreases the absorption of iron and it is apparently the leading cause of hair fall in winters.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Hormonal Imbalances: The reduced time of day-light and colder temperatures causes hormonal changes in the body.  Changes can also be seen in metabolism, diet, and pattern of sleep. Vitamin D helps to develop the new hair follicles. Reduced levels of vitamin D in winters lead to the shedding of hair strands.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How can it be prevented?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Eating Right</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Diet is the most important factor for hair loss problems. As winter makes us crave more carbohydrates, it is necessary to stick to a balanced diet plan. A protein-rich diet helps to restore the texture of hair. similarly, Green leafy vegetables help to replenish the levels of iron and calcium in our bodies and nourish our hair. Limit caffeine intake. Keep a check on your water intake. Sometimes, lack of moisture is due to internal dehydration.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Exercise Everyday</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Light to moderate exercise improves blood circulation and maintains the equilibrium between hormonal and metabolic changes inside the body. This automatically helps increase nutrition to hair follicles and makes hair healthier. Yoga is an excellent choice to enhance flexibility and meditation keeps the stress away.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Proper hair management</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Wash your hair gently with a mild shampoo. Avoid tight buns or ponytails. Conditioning of shaft and roots is important to restore moisture. Air drying should be chosen over blow-drying. All the chemical treatments like keratin, coloring or styling should be avoided as they can aggravate hair loss.</p>\r\n\r\n<p> </p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What are the available treatment options?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Skinfinity has the <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/hair-fall-treatment/\">best hair-fall treatment in Noida</a>. There are various therapies available that are customized as per the individual’s concern.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Mesotherapy: Goodness of vitamins, hair peptides, and growth factors in one single vial which is delivered to your scalp by a meso-gun. It is a non-invasive treatment procedure that promotes regrowth.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>Microneedling: It is done with the help of derma rollers and it aims to improve the blood circulation in the scalp and promotes the growth of collagen fibers which enhance hair growth.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n <li>\r\n <p>A Cell therapy: A-cells with PRP helps to initiate the growth of new follicles and promotes hair growth. It is the most efficient technology to control hair loss.</p>\r\n </li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Air Pollution, smog, over-exposure by sun can cause serious damage to hair. If you are dealing with hair loss, then you need to act fast. Our experts will guide you with the required treatment, good diet and good products that can help you fight hair fall.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>consult a <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/dermatologist-in-gurgaon/\"><strong>dermatologist in gurgaon</strong> </a>and get complete treatment following proper protocol.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>At <strong>Skinfinity Derma Clinic</strong>, our leading <strong>dermatologist in Gurgaon</strong> and <a href=\"https://www.skinfinityderma.com/\"><strong>dermatologist in Noida</strong></a> are ready for your consultation:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://share.google/QWnBOKzMe7Ay6jqFh\" target=\"_new\">Gurgaon link</a> | <a href=\"https://share.google/QDMZRhFL4Bh0etsEe\" target=\"_new\">Noida link</a></p>\r\n', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/assets/blog/ae2f7f53ffac2fd9709bfdbc4c8fa49f.jpg', 'Does hair loss increase in winters', 'Does hair loss increase in winters?', 'Hair loss is undoubtedly the most common problem faced by most of us. Before we even realize it, a massive volume is already gone. Before long, you’ll find strands on your pillow, your clothes and clogging your drain.', 'Does hair loss increase in winters', 'https://www.skinfinityderma.com/does-hair-loss-increase-in-winters/', 'Dr. Ipshita Johri', NULL, '[\"Does hair loss increase in winters\"]', 0, 1, '2021-11-28 04:30:00', '2026-11-01 16:56:51', '2026-11-01 18:18:24');
